of Professional Writing City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Job Summary The English Department at Purdue University welcomes applications for a Clinical Assistant Professor of Professional Writing. A full-time academic year (August to May) position, this position is based in West Lafayette with a start date in August 2027. The faculty member will have the opportunity to teach courses in our undergraduate major in Professional Writing , as well as courses in our new Games, Narrative, and eSports certificate and possibly courses in our doctoral program in Rhetoric and Composition . Questions should be addressed to the Search Committee Chair, Professor Jennifer Bay (jbay@purdue.edu). Position Responsibilities The expected course load is four courses each semester, with administrative opportunities that could reduce the number of courses per semester. We seek applicants with outstanding teaching skills and significant expertise in the scholarship of teaching and learning. We are particularly interested in scholars who work across varied areas of study, including rhetorical theory, technical communication, storytelling, internships and career readiness, game studies, emerging technologies, and AI. Education and Experience Qualifications: A PhD in Rhetoric, Technical and/or Professional Communication, or related field is required at the time of appointment. ABD candidates will be considered for interviews, but PhD must be completed prior to August 2027. Purdue University As a top-tier public, research-intensive institution, Purdue University serves 51,000 students. Purdue University, located in West Lafayette, Indiana, is one hour from Indianapolis and two hours from Chicago. Application Procedures Candidates should submit the following application materials electronically at Purdue Careers : a letter of application describing their experience and scholarship; a CV; names and contact information for three references; evidence of teaching effectiveness; and a writing sample of no more than 25 pages. Review of applications will begin on November 9, 2026, and continues until the position is filled. Initial interviews will be conducted online. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/13/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Energy-Innovation-Engineering/44435-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Energy Innovation - Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Energy Innovation - Engineering Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44435 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Energy Innovation - Engineering City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Purdue Engineering invites applications for multiple tenure/tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor positions as part of a cluster hire in energy innovation at our West Lafayette location, led by Purdue’s Institute for Energy Innovation (IEI) . IEI brings together faculty, students, industry, government, and community partners to develop industry-driven energy solutions. IEI seeks to ensure the availability of abundant, reliable, and affordable energy; advance U.S. energy leadership and domestic supply-chain resilience; and accelerate the translation of research into technologies that are technically sound, commercially viable, and economically scalable. Its activities are organized around five major initiatives: Grid of Tomorrow, Nuclear Energy, Battery and Energy Storage, Geothermal and Natural Gas, and Critical Materials. Through this cluster hire, Purdue Engineering seeks exceptional candidates whose research interests and expertise align with one or more of the following initiatives or the crosscutting research themes described below. Research topics include, but are not limited to, the examples below: 1. Grid of Tomorrow : Power systems research to modernize the electrical grid, including grid planning and operations with large data center and industrial loads; grid data analytics and artificial intelligence and machine learning (AI/ML); grid flexibility; large-scale integration of distributed energy resources and storage; power electronics; protection; and power system dynamics. 2. Nuclear Energy : Nuclear power technologies, including small modular reactors and microreactors for distributed energy generation and industrial applications; advanced reactor technologies, nuclear materials, and the nuclear fuel cycle; fusion and plasma engineering; tritium production, handling, and management; and integration of nuclear energy with electrical grids and industrial energy systems. 3. Battery and Energy Storage : Resilient and sustainable energy-storage architectures; next-generation battery chemistries, including those using earth-abundant materials; and storage solutions for electrified mobility, aviation, defense, and the electrical grid. Across these areas, topics of interest include novel metrology, characterization, analytics, predictive modeling, safety, recycling, and scalable manufacturing. 4. Geothermal and Natural Gas : Technologies that provide reliable and abundant sources of electricity, industrial heat, and fuels, including geothermal resource development and energy systems; efficient utilization and catalytic conversion of natural gas and light hydrocarbons; carbon management; and engines and combined heat and power. 5. Critical Materials : Materials innovation and resilient domestic supply chains for energy technologies, including the discovery, design, synthesis, characterization, recovery, separation, purification, recycling, and scalable manufacturing of critical materials used in batteries, magnets, semiconductors, nuclear systems, and other energy technologies, as well as alternatives that reduce dependence on scarce materials. Across these initiatives, we welcome research on Energy Utilization , including heat pumps and industrial efficiency. Examples include technologies that improve energy efficiency in chemical, cement, and steel processing. We also welcome research on energy systems integration and engineering approaches that incorporate techno-economic analysis, energy markets, supply chains, and deployment. Opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration and industry engagement are central to IEI’s mission. Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Chemical Engineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Materials Engineering, Nuclear Engineering, or a closely related discipline by the start of employment. Early-career applicants should show evidence of initiating independent research, while mid-career applicants should demonstrate a sustained record of independent research within academic or industrial organizations, and contributions to education and/or mentoring. Successful candidates will be expected to conduct original research, attract external research support, advise graduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, and contribute service to their academic unit, the College of Engineering, Purdue University, and the broader profession. Appointments will be made in the academic school within Purdue’s College of Engineering that most closely aligns with each candidate’s background and research expertise. Applicants interested in a position in any of Purdue’s engineering schools are welcome to apply. Successful candidates will also engage with IEI and collaborate across disciplines to develop research and education programs and partnerships in energy innovation. Institute and College The Institute for Energy Innovation connects Purdue’s strengths in engineering and science with expertise in business, economics, and policy. Through interdisciplinary research, hands-on education, and partnerships with industry, government, and national laboratories, IEI helps faculty translate fundamental discoveries into practical energy technologies. Its industry engagement brings research needs and deployment challenges into academic collaborations and prepares students to contribute to the energy workforce.  Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 8 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering is a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process Applicants should submit the following materials to this site: 1. A cover letter identifying the IEI initiative or initiatives, or crosscutting research themes, most closely aligned with the applicant’s expertise and the engineering school of primary interest; 2. A complete curriculum vitae; 3. A research statement (maximum two pages, excluding references) describing the applicant’s research accomplishments and future plans, including their alignment with IEI and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration and technology translation; 4. A teaching statement (maximum two pages, excluding references) describing the applicant’s interests and approach to undergraduate and graduate education and student mentoring; and 5. The names and contact information of at least four references. Review of applications will begin on November 9, 2026 and will continue until the positions are filled. Questions regarding the positions or application process may be directed to Purdue Engineering Academic Affairs, coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . A background check is required for employment in these positions. Purdue University and the College of Engineering offer a Concierge Program that provides dual-career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/8/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Exercise-Physiology/44395-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor in Exercise Physiology",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor in Exercise Physiology Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44395 Job Title: Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor in Exercise Physiology City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Health & Kinesiology at Purdue University seeks applicants for an academic-year (9-month) clinical faculty (non-tenure track) position (Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor) with a focus in clinical exercise physiology beginning August 16, 2027. The successful candidate will teach within the Applied & Clinical Exercise Physiology graduate program and the BS in Kinesiology program. An ability to contribute to our Health and Wellness Coaching specialization is preferred but not required. The successful candidate will work with program and department leadership to develop and implement the Applied/Clinical Exercise Physiology concentration within our MS in Health and Kinesiology degree. In addition, the candidate will contribute to program accreditation. This is an exciting opportunity to work within a collaborative team at a leading public institution. Applicants must hold a master’s or doctoral (preferred but not required) degree by the time of employment in Clinical Exercise Physiology or a related field (e.g. Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Exercise Physiology, Human Performance). Applicants must have teaching experience and professional experience in applied and/or clinical exercise physiology. American College of Sports Medicine Clinical Exercise Physiologist (ACSM-CEP) or Certified Exercise Physiologist (ACSM-EP) certification is preferred. How to Apply Applications packages must be submitted as a single PDF through SuccessFactors, via the Apply Now button on the careers.purdue.edu site, Purdue Job # 44395. Inquiries and materials will be treated confidentially. All application packages should include: A curriculum vita Letter of interest describing teaching experience in higher education and/or experience in a clinical education setting Statements on Teaching and Clinical Practice Philosophy Three letters of reference (sent separately by the recommender) Three letters of reference should be sent electronically (by the recommender) to Mrs. Christy Daugherty ( daugher2@purdue.edu ), referencing the position applied for. The position will be open until it is filled. The review process will begin November 9, 2026. Questions about the position can be sent to the search chair, Cassandra Ledman, cledman@purdue.edu. A background check is required for employment in this position. About the Department of Health and Kinesiology The Department of Health & Kinesiology is one of nine units in the College of Health & Human Sciences and is home to 30 full-time faculty, 680 undergraduate students, and 80 graduate students. We offer a BS in Kinesiology with concentrations in Sports Medicine, Sport Management, and Clinical Exercise Physiology. Our graduate programs include the MS in Athletic Training (MSAT), MS in Sport Management (MSSM), MS in Health and Kinesiology, and PhD in Health and Kinesiology. Our MSAT and MSSM programs are offered in both West Lafayette and Indianapolis. About the Area About Purdue Purdue University is one of the nation’s leading land grant universities with a full range of academic majors, over 50,000 students, more than 10,000 employees, and ranked among the leading research institutions in the country. Purdue is located in West Lafayette, Indiana within easy driving distance of both Indianapolis and Chicago. The diverse greater Lafayette/West Lafayette community ( http://www.homeofpurdue.com ) has a population of approximately 200,000, and a low cost of living. Lafayette/West Lafayette Community Greater Lafayette Indiana is home to Purdue University and is one of the fastest growing communities in the Midwest. Subaru of Indiana Automotive, Caterpillar, Dow AgroSciences, Rolls-Royce, GE Aviation, Schweitzer Engineering Laboratories, Wabash National, Saab Global Defense and Security Company, high tech firms and small businesses all call Greater Lafayette their home. Conveniently located between Chicago and Indianapolis, Greater Lafayette is also near several other major metropolitan cities. ' 'Visit Lafayette-West Lafayette' and 'Greater Lafayette Commerce' are resources that highlight our great community. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/8/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
