      "description": "Associate/Full Professor of Engineering Practice - Mechanical & Civil and Construction Engineering Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44425 Job Title: Associate/Full Professor of Engineering Practice - Mechanical & Civil and Construction Engineering City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The School of Mechanical Engineering (ME) and the Lyles School of Civil and Construction Engineering (LSCCE) at Purdue University invite applications for a non-tenure track Faculty of Engineering Practice position at the rank of associate or full professor. An appointment in either School or a joint appointment is possible. Purdue University seeks to attract exceptional candidates with interests and expertise in solid mechanics, structural analysis, design, manufacturing, automation, dynamics, and/or vibration. Successful candidates must hold a Ph.D. degree, or an MSc. degree with at least 10 years of professional experience, in Civil Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Structural Engineering, Bridge Engineering, Design and Manufacturing, Automation, or a related discipline by the start date of employment. The successful candidate will have to identify an area of engineering practice that integrates their professional experiences with the Schools of Mechanical and/or Civil and Construction Engineering’s research, education, and/or engagement/outreach programs. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate core and elective courses. There will be opportunities to teach graduate level courses and to be involved in research.  Additionally, the candidate will assist with student experiential learning activities, support the Schools through industry outreach, and/or contribute to senior capstone design activities. The location of this position, including teaching responsibilities, is in Indianapolis. Schools and College The School of Mechanical Engineering at Purdue University is ranked 4th nationally for undergraduate programs, 8th for graduate programs, and 1st for online graduate programs by U.S. News and World Report. The School of ME is one of the largest in the nation, with approximately 3400 undergraduate students, 1250 graduate students, 125 faculty, and 70 staff. The School of ME is home to several high-profile research laboratories with significant infrastructure and a long tradition of collaboration with industry, national laboratories, and other universities, including Ray W. Herrick Labs, Maurice Zucrow Labs, and Maha Labs.  Purdue University motorsports engineering program has partnered with Dallara, offering students real-world hands-on training and access to cutting-edge design, aerodynamics, controls and vehicle systems in the heart of motorsports industry. The Lyles School of Civil and Construction Engineering at Purdue University in ranked 4th nationally for undergraduate programs, 7th for graduate programs, and 1st for online Master of Science in Civil Engineering by U.S. News and World Report. LSCCE has 564 students majoring in Civil Engineering (BSCE) and 94 in Construction Engineering (BSCNE). LSCCE Burke Graduate Program has 201 MSCE and 172 PhD students. There are 60 faculty, 6 lecturers, and 56 staff members supporting teaching, research, outreach, and operations. The School has large, world-class, teaching and research facilities such as the Robert L. and Terry L. Bowen Laboratory for Large-Scale Civil Engineering Research, the Christopher and Susan Burke Hydraulics and Hydrology Laboratory, the S-BRITE Center for Steel Bridge Research, Inspection, Training and Education, and the Harold Michael Traffic Operations Laboratory. The Schools of ME and CCE are integral parts of Purdue Engineering. Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 8 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering is a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit an application to this site including (1) a cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a two-page teaching plan, (4) a two-page plan that defines the area of engineering practice, and (5) names and contact information for at least three references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For information/questions regarding applications, contact Academic Affairs, College of Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on November 8th, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University offers immigration sponsorship (including both employment-based work visas and permanent residence) for highly qualified international candidates hired into eligible faculty positions, in accordance with applicable federal immigration laws and university policies. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/7/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Visiting-Assistant-Professor-in-Educational-Psychology/44392-en_US": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor in Educational Psychology",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor in Educational Psychology Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44392 Job Title: Visiting Assistant Professor in Educational Psychology City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Position Visiting Assistant Professor of Educational Psychology Job Position Description The Department of Educational Studies ( www.edst.purdue.edu ) at Purdue University invites applications for a one-year on campus Visiting Assistant Professor position in Educational Psychology to begin in August 2027, with the potential for extension for a second year. The ideal candidate will have scholarly and applied interests in educational psychology, with a focus on cognition, learning, development, and/or motivation contextualized in educational settings, such as classroom and/or informal learning environments. Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to: Conduct research and build their educational psychology-relevant scholarship. Contribute to the educational psychology graduate program area course needs by teaching courses in areas such as educational psychology, personal and social development, cognition in learning contexts, culture and cognition, and/or courses in line with their expertise, including graduate seminars and special topic seminars (2-2 course load). Mentor master’s and doctoral students in their area of expertise. Engage in other College of Education (COE) activities as appropriate, which might include forming collaborations with faculty, attending speakers’ series, and contributing to program area and departmental activities and meetings. Required Qualifications Minimum qualifications include a Doctorate in educational psychology or a closely related area by the position start date (e.g., Learning Sciences, Applied Developmental Psychology). Candidates who are ABD will be considered, but they must have their doctoral degree conferred prior to starting in August 2027. Research experience and interests relevant to educational psychology, which might include topics such as learner cognitive development, teacher quality, learner scaffolds, self-regulated learning, collaborative processes, identity, among others. Previous and sustained engagement in research as evidenced by publications, conference proceedings and presentations, and experience with a variety of research projects. Prior experience in teaching educational psychology-relevant courses within undergraduate and/or graduate preparation programs. Preferred Qualifications Excellent communication skills and demonstrated collaborative experience. Experience mentoring undergraduate or graduate students in research. The Faculty of the Educational Psychology and Research Methodology program area are committed to advancing knowledge through their scholarship and preparing scholars to be leaders in research that addresses significant educational and psychological problems. Our internationally recognized faculty members offer students strong, individualized mentoring and opportunities to develop their skills to design and conduct research. The Educational Psychology program offers a Ph.D. in Educational Studies with a concentration in Educational Psychology and Research Methodology, and a Master of Science with a concentration in Educational Psychology and Research Methodology. Both are residential programs. The successful candidate would be welcome to participate in the COE’s faculty mentoring program and receive mentoring from senior faculty. Salary Salary and benefits commensurate with qualifications and experience. Starting Date August 16, 2027 Application Procedure Applicants should submit the following: a cover letter addressing their qualifications and a statement of interest full curriculum vita teaching philosophy statement graduate transcripts, and the names and contact information of three references All materials must be submitted through Success Factors , but addressed to Toni Kempler Rogat, Chair, Educational Psychology Search Committee, Department of Educational Studies, BRNG, 100 North University Street, West Lafayette, IN 47907 . Review of applications will begin on January 19, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. Candidate must have the ability to work in the US without immigration sponsorship from Purdue University. Background Check A background check will be required for employment in this position. Equal Opportunity Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/6/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Artificial-Intelligence-for-Animal-Improvement/44394-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Artificial Intelligence for Animal Improvement",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Artificial Intelligence for Animal Improvement Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44394 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Artificial Intelligence for Animal Improvement City: Indianapolis Job Description: Title Assistant Professor of Artificial Intelligence for Animal Improvement Purdue University in Indianapolis Artificial Intelligence | Genomics | Biotechnology | Precision Animal Systems Develop the next generation of data analytics and AI-enabled methods for selecting animals, deriving novel phenotypes, and implementing precision management or interventions to improve animal production systems. Position Purdue University invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position focused on data analytics and artificial intelligence (AI)-enabled selection in animal systems. This position will be housed in Indianapolis where the candidate will have the opportunity to shape the academic and research programs offered there. We seek an innovative scholar who develops and applies AI, machine learning, data science, genomics, biotechnology, and predictive modeling to improve decision-making across animal agriculture. The successful candidate will use advanced data science and AI-enabled techniques in areas of interest, including selection and breeding of animals, derivation of novel traits and high-throughput phenotypes, health interventions, infectious disease control, precision management strategies, or production systems. The ultimate goal is to help create the next generation of intelligent animal agriculture. Candidates developing foundational or applied methods in AI, computational biology, quantitative genetics, engineering, bioinformatics, multi-omics data analytics, statistics, or related fields whose work can accelerate improvement across livestock, poultry, aquaculture, companion animals, biomedical animal models, and other relevant animal systems are encouraged to apply. Prior research centered on agricultural animals is valued but not required when a candidate's expertise can be applied to consequential problems in animal agriculture and health. The successful candidate will establish an internationally recognized and externally funded research program; collaborate across disciplines; mentor graduate students and postdoctoral scholars; and contribute to undergraduate and graduate education. The anticipated appointment will be in the Department of Animal Sciences with opportunities for collaboration and appropriate joint or courtesy appointments across Purdue. Grand Challenge How can advanced data analytics and AI enable faster, more accurate, and responsible genetic improvement and precision management to enhance animal health, resilience, productivity, welfare, and sustainability? Potential Areas of Scholarship AI-enabled selection, breeding, and genetic improvement, including genomic prediction of breeding values and phenotypes and next-generation quantitative genetics Machine learning and foundation models that integrate genomic, phenotypic, environmental, management, imaging, sensor, and multi-omics data High-throughput and digital phenotyping using computer vision, acoustic monitoring, wearable and spectroscopic technologies, robotics, and advanced sensing/diagnostics Selection of animals and derivation of novel traits for animal health and welfare, disease resistance, climate resilience, reproduction, efficiency, and product quality AI-guided selection of nutritional, microbiome, therapeutic, or management interventions Digital twins, causal models, and decision systems that predict animal performance across environments and production systems Responsible and transparent AI, including model validation, interpretability, uncertainty, fairness, data governance, and deployment in real-world animal systems Large-scale and complex data integration from diverse livestock data sources Precision animal agriculture, autonomous monitoring, and producer-facing decision support One Health applications connecting animal, human, food, and environmental health Qualifications Required Ph.D. or equivalent doctoral degree in animal sciences, artificial intelligence, animal breeding, computer science, data science, engineering, genetics, genomics, bioinformatics, computational biology, biotechnology, statistics, applied mathematics, veterinary medicine, or a closely related field by the start date. Evidence of research excellence and the potential to establish an internationally recognized, externally funded program. Demonstrated ability or strong potential to collaborate across disciplinary boundaries, teach effectively, and mentor students. Preferred Expertise in developing or applying advanced AI and machine-learning approaches to complex biological systems. Experience integrating large, multimodal, longitudinal, or multi-omics datasets. Postdoctoral research and/or teaching experience, particularly with demonstrated applications of machine learning to animal science or animal systems. A strong record of collaborative research, technology translation, industry engagement, or team science. Interest or experience in translating methods developed outside of agriculture to animal systems and real-world decision environments. Responsibilities Develop a high-impact, externally funded research program in AI-enabled selection for farm animal systems. Publish foundational and translational scholarship in impactful venues in the field and develop data resources, algorithms, software, intellectual property, computing infrastructure, or deployable technologies as appropriate. Build interdisciplinary collaborations across agriculture, engineering, computing, veterinary medicine, life sciences, statistics, health, and livestock industries. Teach courses aligned with the candidate's expertise and contribute to curricula in AI, data science, genomics, biotechnology, quantitative methods, or animal systems. Course modality is in person. The potential may exist for teaching online/distance courses during the academic year. Mentor undergraduate students, graduate students, visiting scholars, and postdoctoral researchers. Contribute service and engagement consistent with Purdue's land-grant mission. Purdue Environment Purdue offers an exceptional environment for research at the intersection of artificial intelligence, agriculture, engineering, biotechnology, animal production, animal health, and animal welfare. The successful candidate will be positioned to connect Purdue's strengths in animal sciences, agricultural and biological engineering, computer and data sciences, statistics, genomics, population genetics, bioinformatics, sensing, robotics, and One Health. The position is designed to promote collaboration across Purdue's West Lafayette and Indianapolis locations and with external partners in agriculture, animal health, biotechnology, computing, and the life sciences. The successful candidate will have access to core capabilities in high-performance computing, genomics and multi-omics, advanced instrumentation, animal research and learning facilities, and interdisciplinary graduate education. The successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate with faculty affiliated with interdisciplinary initiatives and centers including the Institute for Digital and Advanced Agricultural Systems, Institute for Plant Sciences, Center for Plant Biology, Institute for Digital Forestry, Institute for a Sustainable Future, Indiana Water Resources Research Center, Institute for Physical Artificial Intelligence (IPAI), Purdue Computes, and Purdue's One Health Initiative, and a growing ecosystem of AI, computing, sustainability, and resilient systems programs. The College The College of Agriculture is one of the world’s leading colleges of agricultural, food, life, and natural resource sciences. The College is ranked third in the U.S. and sixth in the world in the 2026 QS World University Rankings. The College is deeply committed to the three land-grant missions (teaching, research, and extension), to international activities and perspectives that span all missions, and to excellence in all we do. The College has 10 academic departments, 294 faculty, 2,842 undergraduate students, and 694 graduate students. Rank and Appointment This is an academic-year, tenure-track appointment at the Assistant Professor level. Salary, startup support, and resources will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. A background check is required for employment in this position. Application Process Applicants should submit the following materials through Purdue’s online faculty application system: A cover letter describing the candidate's interest in the position and fit with AI-enabled selection for animal systems Curriculum vitae A research statement describing accomplishments, future vision, potential funding pathways, and opportunities for collaboration A teaching and mentoring statement Names and contact information for three references All materials must be combined into a single PDF and submitted electronically in the CV field on the application link Application link: [insert link here] Review date: begins November 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled Search contact: Luiz Brito, britol@purdue.edu A Broad Invitation Candidates from AI, animal sciences, bioinformatics, computer science, engineering, genomics, biotechnology, population or quantitative genetics, computational biology, statistics, and related disciplines are strongly encouraged to apply. Candidates do not need to have built their careers exclusively in animal agriculture. We are interested in scholars whose methods, discoveries, and technologies can be translated to improve farm animal systems. About Purdue University Purdue University is a leading public research institution with a strong land-grant mission and a culture of interdisciplinary innovation. The College of Agriculture advances discovery, education, and engagement across agricultural, food, life, and natural resource sciences. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/6/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Head-of-the-Department-of-Speech%2C-Language%2C-and-Hearing-Sciences-%28SLHS%29/44124-en_US": {
      "title": "Head of the Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences (SLHS)",
      "description": "Head of the Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences (SLHS) Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44124 Job Title: Head of the Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences (SLHS) City: West Lafayette Job Description: Position Summary The Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences (SLHS) in the College of Health and Human Sciences at Purdue University invites applications and nominations for the position of Department Head. The position is a full-time, 12-month appointment and will be available July 1, 2027. We seek an accomplished and dynamic academic leader with a strong record of achievement as a faculty member, a history of skillful interdisciplinary leadership, and an inspiring vision for the Department. The SLHS Head will be an internationally recognized scholar who serves as a member of the College’s leadership team and provides strategic, academic, and administrative leadership for the Department. The Head will oversee all aspects of departmental operations at the West Lafayette campus while fostering a growth-oriented vision for expanding the Department’s presence and opportunities at the Indianapolis campus. Responsibilities Key responsibilities include supporting faculty and staff recruitment, development, and success; advancing excellence and innovation in research, teaching, clinical education, and engagement; strengthening alumni and community relationships; and advocating for the Department within the College, across the University, and among external partners and stakeholders. EDUCATION The Head provides leadership and oversight for the Department’s educational programs, fostering excellence and innovation across undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and clinical education.  The Head supports the continued development of curricula and learning environment that prepare students for excellence in clinical practice, research, and other professional careers. The Head also ensures that accredited programs maintain compliance with the standards of the Council on Academic Accreditation and works collaboratively with faculty and program leaders to identify opportunities for continued growth and improvement. TALENT DEVELOPMENT The Head recruits, develops, supports, and retains outstanding faculty and staff and ensures that key leadership roles within the Department are filled by dedicated and talented individuals. The Head fosters an environment in which faculty and staff can thrive across research, teaching, clinical service, engagement, leadership, and professional development. Recognizing the breadth and interdisciplinary nature of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences, the Head supports the varied contributions and career trajectories of faculty and staff while developing the talent and leadership necessary to advance the Department’s strategic priorities. RESEARCH ADVANCEMENT The Head fosters an environment that supports innovative, high-impact research and scholarship across the breadth of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences. The Head supports faculty in developing and sustaining successful research programs, including efforts to secure external funding, and advocates for the resources and infrastructure necessary to advance the Department’s research mission. The Head also promotes interdisciplinary collaboration within and beyond the Department and identifies opportunities to expand the reach, visibility, and impact of its research. Responsibilities Continued FISCAL OVERSIGHT AND COMPLIANCE The Head provides responsible stewardship of the Department’s financial and other resources, leading budgeting and resource-allocation processes in alignment with departmental priorities and strategic goals. The Head considers diverse perspectives in financial decision-making while effectively managing and leveraging available resources. The Head also ensures compliance with applicable University policies and procedures and relevant regulations and laws. PHILANTHROPY AND ALUMNI RELATIONS The Head works collaboratively with College and University advancement leaders to strengthen philanthropic support for the Department and advance its strategic priorities. The Head articulates the Department’s vision, accomplishments, and opportunities to alumni, donors, and other stakeholders and helps cultivate relationships that may lead to philanthropic investment. The Head also supports alumni engagement efforts that strengthen connections among alumni, the Department, the College, and the University. Minimum Qualifications The successful candidate will have a strong record of academic and/or clinical accomplishment and a demonstrated commitment to advancing the research, teaching, clinical, and engagement missions of the Department. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. or other appropriate terminal degree, have expertise in an area represented within Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences, and be eligible for appointment as a Clinical Professor or tenured Full Professor at Purdue University. Candidates must demonstrate the leadership experience and ability to support and advance the Department’s research portfolio, educational and clinical programs, and the success of its faculty, staff, students, and clinicians. The successful candidate will demonstrate a collaborative and transparent leadership approach that values mentorship, partnership, shared governance, and the contributions of individuals across the Department. The successful candidate will uphold the Department’s core values and foster an environment in which faculty, staff, students, and clinicians can thrive. ADDITIONAL PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Demonstrated record of successful administrative leadership in a complex academic or clinical organization, including fiscal and resource management. History of mentorship and leadership focused on excellence and professional development. Strategic national academic and research leader, grounded in personal integrity with the ability to energize, inspire, and encourage faculty and student innovation as well as interdisciplinary collaboration. Industry partnership experience and vision. Evidence of effective community involvement, outreach, leadership, and demonstrated ability to forge partnerships and build productive relationships with both campus and community constituencies. Demonstrated commitment to student centeredness and optimization of student learning reflected by active and visible engagement in student activities, initiatives, and programs. About the Department The SLHS department is housed within Lyles-Porter Hall, designed specifically to house the research and clinical operations of the department and opened in 2014. The department includes the M.D. Steer Speech, Language and Hearing Clinics, which provide diagnostic and rehabilitative services to patients across the lifespan while facilitating clinical education and research collaborations. SLHS additionally houses state-of-the-art research spaces to support cutting-edge research in areas of speech, language, hearing, voice, swallowing and balance. The Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences is a diverse and collegial department with 17 tenure-track and 15 clinical faculty members and a thriving interdisciplinary community. SLHS is a national leader in clinical education and research and offers an undergraduate degree (BS) and graduate degrees in Audiology (AuD), Speech-Language Pathology (MS-SLHS), and Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences (PhD). The Department's graduate programs in Audiology and Speech-Language Pathology consistently rank among the top 10 nationally according to U.S. News & World Report.  The Department’s research profile is strong and growing, with over $5 million in research expenditures over the prior year, and over $10 million in extramural awards in the past six months. Faculty in the Department lead two interdisciplinary NIH training grants in Communication Disorders and Auditory Neuroscience. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to capitalize on an extraordinary network of collaborations and resources that support interdisciplinary and translational research. Current faculty collaborate with the Department of Psychological Sciences, Weldon School of Biomedical Engineering, Department of Biological Sciences, Department of Linguistics, College of Veterinary Medicine, Indiana University School of Medicine, Purdue Autism Research Center, Methodology Center at Purdue, Center for Brain, Behavior, and NeuroRehabilitation, Purdue Institute for Integrative Neuroscience, Center for Early Learning, Center on Aging and the Life Course, Cognition, Agency, and Intelligence Center, and Purdue Polytechnic Institute. Faculty also have access to an adjacent state-of-the-art MRI research facility. About the College of Health and Human Sciences The College of Health and Human Sciences (HHS) is the fourth-largest College at Purdue. It includes nine academic units that hold national and international recognition for their fundamental scientific and programmatic contributions to improving individuals and communities' health. The College strives to elevate Purdue's reputation in the health and human sciences by positioning the University to meet the health and wellness challenges facing the population, growing and creating opportunities for Indiana and the global economy, and enhancing student learning for success in a rapidly changing world. HHS's multidisciplinary learning environment uniquely prepares students to contribute to improved human health and behavior and to serve as leaders in their disciplines. The College also provides a rich environment for world-changing research and discovery. Purdue's land-grant mission facilitates the translation of these discoveries from theory to application, benefiting not only those in Indiana, but society as a whole. About Purdue University Established in 1869, Purdue is Indiana's land-grant University, a comprehensive educational and research institution, and a member of the American Association of Universities (AAU). In addition to the College of Health and Human Sciences, Purdue University's strengths in Agriculture, Education, Engineering, Liberal Arts, Management, Pharmacy, Science, and Veterinary Medicine contribute to a robust research and educational environment. The West Lafayette and Indianapolis campuses have ten academic colleges with an enrollment of over 57,000 students from over 120 countries. With the new Indianapolis location, Purdue is preparing career-ready students for the jobs of tomorrow. Strong industry partnerships accelerate hands-on learning opportunities, internships, and co-ops. Procedure for Candidacy Nominations and applications will be accepted until the position is filled. For best consideration, applications should be received by December 1, 2026, and include a letter of interest describing relevant experience and qualifications, a statement of leadership philosophy, a full curriculum vitae, and contact information for at least three professional references. Additional references or recommendations may be required based on the faculty appointment type. References will be contacted only for candidates selected for an on-campus interview. Applications must be submitted through Purdue University's online application system at Purdue Careers . Nominations and questions regarding the position may be directed to Aubry Johnson, arjohns@purdue.edu, Lead Executive Recruiter. A background check will be required for employment in this position. Career Stream Faculty 6 Equal Opportunity Employer Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/6/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Philosophy/44309-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate Professor of Philosophy Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44309 Job Title: Assistant / Associate Professor of Philosophy City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary As part of Purdue University’s strategic investment in One Health – Healthy and Resilient Living Systems, the Department of Philosophy within the College of Liberal Arts invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. The Department of Philosophy seeks faculty who can contribute to the Department’s mission while working collaboratively with One Health researchers. Area of Specialization •Bioethics (broadly construed) Area of Competence •One of (1) Philosophy of Science, (2) Philosophy, Politics, and Economics, and (3) Philosophy of Artificial Intelligence Applicants are expected to demonstrate a track record of securing external funding, or the promise of creating one. Purdue’s One Health Initiative This strategic recruitment will help advance Purdue’s One Health initiative ( https://www.purdue.edu/onehealth/) which seeks to tackle complex challenges with real-world impact at the intersection of human, animal, and plant health. This recruitment initiative builds on previous strategic faculty recruitment initiatives in: (1) Integrated Health; (2) AI-Driven Biomolecular Design, and (3) Advanced Chemistry. In addition, a parallel strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Intelligent Medicines is ongoing. Through academic programs, research, facility infrastructure and industry partnerships, Purdue’s One Health efforts are making giant leaps in improving health outcomes for all living things and driving economic growth regionally and globally. This strategic faculty recruitment initiative focused on Healthy and Resilient Living Systems is expected to build on prior recruitment initiatives and existing Purdue research and academic strengths, to transform research and impact human, animal and environmental health by bridging silos and fostering collaboration across disciplines. The health and prosperity of society depend upon resilient living systems that connect ecosystems, plants, animals, insects, microbes, and people. Emerging and chronic diseases, food insecurity, environmental degradation, climate change, nutrient deficiencies, invasive species, and ecosystem disruption are increasingly interconnected challenges that require integrated approaches across biological scales and disciplinary boundaries. This strategic recruitment initiative will help establish Purdue as a national leader in predicting, designing, and improving living systems that support health, sustainability, and economic vitality. Working with existing campus experts, this cluster would develop innovative solutions that enhance health resilience from genes and microbiomes to organisms, food systems, populations, and ecosystems. By integrating strengths in agriculture, engineering, artificial intelligence, data science, and health sciences, Purdue aims to create a globally distinctive platform for addressing complex challenges at the intersection of food systems, environmental stewardship, animal and human health, and economic prosperity. Qualifications •A Ph.D. in Philosophy or a related discipline •A record of research excellence and productivity commensurate with rank •Demonstrated potential or record of interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship •Commitment to teaching and student mentorship Faculty Responsibilities •Establish a vigorous, externally funded research program • Teach and develop undergraduate and graduate courses with the Philosophy program, and mentor and supervise students as needed •Collaborate across disciplines to solve complex global one health challenges Job Summary Continued Integration within the Purdue One Health Community Collectively, the strategic faculty recruitment initiatives represent a forward-thinking investment in Purdue’s research infrastructure and academic excellence. Faculty hired as part of these One Health strategic faculty recruitment initiatives will be supported as part of the overall One Health community. Together, these faculty members are expected to work across diverse disciplines, enhance Purdue’s external funding potential, and drive innovation at the intersection of health, environment, food, and economics. In addition to joining an academic unit, faculty hired under this initiative will have the opportunity to join a vibrant ecosystem of interdisciplinary centers and institutes, that span the hard tech corridor between Indianapolis and West Lafayette including: •Cognition, Agency, and Intelligence Center (CAIC) •Center for Aging and the Life Course (CALC) •Center for Rural and Migrant Health •Center for Health Analytics and Therapeutic Intelligence •Institute for a Sustainable Future The integrated, cross-disciplinary nature of One Health is essential for addressing today’s most urgent One Health challenges and ensuring Purdue’s continued leadership in research, education, and community impact. Application Process To apply, please submit a cover letter, CV, research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin on November 6, 2026 and continue until positions are filled. Applications should be submitted at: https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Philosophy/44309-en_US/ . A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/6/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
