      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice - Indianapolis",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Practice - Indianapolis Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44326 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Practice - Indianapolis City: INDIANAPOLIS Job Description: Job Summary Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice in Mathematics The Department of Mathematics in the College of Science at Purdue University invites applications for multiple appointments as Professor of Practice in Mathematics at Purdue University Indianapolis to begin in August 2027.  These appointments will be at the level of Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice. Purdue University in Indianapolis is a new, fully integrated expansion of the West Lafayette campus, extending to central Indiana the academic rigor and accessible excellence for which Purdue is known. As the state’s only public top 10 university, most trusted university and most innovative university, Purdue is focused and committed to strengthening its presence in Indiana’s industrial and technological center. Purdue in Indianapolis is creating an innovative, STEM-based collegiate experience by connecting future-ready Purdue students and faculty in Indianapolis to local businesses to accelerate Indiana’s STEM pipeline and tech ecosystem, fueling impact for our region and the world. Learn more about Purdue’s latest giant leap at https://www.purdue.edu/campuses/indianapolis/ . For more information about our department, see https://www.math.purdue.edu/ . These positions are non-tenure track faculty positions with multi-year contracts, a promotion track, and a focus on undergraduate teaching and course administration.  Duties will typically consist of teaching 5-6 courses in Indianapolis each academic year, including large-lecture courses, course coordination, and/or other related scholarly and administrative activities. Successful applicants will have a documented record of effective teaching, the ability to teach a range of courses in the undergraduate curriculum, a commitment to teaching, mentoring, and interacting with undergraduate students, and a willingness to observe classes and provide teaching guidance to new instructors. Candidates should specifically note in their application any experience they have had with teaching large-lecture Calculus classes, teaching upper-division undergraduate courses, coordinating learning management or online homework systems, and any other unique teaching qualifications (such as experience with innovative instructional methods). Candidates must have a PhD (or its equivalent) in mathematics or a closely related field by the start of the appointment. Teaching experience after obtaining a PhD will be viewed favorably. Professors of Practice faculty will be involved in departmental activities and have professional development opportunities.  Salary and benefits are competitive. Application Process Applications should be submitted online through www.mathjobs.org and should include (1) the AMS cover sheet for academic employment, (2) a cover letter, (3) a curriculum vitae, (4) a teaching statement, and (5) at least three letters of recommendation focused on the candidate’s teaching qualifications. In addition, for purposes of equity, to be considered for the position, applicants will also need to create a profile including voluntary demographic data at SuccessFactors . Reference letter writers should be asked to submit their letters online through www.mathjobs.org. Direct all inquiries to mathexec@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on 1 November 2026 and continue until the positions are filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Department-HeadProfessor-Political-Science/44329-en_US": {
      "title": "Department Head/Professor Political Science",
      "description": "Department Head/Professor Political Science Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44329 Job Title: Department Head/Professor Political Science City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The College of Liberal Arts at Purdue University invites applications for the position of Department Head, Political Science. The college seeks a dynamic leader with creative vision and an outstanding record of research, teaching, and service as well as previous administrative leadership experience to fill this position. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Liberal Arts, the successful applicant will work alongside talented faculty, promote collaboration across disciplines, and play a crucial role in shaping the future of the college. Department of Political Science Overview In the last three years, the Purdue Political Science Department has hired over a dozen faculty, bringing the total tenure track faculty size to 30, in addition to full-time teaching and visiting faculty.  These investments have created departmental strengths in the study of political institutions and political economy, democracy and authoritarianism, and AI and technology, adding to existing strengths in conflict and modern warfare and environmental politics and policy, as well as politics, groups and identities.  The department’s undergraduate program is one of the largest in the College of Liberal Arts, with 558 majors, a 130 percent increase since 2020. Recent PhD graduates have secured tenure-track positions at R1 and liberal arts institutions, as well as in competitive postdoctoral and industry positions. The Department is home or co-home to several university-recognized research centers, including the Center for C-SPAN Scholarship & Engagement (CCSE), the Governance and Responsible AI Lab (GRAIL), the Joe and Maggie Kernan (JMK) Experimental Lab, the Methodology Center at Purdue (MCAP), and the Program on American Institutional Renewal (PAIR), in addition to a wide variety of active department-level labs.   Weekly presentations by faculty, graduate students, and visiting faculty create a stimulating environment for research discussions and collaborations. The department is an enthusiastic contributor to the College’s high level of interdisciplinarity, through both research centers and instructional opportunities with Cornerstone Integrated Liberal Arts. College of Liberal Arts Overview This is an exciting time to join the leadership team in the College of Liberal Arts at Purdue University. As a vital component of a leading public research university, the college features a wide variety of excellent academic programs across the arts, humanities, and social sciences. We are committed to interdisciplinarity, innovation, and national leadership in higher education, most notably through our nationally recognized Cornerstone Integrated Liberal Arts program, which reaches more than 10,000 students per year across campus. Purdue offers substantial support for research and teaching at both the university and college levels. The college’s Office of Research advances scholarship across its fields through a portfolio of targeted programs designed to promote collaboration and research excellence. The college’s commitment to interdisciplinarity and innovation is apparent through its many faculty-led centers, labs, and initiatives.  The college and its faculty are deeply committed to teaching excellence, and to the central role that liberal arts play in grounding a university curriculum. The deep integration of graduate and undergraduate students into research and experiential learning are among its major strengths. The college values intellectual rigor, open debate, and the exploration of diverse perspectives in the pursuit of knowledge. Job Summary Continued Essential Duties and Responsibilities Department / School Heads in the College of Liberal Arts serve as visionary academic leaders and chief advocates for their departments. They are responsible for driving strategic direction while ensuring operational excellence within their units. Primary responsibilities include academic leadership; managing the department’s budget; faculty and lecturer mentorship and career development; advancing undergraduate and graduate student success, which may include teaching at the graduate level; strategic resource management; and fostering external relations. Heads collaborate closely with the Dean and the college’s senior leadership team, partnering across departments to champion interdisciplinary initiatives and innovative problem-solving. Because Purdue is deeply invested in leadership development, Department Heads are supported by both the college and the provost’s office through programs such as the New Heads Forum and ongoing professional development opportunities. Required Qualifications Applicants must have: a terminal degree related to the research areas of the Department of Political Science; a record of scholarly achievement suitable for appointment as a full professor at Purdue; demonstrated excellence in teaching and mentoring of students and faculty; evidence of effective academic leadership; experience with securing extramural funding; outstanding interpersonal and communication skills with dedication to building and maintaining strong relationships with alumni and other stakeholders; and evidence of successful leadership in promoting a culture of intellectual openness and respectful exchange of ideas across multiple perspectives of scholarship. Applications We encourage qualified candidates to submit application materials online at https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Department-HeadProfessor-Political-Science/44329-en_US/ , including a letter of application that describes qualifications for the position, curriculum vitae, names of three references, and statement of administrative / leadership philosophy. Review of applications will begin November 10, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Questions should be directed to Search Chair, Elena Coda at ecoda@purdue.edu.  A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University, the College of Liberal Arts, and the Department of Political Science are committed to free and open inquiry in all matters. Candidates are encouraged to address in their cover letter how they are prepared to contribute to a climate that values free inquiry and academic freedom. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-One-Health-Intelligent-Medicines-College-of-HHS/44312-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in One Health - Intelligent Medicines - College of HHS",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in One Health - Intelligent Medicines - College of HHS Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44312 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in One Health - Intelligent Medicines - College of HHS City: West Lafayette Job Description: Strategic Faculty Recruitment Initiative in One Health – Intelligent Medicines As part of this strategic recruitment initiative, faculty are being recruited into the Department of Health and Kinesiology and the School of Health Sciences in the College of Health and Human Sciences. The Department of Health and Kinesiology (HK) seeks candidates with expertise in biomechanics, movement science, neuromuscular function, or related disciplines whose research advances Intelligent Medicine for musculoskeletal health and mobility. We are particularly interested in investigators who integrate advanced sensing technologies, artificial intelligence, computational modeling, and digital health approaches to understand human movement, develop digital biomarkers and digital twins, and create innovative solutions for the prevention, diagnosis, treatment, and rehabilitation of musculoskeletal or neurological conditions. Applications aimed at improving mobility, physical function, and personalized healthcare through data-driven and AI-enabled approaches are especially encouraged. The School of Health Sciences (HSCI) is a world leader in identifying mechanisms of disease, thereby discovering novel therapeutic targets. Applicants who can improve human, animal, and environmental health through the integration of technology, data, and systems thinking are most desired. Particularly desired are applicants who use image-guided methods (MRI, PET, CT, optical) to develop therapeutic applications (radiotherapy, immunotherapy, phototherapy), or study environmental health through the integration of technology, data, and systems thinking, with strong alignment towards intelligent medicine. Job Summary Purdue University invites applications for multiple tenured or tenure-track faculty positions as part of a multi-department strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Intelligent Medicines. This strategic recruitment will help advance Purdue’s One Health initiative ( https://www.purdue.edu/onehealth/ ) which seeks to tackle complex challenges with real-world impact at the intersection of human, animal, and plant health. This recruitment initiative builds on previous strategic faculty recruitment initiatives in: (1) Integrated Health; (2) AI-Driven Biomolecular Design, and (3) Advanced Chemistry. In addition, a parallel strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Healthy and Resilient Living Systems is ongoing. Through academic programs, research, facility infrastructure and industry partnerships, Purdue is making giant leaps in improving health outcomes for all living things and driving economic growth regionally and globally. This strategic faculty recruitment initiative focused on Intelligent Medicine s is expected to build on prior recruitment initiatives and existing Purdue research and academic strengths, to transform research and impact human, animal and environmental health by bridging silos and fostering collaboration across disciplines. The Intelligent Medicines theme seeks to create a framework that improves human, animal, and environmental health through the integration of technology, data, and systems thinking. This faculty recruitment initiative is disease agnostic and aims to establish new capabilities in AI-enabled therapeutic development, non-animal models of disease, advanced manufacturing, intelligent health systems, digital twins, robotics, human factors, supply chain resilience, and health technology innovation. By combining strengths in device innovation, computational intelligence, manufacturing systems, and healthcare operations, Purdue intends to create a highly visible flagship that strengthens industry engagement, expands workforce development opportunities, and attracts significant external funding. Faculty Responsibilities Establish a vigorous, externally funded research program Contribute to the education and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students. Teach undergraduate and/or graduate level courses. Course modality is generally in person. The potential may exist for teaching online/distance courses during the academic year. Collaborate across disciplines to solve complex global one health challenges Integration within the Purdue One Health Community Collectively, the strategic faculty recruitment initiatives represent a forward-thinking investment in Purdue’s research infrastructure and academic excellence. Faculty hired as part of these One Health strategic faculty recruitment initiatives will be supported as part of the overall One Health community. Together, these faculty members are expected to work across diverse disciplines, enhance Purdue’s external funding potential, and drive innovation at the intersection of health, environment, food, and economics. In addition to joining an academic unit, faculty hired under this initiative will have the opportunity to join a vibrant ecosystem of interdisciplinary centers and institutes, that span the hard tech corridor between Indianapolis and West Lafayette including: Center for Aging and the Life Course (CALC) Purdue University Research Center in Economics (PURCE) Center for Rural and Migrant Health Center for Health Analytics and Therapeutic Intelligence Purdue Institute for Cancer Research (PICR) Purdue Center for Musculoskeletal Engineering Institute for Digital Forestry Institute for Digital and Advanced Agricultural Systems Institute for a Sustainable Future Indiana Water Resources Research Center The integrated, cross-disciplinary nature of One Health is essential for addressing today’s most urgent health challenges and ensuring Purdue’s continued leadership in research, education, and community impact. Qualifications A doctoral degree in Health and Kinesiology or from a discipline (Sports Medicine, Biomechanics, or Biomedical Engineering) that matched with the needed expertise; or a discipline relevant to this search within the School of Health sciences (e.g., Medical Physics, Toxicology, Biochemistry, Chemistry, Physics, Physiology), or related field A record of research excellence and productivity commensurate with rank Demonstrated potential or record of interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship Commitment to teaching and student mentorship Application Process To apply, please submit a cover letter, CV, research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin on November 5, 2026, and continue until positions are filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Professor%2C-Ophthalmology/43927-en_US": {
      "title": "Professor, Ophthalmology",
      "description": "Professor, Ophthalmology Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 43927 Job Title: Professor, Ophthalmology City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Purdue University College of Veterinary Medicine (PVM), Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences (VCS), invites applications for a full-time (12 month) Clinical or Tenure-Track position in Veterinary Ophthalmology at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. The successful candidate will join three board certified ophthalmologists, and a growing team including registered veterinary technician, veterinary assistant, ophthalmology client liaison, and three ophthalmology residents. The successful candidate will have access to a dedicated ophthalmology operating suite, two state-of-the-art operating microscopes, two phacoemulsification units, anterior and posterior segment digital photography equipment (including an infrared camera, SL19 plus, and RetCam), diode and CO2 lasers, ocular ultrasonography equipment (high resolution and ultrasound biomicroscopy units), Spectralis OCT and OCTA, ERG unit capable of pattern and multi-focal ERG, HRT3 confocal microscope, and an on-site CT and MRI. The caseload is comprised predominantly of small animal and equine cases with additional farm animal and exotic cases. PVM is highly supportive of individual faculty career growth and development. A formal faculty mentoring program is in place and mentorship of junior faculty members is a high priority. Qualifications Qualifications for the position include a DVM or equivalent degree, and completion of an ophthalmology residency program approved by the American Board of Veterinary Ophthalmology (ABVO) or European College of Veterinary Ophthalmologists (ECVO), or board certification by the ABVO/ECVO. Salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. A background check is required for employment in this position. General Information The Purdue University Veterinary Hospital recently completed a large expansion with the opening of the David and Bonnie Brunner Purdue Veterinary Medical Hospital Complex, a 162,500-square-foot facility. The new complex includes the Small Animal Hospital, which adds 65,000 square feet to the existing small animal facilities, as well as the Equine Hospital and the Farm Animal Hospital. These facilities provide exceptional resources for teaching, clinical service, and interdisciplinary research, enabling faculty to deliver outstanding patient care while educating the next generation of veterinary professionals. Responsibilities The successful candidate will actively participate in the learning, discovery, and engagement activities of the PVM and the VCS department with a focus on learning and engagement. Important activities include: Teaching/Learning : Participation in lectures and laboratories in the DVM and veterinary nursing curricula, clinical teaching in the Purdue University Veterinary Hospital (PUVH), and participation in training house officers. Clinical Service : Providing excellent clinical service to both large and small animal patients (typical time commitment: 30 -50% Tenure Track and 60-70% Clinical Track); instructing and supervising veterinary and veterinary nursing students, and house officers; and building strong relationships with referring veterinarians. Discovery : All faculty are expected to collaborate on clinical research projects. Research that complements the interests and strengths of current faculty is ideal but can also be tailored to the candidate’s specific background and interests. Strong internal grant programs are available to support faculty and resident research. Faculty also participate in university-wide graduate programs (MS and PhD). Service and Engagement : Faculty are also expected to participate in committee work, professional organizations and community service, deliver of continuing education programs and other appropriate professional activities. College and Department Commitment to the College and Departmental missions of learning, discovery, and engagement, and support of the College and Department strategic plans are essential. The College of Veterinary Medicine at Purdue University values, nurtures, and respects all members of its community and ensures an environment of inclusive excellence where all students, faculty, and staff are inspired and empowered to achieve their full potential. Applications Review of applications will begin in November 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should provide a letter of intent describing professional goals, including teaching philosophy; curriculum vitae; and the names and contact information of three professional references via the provided link: Current employees apply via the provided link: Equal Opportunity Purdue University is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-One-Health-Healthy-and-Resilient-Living-Systems-College-of-HHS/44311-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in One Health - Healthy and Resilient Living Systems - College of HHS",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in One Health - Healthy and Resilient Living Systems - College of HHS Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44311 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in One Health - Healthy and Resilient Living Systems - College of HHS City: West Lafayette Job Description: Strategic Faculty Recruitment Initiative in One Health – Healthy and Resilient Living Systems As part of this strategic recruitment initiative, faculty are being recruited into the Departments of Psychological Sciences and Public Health in the College of Health and Human Sciences. The Department of Psychological Sciences seeks faculty who could speak to the Cluster’s focus on the interplay between nutritional health and environmental factors, stress, and metabolism, complemented by related work on environmental contaminants and their effects on brain function and mental health. Another area of interest is in sustainable work systems, worker health and safety, and organizational resilience, connecting individual and workplace health to broader community and system-level resilience. Individuals who can contribute to the Behavioral Neuroscience, Industrial-Organizational, and Clinical Psychology areas are particularly desired. Candidates' research should address behavior, brain function, or mental health. The Department of Public Health emphasizes collaborative interdisciplinary approaches to improving health at the intersection of human, animal, plant, and environmental health. The Department’s research encompasses social determinants of health, health inequities, disease prevention, epidemiology, biostatistics, nutrition, and community-engaged interventions. Particular areas of interest include, but are not limited to, emerging infectious diseases and One Health epidemiology; environmental and climate health; food systems, nutrition, and population health; rural and community health resilience; and artificial intelligence, data science, and population health. Job Summary Purdue University invites applications for multiple tenured or tenure-track faculty positions as part of a multi-department strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Healthy and Resilient Living Systems. This strategic recruitment will help advance Purdue’s One Health initiative ( https://www.purdue.edu/onehealth/ ) which seeks to tackle complex challenges with real-world impact at the intersection of human, animal, and plant health. This recruitment initiative builds on previous strategic faculty recruitment initiatives in: (1) Integrated Health; (2) AI-Driven Biomolecular Design, and (3) Advanced Chemistry. In addition, a parallel strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Intelligent Medicines is ongoing. Through academic programs, research, facility infrastructure and industry partnerships, Purdue’s One Health efforts are making giant leaps in improving health outcomes for all living things and driving economic growth regionally and globally. This strategic faculty recruitment initiative focused on Healthy and Resilient Living Systems is expected to build on prior recruitment initiatives and existing Purdue research and academic strengths, to transform research and impact human, animal and environmental health by bridging silos and fostering collaboration across disciplines. The health and prosperity of society depend upon resilient living systems that connect ecosystems, plants, animals, insects, microbes, and people. Emerging and chronic diseases, food insecurity, environmental degradation, climate change, nutrient deficiencies, invasive species, and ecosystem disruption are increasingly interconnected challenges that require integrated approaches across biological scales and disciplinary boundaries. Th is strategic recruitment initiative will help establish Purdue as a national leader in predicting, designing, and improving living systems that support health, sustainability, and economic vitality. Working with existing campus experts, this cluster would develop innovative solutions that enhance health resilience from genes and microbiomes to organisms, food systems, populations, and ecosystems. By integrating strengths in agriculture, engineering, artificial intelligence, data science, and health sciences, Purdue aims to create a globally distinctive platform for addressing complex challenges at the intersection of food systems, environmental stewardship, animal and human health, and economic prosperity. Faculty Responsibilities Establish a vigorous, externally funded research program. Contribute to the education and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students. Teach undergraduate and/or graduate level courses. Course modality is generally in person. The potential may exist for teaching online/distance courses during the academic year. Collaborate across disciplines to solve complex global one health challenges. Integration within the Purdue One Health Community Collectively, the strategic faculty recruitment initiatives represent a forward-thinking investment in Purdue’s research infrastructure and academic excellence. Faculty hired as part of these One Health strategic faculty recruitment initiatives will be supported as part of the overall One Health community. Together, these faculty members are expected to work across diverse disciplines, enhance Purdue’s external funding potential, and drive innovation at the intersection of health, environment, food, and economics. In addition to joining an academic unit, faculty hired under this initiative will have the opportunity to join a vibrant ecosystem of interdisciplinary centers and institutes, that span the hard tech corridor between Indianapolis and West Lafayette including: Center for Aging and the Life Course (CALC) Purdue University Research Center in Economics (PURCE) Center for Rural and Migrant Health Center for Health Analytics and Therapeutic Intelligence Purdue Institute for Cancer Research (PICR) Purdue Center for Musculoskeletal Engineering Institute for Digital Forestry Institute for Digital and Advanced Agricultural Systems Institute for a Sustainable Future Indiana Water Resources Research Center Ingestive Behavior Research Center (IBRC) The integrated, cross-disciplinary nature of One Health is essential for addressing today’s most urgent One Health challenges and ensuring Purdue’s continued leadership in research, education, and community impact. Qualifications For Psychological Sciences, candidates may hold a PhD or other appropriate doctoral degree in psychology (including behavioral neuroscience, clinical psychology, or industrial-organizational psychology), neuroscience, biopsychology, physiology, endocrinology, nutritional sciences, toxicology, organizational behavior, or a related discipline. For Public Health, candidates may hold a PhD or other appropriate doctoral degree in psychology, neuroscience, public health, epidemiology, community health, environmental health sciences, One Health, nutritional sciences, health sciences, health services research, biostatistics, or a related discipline. A record of research excellence and productivity commensurate with rank Demonstrated potential or record of interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship Commitment to teaching and student mentorship Application Process To apply, please submit a cover letter, CV, research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin on November 5, 2026 and continue until positions are filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor%2C-Dermatology/43428-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Dermatology",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Dermatology Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 43428 Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor, Dermatology City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Purdue University College of Veterinary Medicine (PVM), Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences (VCS), invites applications for a full-time, 12-month Clinical-Track or Tenure-Track faculty position in Veterinary Dermatology at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. The successful candidate will join a well-established comparative dermatology service that currently includes one clinical-track associate professor, one licensed veterinary technician, and one veterinary technician assistant. Applicants must hold a DVM or equivalent degree and meet at least one of the following criteria: hold board certification by the ACVD or ECVD, have completed an ACVD-approved residency, or be currently enrolled in an ACVD-approved residency with an interest in an academic career. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience, and employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. The Dermatology Service is equipped with advanced technology, including a Karl Storz video otoscope, a VetScalpel CO₂ surgical laser, Nikon microscopy systems, and modern anesthesia equipment. Facilities comprise a spacious main procedure room with a wet table, an adjacent room dedicated to minor procedures and housing cage banks, and a shared surgical suite for laser procedures. Together, these resources support a diverse and growing caseload while fostering excellent opportunities for clinical training, scholarship, and innovation. Responsibilities The successful candidate will actively contribute to the College's missions of learning, discovery, and engagement. Teaching responsibilities include participation in lectures and laboratories within the Doctor of Veterinary Medicine and Veterinary Technology programs, clinical instruction in the Purdue University Veterinary Hospital (PVH), and mentorship of house officers, including interns and residents. Faculty members also have opportunities to participate in university-wide graduate education programs leading to MS and PhD degrees. Clinical responsibilities include providing specialty dermatology services within the Purdue University Veterinary Hospital, supervising veterinary students as well as house officers, and fostering strong relationships with referring veterinarians. Clinical-track faculty are expected to engage in collaborative clinical research and scholarly activities. Purdue University's highly collaborative environment offers extensive opportunities for both clinical and basic science research within and beyond the College of Veterinary Medicine. These opportunities include retrospective and prospective studies involving both small and large animal dermatology. Candidates appointed to the Tenure Track will be expected to develop and sustain an independent research program in veterinary dermatology. The College is strongly committed to faculty success and professional development and offers a formal mentoring program to support career growth and advancement. Service and engagement activities are also valued components of the position. Faculty are encouraged to participate in departmental, college, and university committees; contribute to professional organizations; provide continuing education programs; engage in community outreach; and support other activities that advance the missions of the Department and College. College and Department The Purdue University Veterinary Hospital recently completed a large expansion with the opening of the David and Bonnie Brunner Purdue Veterinary Medical Hospital Complex, a 162,500-square-foot facility. The new complex includes the Small Animal Hospital, which adds 65,000 square feet to the existing small animal facilities, as well as the Equine Hospital and the Farm Animal Hospital. These facilities provide exceptional resources for teaching, clinical service, and interdisciplinary research, enabling faculty to deliver outstanding patient care while educating the next generation of veterinary professionals. Commitment to the College and Departmental missions of learning, discovery, and engagement, and support of the College and Departmental strategic plans are essential. Applications Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Applicants should submit a letter of intent describing their professional goals and teaching philosophy, a current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information of three professional references through the application portal via the link provided: Current Purdue employees should apply through the employee application system: Equal Opportunity Purdue University is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access University. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Head-and-Professor-of-English/44308-en_US": {
      "title": "Head and Professor of English",
      "description": "Head and Professor of English Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44308 Job Title: Head and Professor of English City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The College of Liberal Arts at Purdue University invites applications for the position of Department Head, English. The college seeks a dynamic leader with creative vision and an outstanding record of research, teaching, and service as well as previous administrative leadership experience to fill this position. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Liberal Arts, the successful applicant will work alongside talented faculty, promote collaboration across disciplines, and play a crucial role in shaping the future of the college. Department of English Overview The Department offers the B.A., M.A., and Ph.D. degrees. Undergraduates may specialize in Literary Studies, Professional Writing, or Creative Writing. At the graduate level, the department offers an M.A. in English (open specialization) and a Ph.D. in Literature, Theory, Cultural Studies and in Rhetoric and Composition. Faculty are also involved in such interdisciplinary programs as the highly regarded Purdue OWL; African American Studies; American Studies; Comparative Literature; Linguistics; and Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies.  The department’s population includes thirty-four tenured or tenure-track faculty, ten lecturers, four clinical teaching professors, and twenty limited-term lecturers. Purdue University’s Department of English is committed to maintaining a welcoming and inclusive environment in all areas of faculty effort, including scholarship, instruction, and engagement. The department is home to a number of exciting and dynamic ventures in different disciplinary areas, including the CROW (Corpus & Repository of Writing) Lab; the COVE Collective; the Games, Narrative, and Esports Certificate; several grant-funded digital humanities projects; and community engagement projects, such as the Big Read and the Literary Awards Contest. The department is also home to two major scholarly journals: Modern Fiction Studies and Arthuriana, as well as the undergraduate arts journal The Bell Tower. College of Liberal Arts Overview This is an exciting time to join the leadership team in the College of Liberal Arts at Purdue University. As a vital component of a leading public research university, the college features a wide variety of excellent academic programs across the arts, humanities, and social sciences. We are committed to interdisciplinarity, innovation, and national leadership in higher education, most notably through our nationally recognized Cornerstone Integrated Liberal Arts program, which reaches more than 10,000 students per year across campus. _ Purdue offers substantial support for research and teaching at both the university and college levels. The college’s Office of Research advances scholarship across its fields through a portfolio of targeted programs designed to promote collaboration and research excellence. The college’s commitment to interdisciplinarity and innovation is apparent through its many faculty-led centers, labs, and initiatives.  The college and its faculty are deeply committed to teaching excellence and to the central role that liberal arts play in grounding a university curriculum. The deep integration of graduate and undergraduate students into research and experiential learning is among its major strengths. The college values intellectual rigor, open debate, and the exploration of diverse perspectives in the pursuit of knowledge. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Department / School Heads in the College of Liberal Arts serve as visionary academic leaders and chief advocates for their departments. They are responsible for driving strategic direction while ensuring operational excellence within their units. Primary responsibilities include academic leadership; managing the department’s budget; faculty and lecturer mentorship and career development; advancing undergraduate and graduate student success, which may include teaching at the graduate level; strategic resource management; and fostering external relations. Heads collaborate closely with the Dean and the college’s senior leadership team, partnering across departments to champion interdisciplinary initiatives and innovative problem-solving. Because Purdue is deeply invested in leadership development, Department Heads are supported by both the college and the Provost’s Office through programs such as the New Heads Forum and ongoing professional development opportunities. Required Qualifications Applicants must have: a terminal degree related to the research areas of the Department of English; a record of scholarly achievement suitable for appointment as a full professor at Purdue; demonstrated excellence in teaching and mentoring of students and faculty; evidence of effective academic leadership; experience with securing extramural funding; outstanding interpersonal and communication skills with dedication to building and maintaining strong relationships with alumni and other stakeholders; and evidence of successful leadership in promoting a culture of intellectual openness and respectful exchange of ideas across multiple perspectives of scholarship. _ Applications We encourage qualified candidates to submit application materials online at https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Head-and-Professor-of-English/44308-en_US/ , including a letter of application that describes qualifications for the position, curriculum vitae, names of three references, and statement of administrative / leadership philosophy. Review of applications will begin November 10, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Questions should be directed to Dr. Fritz Davis frdavis@purdue.edu.  A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University, the College of Liberal Arts, and the Department of English are committed to free and open inquiry in all matters. Candidates are encouraged to address in their cover letter how they are prepared to contribute to a climate that values free inquiry and academic freedom. EEO/AA Statement Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Biomedical-Robotics-Engineering-%28Indianapolis%29/44332-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Biomedical Robotics - Engineering (Indianapolis)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Biomedical Robotics - Engineering (Indianapolis) Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44332 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Biomedical Robotics - Engineering (Indianapolis) City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary Purdue University College of Engineering invites applications for multiple tenured/tenure track positions at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in biomedical-related robotics to strengthen its growing leadership at the intersection of robotics, engineering, and human health in our Indianapolis location. The candidate’s research focus should target areas where robotics, controls and autonomy impact the biomedical, medicine, and heath fields such as surgical robotics, active prostheses, self-driving labs for diagnostics, surgery and therapies, or rehabilitative systems. Tenured or tenure-track positions are expected to collaborate with an interdisciplinary group spanning Biomedical Engineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Industrial Engineering, and/or Mechanical Engineering with active degree programs based in Indianapolis. Successful candidates must hold a Ph.D. degree in Biomedical Engineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Industrial Engineering, Computer Science or a related discipline by the employment start date. Early-career applicants should show evidence of initiating independent research, while mid-career applicants should demonstrate a sustained record of independent research within academic or industrial organizations, and contributions to education and/or mentoring. The successful candidate will conduct original research, advise graduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate level courses, and perform service at the School, College, and University levels. The position would also enhance Purdue’s ability to attract major federal and industry-sponsored research, train students in a rapidly expanding field, and translate fundamental advances in robotics into technologies that address important biomedical and healthcare challenges. Applicants interested in a position in any of Purdue’s engineering schools are welcome to apply. College of Engineering Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 8 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering is a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit application to this site including (1) cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a 2-page teaching plan, (4) a 3-page research plan, and (5) names and contact information for at least 4 references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For information/questions regarding applications contact Academic Affairs, College of Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on November 5, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Electrical-and-Computer-Engineering-%28Indianapolis%29/44333-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Electrical and Computer Engineering (Indianapolis)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Electrical and Computer Engineering (Indianapolis) Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44333 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Electrical and Computer Engineering (Indianapolis) City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary Purdue has begun a major growth effort at our new location in Indianapolis—a dynamic, affordable city offering a vibrant urban lifestyle, rich cultural scene, and strong connections to industry and healthcare innovation. As part of this initiative, the Elmore Family School of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Purdue University invites applications for a tenure-track/tenured Assistant/Associate Professor to be based in Indianapolis . Purdue University seeks to attract exceptional candidates in Electrical and Computer Engineering. Particular areas of interest include Autonomy and Controls, Software Engineering and Systems, and Computer Vision , but exceptional candidates in other areas, especially those who have application interests in medicine and healthcare, are welcome. Successful candidates must hold a Ph.D. degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science , or a related discipline by the start of employment. Early-career applicants should show evidence of initiating independent research, while mid-career applicants should demonstrate a sustained record of independent research within academic or industrial organizations, and contributions to education and/or mentoring. The successful candidate will conduct original research, advise graduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses, and perform service at the School, College, and University levels. School and College The Elmore Family School of Electrical and Computer Engineering is the largest academic unit at Purdue University and one of the largest in the nation with more than 130 faculty members (7 NAE members, more than 40 Fellows in multiple societies), 2,500 undergraduate students (sophomores-seniors), and 1,700 graduate students. In Indianapolis, ECE is home to the Transportation and Autonomous Systems Institute (TASI) which collaborates closely with industry partners in developing and testing cutting-edge vehicle autonomy systems, as well as the newly-launched Intelligent Software & Systems Center , which is re-envisioning the software lifecycle in the age of agentic AI and the impact on AI-native systems. These institutions will provide a strong foundation to new faculty joining in Indianapolis. ECE’s undergraduate programs in Electrical Engineering and Computer Engineering are ranked 10th and 9th, respectively. Its graduate programs are ranked 8th and 9th. And its online MS in ECE is ranked 1st in the nation. Faculty in ECE collaborate closely with industry. The Purdue West Lafayette–Indianapolis Hard Tech Corridor is strategically established to drive transformative industry engagement across a 60-mile innovation corridor, unified by a seamlessly integrated campus that serves as a catalyst for economic growth, technological advancement, and global leadership in hard tech development. The School is an integral part of Purdue Engineering. Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 8 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering is a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit application to this site including (1) a cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a 2-page teaching plan, (4) a 3-page research plan, and (5) names and contact information for at least 4 references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For information/questions regarding applications, contact Academic Affairs, College of Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on 11/5/2026 and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssociateFull-Professor-of-Engineering-Practice-in-Industrial-Engineering-%28Indianapolis%29/44371-en_US": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor of Engineering Practice in Industrial Engineering (Indianapolis)",
      "description": "Associate/Full Professor of Engineering Practice in Industrial Engineering (Indianapolis) Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44371 Job Title: Associate/Full Professor of Engineering Practice in Industrial Engineering (Indianapolis) City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The Edwardson School of Industrial Engineering at Purdue University invites applications for a Professor of Engineering Practice at the Associate or Full rank. This position is based at the Purdue Indianapolis location. Purdue University in Indianapolis seeks to attract exceptional candidates with teaching and educational interests and expertise in all areas of Industrial Engineering, including Production and Supply Networks, Operations Research, Manufacturing, and Human Factors. The successful candidate will teach core undergraduate courses across Industrial Engineering and assist with development of strategic initiatives at Purdue University in Indianapolis. Candidates must hold a Ph.D., or M.S. with more than five years of professional experience, in Industrial Engineering, Operations Research, Human Factors, Manufacturing, Systems Engineering or a related field by the employment start date. Ideal candidates will have relevant industry experience with demonstrable evidence of leadership. In addition to instructional duties, the successful candidate will work effectively with industry partners and faculty, provide mentoring to students and other program support staff, and perform service both at the School and the University levels as needed. They will have demonstrated skills in innovative pedagogical techniques, project/problem-based learning, and industry applications of current methodologies. School and College New faculty members will become part of a vibrant community of scholars who are committed to Rethinking IE and helping to guide the profession to impact societal grand challenges of the 21st century. The Edwardson School of Industrial Engineering at Purdue University is making significant investments in advancing the frontiers of next generation information engineering and data analytics, systems science, cognition and decision-making, and manufacturing of products and services. The Edwardson School of Industrial Engineering at Purdue University is ranked 1st in online MS programs, 2nd in undergraduate programs, and 4th in graduate programs according to the latest USNWR rankings. The School is an integral part of Purdue’s College of Engineering. Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 8 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering is a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit application to this site including (1) cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a teaching statement (no more than two pages) and a sample proposed course syllabus, and (4) names and contact information for at least three references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For information/questions regarding applications, contact the Office of Academic Affairs, College of Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on November 5, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled.  A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
