    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor%2C-Artificial-Intelligence-for-AgricultureForestryNatural-Systems/44262-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Artificial Intelligence for Agriculture/Forestry/Natural Systems",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Artificial Intelligence for Agriculture/Forestry/Natural Systems Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44262 Job Title: Assistant Professor, Artificial Intelligence for Agriculture/Forestry/Natural Systems City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Purdue University College of Agriculture seeks applicants for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position. This is a full-time (9-months) position with an appointment in research and teaching. The candidate for this position could have a home department in Agronomy, Agricultural & Biological Engineering and/or Forestry & Natural Resources. Within the context of natural, forestry, and/or cropping systems, we are looking for candidates with experience and potential integration of two or more of the following topic areas: •    artificial intelligence (AI) including machine learning (ML), deep learning, knowledge-guided AI, and/or translational applied AI models •    digital agriculture including crop modeling and/or digital twins of assorted scales •    remote-, proximal- and near-proximal- sensing, and/or Internet of Things (IoT) •    data science, geo-spatial analysis, GeoAI, and/or integration of data pipelines •    agroecosystem (crop-soil-environmental) and/or ecosystem modeling •    applications of robotics and/or autonomous systems Applications of the work could relate to productivity improvement, resource optimization, systems efficiency, and/or operational strategies and logistics. We expect the candidate to build a nationally and internationally recognized research program that advances discovery and innovation across these areas at the intersection of agricultural, environmental, and data sciences. Demonstrated experience and interest in working with multi-disciplinary teams is beneficial. The selected candidate will develop and teach undergraduate and/or graduate level courses. Course modality is generally in person. The potential may exist for teaching online/distance courses during the academic year. The College The College of Agriculture is one of the world’s leading colleges of agricultural, food, life, and natural resource sciences. The College is ranked third in the U.S. and sixth in the world in the 2026 QS World University Rankings. The College is deeply committed to the three land-grant missions (teaching, research, and extension), to international activities and perspectives that span all missions, and to excellence in all we do. The College has 10 academic departments, 294 faculty, 2842 undergraduate students, and 694 graduate students. Qualifications Applicants must possess a Ph.D. degree in forestry and natural resources, agronomy, soil science, agricultural and biological engineering, or a related discipline at the start of appointment. A record of research excellence and productivity commensurate with rank is required as well as demonstrated record or potential of interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship. Applicants must have demonstrated commitment to teaching and student mentorship. Ideal qualifications would include cross-discipline training among degrees earned with at least one degree in an agricultural or natural resources field. Application Process Interested applicants must submit a cover letter, CV, research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should be submitted at: https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor%2C-Artificial-Intelligence-for-AgricultureForestryNatural-Systems/44262-en_US/ . Application materials must be combined into a single pdf and submitted electronically in the CV field on the application site. Contact Ignacio Ciampitti ( iciampit@purdue.edu ) if questions. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/4/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-of-Basic-Medical-Sciences-One-Health/44286-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Basic Medical Sciences - One Health",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Basic Medical Sciences - One Health Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44286 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Basic Medical Sciences - One Health City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary As part of Purdue University’s strategic investment in One Health – Intelligent Medicines , the Department of Basic Medical Sciences in the College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. We seek innovative scientists whose research addresses fundamental mechanisms of cancer and disease at the intersection of tumor biology, neuroscience, immunology, regenerative biology, and the skeletal system. We welcome investigators who leverage comparative , translational , and cross-species approaches to understand how interactions among tumors, neural circuits, immune cells, stem cell niches, and tissue microenvironments influence disease initiation, progression, metastasis, and therapeutic response. Leveraging Purdue's strengths in comparative medicine and naturally occurring disease models, successful candidates will have unique opportunities to pursue translational discovery across species and advance One Health solutions relevant to both animal and human health. Candidates may utilize naturally occurring disease in veterinary patients, experimental model systems, organoids, or emerging computational and AI-enabled approaches to address questions relevant to both animal and human health. Areas of Research Interest We welcome candidates pursuing innovative research in: Cancer Neuroscience and Tumor-Neural Interactions: Neural regulation of cancer initiation, progression, metastasis, treatment response, and cancer-associated symptoms. Bone Metastasis and Skeletal Tumor Biology: Mechanisms governing tumor-bone interactions, metastatic colonization, dormancy, and skeletal remodeling. Neuro-Immune and Bone-Immune Crosstalk: Interactions among neural, immune, and skeletal systems that shape tumor progression and anti-tumor responses. Innovative Models and Technologies: Comparative animal models, organoids, spatial and single-cell biology, advanced imaging, computational approaches, AI/ML, and other emerging technologies for studying complex biological systems. Purdue’s One Health Initiative This strategic recruitment will help advance Purdue’s One Health Initiative which seeks to tackle complex challenges with real-world impact at the intersection of human, animal, and plant health. This recruitment initiative builds on previous strategic faculty recruitment initiatives in: (1) Integrated Health; (2) AI-Driven Biomolecular Design, and (3) Advanced Chemistry. In addition, a parallel strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Healthy and Resilient Living Systems is ongoing. Through academic programs, research, facility infrastructure and industry partnerships, Purdue is making giant leaps in improving health outcomes for all living things and driving economic growth regionally and globally. This strategic faculty recruitment initiative focused on Intelligent Medicines is expected to build on prior recruitment initiatives and existing Purdue research and academic strengths, to transform research and impact human, animal and environmental health by bridging silos and fostering collaboration across disciplines. The Intelligent Medicines theme seeks to create a framework that improves human, animal, and environmental health through the integration of technology, data, and systems thinking. This faculty recruitment initiative is disease agnostic and aims to establish new capabilities in AI-enabled therapeutic development, non-animal models of disease, advanced manufacturing, intelligent health systems, digital twins, robotics, human factors, supply chain resilience, and health technology innovation. By combining strengths in device innovation, computational intelligence, manufacturing systems, and healthcare operations, Purdue intends to create a highly visible flagship that strengthens industry engagement, expands workforce development opportunities, and attracts significant external funding. Qualifications A Ph.D. in a biological science and a minimum of 2 years relevant post-doctoral experience. A record of research excellence and productivity commensurate with rank. Demonstrated potential or record of interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship. Commitment to teaching and student mentorship. Faculty Responsibilities Establish a vigorous, externally funded research program. Teach courses in undergraduate or professional programs, mentor students, and train graduate students and postdoctoral fellows. Engage in service to the Department, College, and University. Collaborate across disciplines to solve complex global one health challenges. Integration within the Purdue One Health Community Collectively, the strategic faculty recruitment initiatives represent a forward-thinking investment in Purdue’s research infrastructure and academic excellence. Faculty hired as part of these One Health strategic faculty recruitment initiatives will be supported as part of the overall One Health community. Together, these faculty members are expected to work across diverse disciplines, enhance Purdue’s external funding potential, and drive innovation at the intersection of health, environment, food, and economics. In addition to joining an academic unit, faculty hired under this initiative will have the opportunity to join a vibrant ecosystem of interdisciplinary centers and institutes, that span the hard tech corridor between Indianapolis and West Lafayette including: Center for Health Analytics and Therapeutic Intelligence Purdue Institute for Cancer Research (PICR) Purdue Center for Musculoskeletal Engineering (PCME) The integrated, cross-disciplinary nature of One Health is essential for addressing today’s most urgent health challenges and ensuring Purdue’s continued leadership in research, education, and community impact. Application Process To apply, please submit a cover letter, complete curriculum vitae, 2–3 page description of current and future research, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin on November 2, 2026 and continue until positions are filled. Applications should be submitted at: https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Basic-Medical-Sciences-One-Health/44286-en_US/ . A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/2/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Basic-Medical-Sciences/44079-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Basic Medical Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Basic Medical Sciences Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44079 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Basic Medical Sciences City: West Lafayette or Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Basic Medical Sciences within the Purdue University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a full-time, academic year, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain an extramurally-funded research program in an area consistent with current departmental strengths such as cancer biology, musculoskeletal biology, and neuroscience. In addition to the department and the college, this position offers unique opportunities for collaboration through the Purdue Health and Life Sciences cluster within Purdue’s Discovery Park and the Purdue One Health Initiative . Purdue University spans the hard tech corridor between West Lafayette and Indianapolis, offering a variety of locations for living, research, and teaching. Applicants must possess a Ph.D. in biology or related field and have demonstrated excellence in research. Candidates who also possess an additional medical degree ( e.g., D.V.M., V.M.D., or M.D.) are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain an energetic research program, participate in graduate student training, and teach at the undergraduate, graduate, and/or professional veterinary levels. Application materials should include a letter of intent, a complete CV, a 2-3 page description of current and future research goals, a 1-2 page description of mentoring/teaching philosophy and experience, and the names and contact information for three references. We encourage applicants to apply here: https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Basic-Medical-Sciences/44079-en_US/ . Review of applications will begin November 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. The starting date for the position is negotiable. A background check is required for employment in this position. For questions regarding applications contact Makayla Espinosa ( msespino@purdue.edu ). The College of Veterinary Medicine at Purdue University values, nurtures, and respects all members of its community and ensures an environment of excellence where all students, faculty, and staff are inspired and empowered to achieve their full potential. Purdue University has a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/2/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Head%2C-Hospitality-and-Tourism-Management-%28White-Lodging-J_W_-Marriott%2C-Jr_-School%29/44114-en_US": {
      "title": "Head, Hospitality and Tourism Management (White Lodging-J.W. Marriott, Jr. School)",
      "description": "Head, Hospitality and Tourism Management (White Lodging-J.W. Marriott, Jr. School) Job Details | Purdue University Head, Hospitality and Tourism Management (White Lodging-J.W. Marriott, Jr. School) By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44114 Job Title: Head, Hospitality and Tourism Management (White Lodging-J.W. Marriott, Jr. School) City: West Lafayette Job Description: JOB SUMMARY White Lodging Services Head White Lodging-J.W. Marriott, Jr. School of Hospitality and Tourism Management The White Lodging-J.W. Marriott, Jr. School of Hospitality and Tourism Management invites applications and nominations for the position of the White Lodging Services Head of the White Lodging-J.W. Marriott, Jr. School of Hospitality and Tourism Management (HTM), College of Health and Human Sciences, Purdue University. Purdue University seeks an accomplished, dynamic, energetic, and visionary leader who fosters innovation and collaboration in a shared governance environment. With roots dating back to 1887, the White Lodging-J.W. Marriott, Jr. School of Hospitality and Tourism Management (The School), is one of the nation’s oldest and most respected hospitality management programs. In 2021, the School was named in honor of White Lodging’s founder and CEO, Bruce White, and his family for their longstanding financial and in-kind support of Purdue University. The School’s name also honors the career and contributions of J.W. “Bill” Marriott, Jr., executive chairman and chairman of the board of Marriott International. Home to world-class faculty, the School is currently ranked seventh in the world and third in the nation for Hospitality and Tourism Management in the Global Ranking of Academic Subjects published by the Academic Ranking of World Universities (ARWU), known as the Shanghai Ranking. OPPORTUNITY The School is one of only seven named units at the University, with generous support from the White Family. The School is also one of the first departments to add undergraduate programs at the new Purdue University in Indianapolis location, a part of the Purdue flagship campus. The unique blend of flagship and urban campuses allows the School to expand student and faculty opportunities as well as extend its brand into a top 20 US city that is a key Midwest business hub. POSITION SUMMARY AND RESPONSIBILITIES The White Lodging Services Head (Head) is part of the college's leadership team and is responsible for overseeing all aspects of school operations at both the West Lafayette and Indianapolis campus locations, including faculty/staff development, alumni relations, and advocacy for the School to the College, University, and larger community. The Head will be an internationally recognized academic scholar, providing leadership and vision, while facilitating excellence in research, teaching, and engagement activities in the School. We seek a leader with a strong record of excellence in the academy and enthusiasm to grow the School’s academic and research programs, with an additional focus on advancing program reputation and opportunity at the Indianapolis location. The next Head will have a history of accomplishment in strong educational programming, research productivity, and an excellent record of service. The successful candidate will be responsible for managing all aspects of the School’s programs, including education, program accreditation, faculty recruitment and retention, engagement, and development of educational and relevant research programs. The Head will work closely with the Dean and faculty to strengthen and expand interdisciplinary educational programs to support the academic missions of the University and be committed to nurturing programs and School faculty activity. The Head will have dedicated time for administrative, educational, strategic, and research initiatives. ADDITIONAL RESPONSIBILITIES EDUCATION The Head supports and oversees the delivery of comprehensive and state-of-the-art educational programs and ensures compliance with accrediting organizations and promotes the delivery of a curriculum and learning environment designed to produce graduates of the highest caliber. The Head enhances the graduate programs of the School and makes necessary changes to ensure excellence of graduate training and research in the School. TALENT DEVELOPMENT The Head assures that key leadership roles within the School are filled by a group of dedicated and talented faculty and staff who are mentored and supported to deliver excellent educational programs, cutting-edge research, and professional development. The Head should recognize the nuances of Hospitality and Tourism Management, actively recruiting and working to motivate and retain top-quality faculty and program leaders so that the School has the talent to carry out strategic plans. RESEARCH ADVANCEMENT The Head supports the pursuit and advancement of world-class research by assisting principal investigators and other faculty in efforts to secure grant funding. The Head fosters growth in interdisciplinary research activities beyond the School. FISCAL OVERSIGHT AND COMPLIANCE The Head leads the financing and budgeting processes for the School, taking divergent views on financial decisions into consideration while effectively managing and leveraging allocated resources. The Head ensures that applicable policy, procedures, regulations, and laws are followed. PHILANTHROPY AND ALUMNI RELATIONS Working with University leaders and building upon a future for the School that is as illustrious as its past will require continued fundraising activities. The Head will work with fellow institutional leaders to facilitate advancement programs and present the School's case for major financial support to potential donors. The Head also helps lead alumni relations engagement programs focused on increasing the depth and scope of the relationships within the School and on behalf of the University. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS The preferred candidate will have scholarly credentials commensurate with the rank of Full Professor (clinical or tenure track), including an earned Doctorate in HTM or related consumer-focused disciplines from an accredited school or program. Regardless of academic specialty, candidates should have a strong understanding of and appreciation for hospitality and tourism management issues and concerns. Desirable attributes include a strong record of published research, external funding, and industry partnerships; prior experience in academic administration and undergraduate and graduate education; excellent communication skills; commitment to teaching ; , and the development and advancement of individual faculty, staff, students, and the School as a whole. This position is a full-time, 12-month, position. ADDITIONAL PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Demonstrated record of successful academic leadership and administration in higher education, supported by strong academic and research accomplishments, with demonstrated success in strategic planning, fiscal management, resource development, and advancing the strategic priorities of an academic unit. Demonstrated commitment to fostering a culture of excellence and success for faculty, staff, and students, with a record of recruiting, retaining, mentoring, and developing outstanding faculty and staff; building effective teams; and advancing student-centered education and student success through active engagement in student programs, initiatives, and learning experiences. Strategic national academic and research leader, grounded in personal integrity with the ability to energize, inspire, and encourage faculty and student innovation as well as interdisciplinary collaboration. Demonstrated ability to lead and manage a complex academic organization while building and sustaining productive, mutually beneficial partnerships across campus and with industry, professional organizations, community stakeholders, and other external constituencies. Demonstrated ability to motivate key constituencies; lead the development of mutually beneficial relationships with partners; and recruit, retain, and develop superb academic faculty and leaders. ABOUT THE SCHOOL – WHITE LODGING-J.W. MARRIOTT, JR. SCHOOL OF HOSPITALITY AND TOURISM MANAGEMENT Reimagined in 2019 by the Purdue University Board of Trustees, the White Lodging-J.W. Marriott, Jr. School of Hospitality and Tourism Management hosts a complex mix of specialties, including the world-renowned hospitality and tourism management; a global leader in hospitality management education; financial counseling and planning ; and selling and sales management programs. The School is home to a collegial and diverse staff of 22 tenured/tenure track and clinical faculty, 19 lecturers and staff, and 750 undergraduate and graduate students. Beyond an academic curriculum that fuses theory and practice, HTM prepares its students to be citizens of the world. The Head will provide visionary leadership to guide the School through fundamental global shifts in HTM, while leveraging top-ranked programs in financial counseling and planning, and selling and sales management. ABOUT THE COLLEGE OF HEALTH AND HUMAN SCIENCES The College of Health and Human Sciences (HHS) is the fourth-largest College at Purdue. It includes nine academic units that hold national and international recognition for their fundamental scientific and programmatic contributions to improving individuals and communities' health. The College strives to elevate Purdue's reputation in the health and human sciences by positioning the University to meet the health and wellness challenges facing the population, growing and creating opportunities for Indiana and the global economy, and enhancing student learning for success in a rapidly changing world. HHS's multidisciplinary learning environment uniquely prepares students to contribute to improved human health and behavior and to serve as leaders in their disciplines. The College also provides a rich environment for world-changing research and discovery. Purdue's land-grant mission facilitates the translation of these discoveries from theory to application, benefiting not only those in Indiana, but society as a whole. ABOUT PURDUE UNIVERSITY Purdue University is a globally recognized research institution demonstrating excellence at scale. Ranked among top 10 public universities and with two colleges in the top four in the United States, Purdue discovers and disseminates knowledge with a quality and at a scale second to none. With a proven reputation of excellence in science, technology, engineering, health, agriculture, management, liberal arts and more, Purdue consistently earns top spots in national and global rankings. Committed to affordability and accessibility, Purdue’s main campus has frozen tuition 14 years in a row. Purdue never stops in the persistent pursuit of the next giant leap, including its first comprehensive urban campus in Indianapolis; the Mitch Daniels School of Business; Purdue Computes; and the One Health initiative. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Applications and nominations will be accepted until the position is filled. Review of applications will begin November 2, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Inquiries/questions may be directed to Dr. Laura Murray-Kolb ( lmurrayk@purdue.edu ), Chair of the Search Committee. A background check is required for this position. Career Stream Faculty 6 Equal Opportunity Employer Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/1/26 Search Jobs Job Alerts Link Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Statistics-in-Sports-Analytics%2C-Indianapolis/44123-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Statistics in Sports Analytics, Indianapolis",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Statistics in Sports Analytics, Indianapolis Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44123 Job Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Statistics in Sports Analytics, Indianapolis City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The College of Science at Purdue University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Sports Analytics at the assistant or associate professor level, based at Purdue’s Indianapolis campus. The position will be housed in the Department of Statistics and is intended to strengthen research and teaching at the intersection of statistical science, data science, and sports analytics. This position is part of an initiative to expand the Department of Statistics’ presence at the Indianapolis campus, including the recruitment of additional instructional faculty to support and advance the department’s teaching mission. Purdue University in Indianapolis is a new, fully integrated expansion of the West Lafayette campus, extending to central Indiana the academic rigor and accessible excellence for which Purdue is known. As the state’s only public top-10 university, most trusted university, and most innovative university, Purdue is focused on strengthening its presence in Indiana’s industrial and technological center. Purdue in Indianapolis is creating an innovative, STEM-based collegiate experience by connecting future-ready students and faculty with local businesses to accelerate Indiana’s STEM pipeline and technology ecosystem, fueling impact for our region and the world. Learn more about Purdue’s latest giant leap at: https://www.purdue.edu/campuses/indianapolis/ . Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in statistics, biostatistics, sports analytics, or a closely related field by August 16, 2027 and have demonstrated excellence in research and a strong commitment to teaching. Outstanding applicants whose research is grounded in statistical science and motivated by sports or human-performance applications will be considered. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, statistical learning and machine learning, Bayesian methods, causal inference, functional data analysis, longitudinal and spatiotemporal data analysis, high-dimensional data, statistical computing, and other modern methods for complex sports data. Candidates should demonstrate the potential to contribute to core areas of statistics while developing impactful applications in sports analytics. Principal Duties Successful candidates will be expected to develop an independent research program in statistical science with strong connections to sports analytics, teach undergraduate and graduate courses in statistics and sports analytics, develop an external funding portfolio, build interdisciplinary connections with researchers and partners in sports and related data-intensive fields, and participate in department, college, and broader university activities. The Department and College Purdue’s Department of Statistics is consistently recognized as one of the top statistics programs in the country. The department advances statistical sciences and data science in both theory and applications, with strengths spanning statistical methodology, computation, machine learning, and interdisciplinary data science. The Sports Analytics position will add a distinctive application area in which modern statistical methods can be developed, evaluated, and translated to complex real-world data. The department also plays a central role in Purdue’s statistical science education and connects with broader data-intensive initiatives across the university. The Department of Statistics is part of the College of Science, which encompasses the mathematical, computational, physical, and life sciences at Purdue. The College is the second-largest at Purdue with over 350 faculty members and more than 7,000 students. The College is pursuing significant new initiatives that align with campus-wide plans. Opportunities for collaboration span statistics, mathematics, computer science, data science, the physical and life sciences, the newly reimagined School of Business, and Purdue’s growing campus presence in the center of Indianapolis. For more information about Purdue’s Department of Statistics, see https://www.stat.purdue.edu/ . Application Procedure Applications should be submitted online through https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/PurdueStatistics/PSSA , and should include (1) a cover letter, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a research statement, (4) a teaching statement, and (5) four letters of recommendation, one of which should address the candidate’s teaching qualifications. Reference letter writers should submit their letters online through www.mathjobs.org . Inquiries may be directed to Dr. Kiseop Lee at kiseop@purdue.edu. Applications will be considered on a continuing basis, but candidates are encouraged to apply by Nov 6, 2026 for full consideration. A background check will be required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/29/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-of-Engineering-Practice-in-Engineering-Education/44197-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Engineering Practice in Engineering Education",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Engineering Practice in Engineering Education Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44197 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Engineering Practice in Engineering Education City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The School of Engineering Education at Purdue University invites applications for a full-time Professor of Engineering Practice (PEP) position at the Assistant or Associate level starting in Fall 2027. We seek an accomplished individual to help develop and grow our undergraduate degree programs in Multidisciplinary Engineering and Interdisciplinary Engineering Studies (MDE/IDES) and graduate programs in Engineering Education (certificate, MSENE, and PhD). The successful candidate will have unique opportunities to lead and support initiatives that are synergistic with our full range of academic programs and aligned with one or more focus areas, such as engineering design and design studies, the scholarship of teaching and learning (SoTL), relating engineering education research to practice, and AI and STEM education. Consideration will also be given to how a candidate’s background and interests align with key MDE/IDES concentration and growth areas, such as systems engineering, complex product design and prototyping, technical program management, AI and digital tools in engineering practice, etc. Professors of Engineering Practice bridge academia and other sectors by integrating real-world engineering practices and applied research into the classroom, fostering strategic industry and community partnerships, and driving practice-informed educational innovation. Candidates must hold a doctorate in engineering education or another relevant field, including but not limited to Biomedical, Mechanical, Electrical or Chemical Engineering, by the employment start date and have demonstrated independence in their profession. Candidates who have at least five years of experience in higher education and at least one other sector, such as an engineering industry, non-profit, or government, are particularly encouraged to apply. In addition to instructional and administrative duties, the successful candidate will work effectively with industry partners and faculty, mentor and advise students in our MSENE and graduate certificate programs, and perform service at the School and University levels as needed. The successful candidate may also have demonstrated skills in innovative pedagogical techniques, project/problem-based learning, online/remote learning, or program administration and leadership. This position is based in West Lafayette, and it is expected that the faculty member will teach and contribute to both of Purdue’s two main campus locations in West Lafayette and Indianapolis, IN. School and College Established in 2004, the School of Engineering Education is recognized as the first department of its type and a global leader. Our mission is to transform engineering education and the engineering profession in the state of Indiana, the nation, and the world based on foundational and translational research. To learn more, visit: https://engineering.purdue.edu/ENE . The School of Engineering Education is an integral part of Purdue Engineering. Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 9 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering continues to remain a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit an application to this site including: (1) a cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a 2-page teaching plan, (4) a 2-page engagement/outreach plan, and (5) names and contact information for at least 3 references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For information/questions regarding applications, please contact Engineering Academic Affairs, Purdue Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 29, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/28/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Department-HeadProfessor-of-Communication/44256-en_US": {
      "title": "Department Head/Professor of Communication",
      "description": "Department Head/Professor of Communication Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44256 Job Title: Department Head/Professor of Communication City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The College of Liberal Arts at Purdue University invites applications for the position of Department Head, Brian Lamb School of Communication. The college seeks a dynamic leader with creative vision and an outstanding record of research, teaching, and service as well as previous administrative leadership experience to fill this position. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Liberal Arts, the successful applicant will work alongside talented faculty, promote collaboration across disciplines, and play a crucial role in shaping the future of the college. Brian Lamb School of Communication Overview The Brian Lamb School of Communication is part of Purdue University’s College of Liberal Arts and is home to the largest undergraduate population within the College’s nine departments. The Lamb School consists of six interdependent units that focus on a broad array of human communication: health and risk communication; interpersonal communication; organizational communication; media, technology, and society; public relations; and political communication. The School has 43 full-time faculty and lecturers and more than 30 part-time instructors. Its top-ranked graduate program includes 30 funded students at both the Master’s and PhD levels. Additionally, the Lamb School has a highly regarded online Master’s program that regularly enrolls more than 100 graduate students. The Lamb School also reaches far beyond the confines of the college and university. Its Center for C-SPAN Scholarship and Engagement (CCSE) is an interdisciplinary hub that works toward increased utilization of the C-SPAN Video Library and supports initiatives that foster academic research, experiential learning, and community engagement. The Lamb School is home to the Digital Media Production Center (DMPC), which provides opportunities to learn about and use digital media for presentations, interviewing, and reporting. More information about the Brian Lamb School of Communication is available at: www.cla.purdue.edu/communication . College of Liberal Arts Overview This is an exciting time to join the leadership team in the College of Liberal Arts at Purdue University. As a vital component of a leading public research university, the college features a wide variety of excellent academic programs across the arts, humanities, and social sciences. We are committed to interdisciplinarity, innovation, and national leadership in higher education, most notably through our nationally recognized Cornerstone Integrated Liberal Arts program, which reaches more than 10,000 students per year across campus. Purdue offers substantial support for research and teaching at both the university and college levels. The college’s Office of Research advances scholarship across its fields through a portfolio of targeted programs designed to promote collaboration and research excellence. The college’s commitment to interdisciplinarity and innovation is apparent through its many faculty-led centers, labs, and initiatives.  The college and its faculty are deeply committed to teaching excellence, and to the central role that liberal arts play in grounding a university curriculum. The deep integration of graduate and undergraduate students into research and experiential learning are among its major strengths. The college values intellectual rigor, open debate, and the exploration of diverse perspectives in the pursuit of knowledge. Position Details Essential Duties and Responsibilities Department / School Heads in the College of Liberal Arts serve as visionary academic leaders and chief advocates for their departments. They are responsible for driving strategic direction while ensuring operational excellence within their units. Primary responsibilities include academic leadership; managing the department’s budget; faculty and lecturer mentorship and career development; advancing undergraduate and graduate student success which may include teaching at the graduate level; strategic resource management; and fostering external relations. Heads collaborate closely with the Dean and the college’s senior leadership team, partnering across departments to champion interdisciplinary initiatives and innovative problem-solving. Because Purdue is deeply invested in leadership development, Department Heads are supported by both the college and the provost’s office through programs such as the New Heads Forum and ongoing professional development opportunities. Required Qualifications Applicants must have: a terminal degree related to the research areas of the Brian Lamb School of Communication; a record of scholarly achievement suitable for appointment as a full professor at Purdue; demonstrated excellence in teaching and mentoring of students and faculty; evidence of effective academic leadership; experience with securing extramural funding; outstanding interpersonal and communication skills with dedication to building and maintaining strong relationships with alumni and other stakeholders; and evidence of successful leadership in promoting a culture of intellectual openness and respectful exchange of ideas across multiple perspectives of scholarship. Applications We encourage qualified candidates to submit application materials online at https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Department-HeadProfessor-of-Communication/44256-en_US/ , including a letter of application that describes qualifications for the position, curriculum vitae, names of three references, and statement of administrative / leadership philosophy. Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Questions should be directed to Search Chair, Melissa Remis at remis@purdue.edu. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University, the College of Liberal Arts, and the Brian Lamb School of Communication are committed to free and open inquiry in all matters. Candidates are encouraged to address in their cover letter how they are prepared to contribute to a climate that values free inquiry and academic freedom. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/28/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Chemistry/44120-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44120 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Chemistry City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Chemistry in the College of Science at Purdue University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in Theoretical Quantum Information, Algorithms and Materials, or related areas. Successful candidates may have interests in developing quantum algorithms and quantum information theory, and applying such algorithms to chemically relevant processes and materials. Qualifications Candidates must have a PhD in chemistry, physics, or a related field by the start of the appointment, with outstanding research credentials, an excellent publication record, and a strong commitment to teaching excellence.  Successful candidates are expected to develop a vibrant research program supported by extramural funding and teach at the graduate and undergraduate levels. The Department and College With over 50 full-time faculty, more than 380 PhD students, and over 500 outstanding undergraduates, Purdue’s highly ranked chemistry department is one of the largest and most diverse in the country. The wide-ranging expertise of the faculty enables fast and effective responses to interdisciplinary research opportunities, positioning it as a key partner in many university-wide centers, institutes, and initiatives. For more information, see http://www.chem.purdue.edu/ . Chemistry is part of the College of Science, which comprises the physical, computing and life sciences at Purdue. It is the second-largest college at Purdue with over 350 faculty and more than 6000 students. With multiple commitments of significant investment and strong alignment with Purdue leadership, the College is committed to supporting existing strengths and enhancing the scope and impact of the Department of Chemistry. Purdue itself is one of the nation’s leading land-grant universities, with an enrollment of over 41,000 students primarily focused on STEM subjects.  For more information, see https://www.purdue.edu/purduemoves/initiatives/stem/index.php . Application Procedure Applicants should apply electronically at https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Chemistry/44120-en_US/?st=54ED85CB7B670357B5C37A09C1881128990B4E26 that includes (1) a complete curriculum vitae, (2) a teaching plan, and (3) a research plan. Lastly, applicants should arrange for three letters of reference to be e-mailed to the Search Chair at pchemsearch@purdue.edu , specifically indicating the position for which the applicant is applying. Applications will be held in strict confidence and will be reviewed beginning October 26, 2026. Applications will remain in consideration until the position is filled. A background check will be required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/28/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor/44250-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44250 Job Title: Assistant Professor City: West Lafayette Job Description: Strategic Faculty Recruitment Initiative in One Health Healthy and Resilient Living Systems - College of Agriculture, Plant Sciences Position Summary As part of a transformative, university-wide initiative in One Health – Healthy and Resilient Living Systems, the College of Agriculture invites applications for an academic year tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level. Specifically, the College seeks to recruit a basic plant biologist whose discovery-driven research advances fundamental understanding of plant biology and biochemistry at one or more biological scales – from genes and molecules to cells, organisms, populations, communities, or ecosystems. Successful candidates will be practiced in leveraging current and emerging artificial intelligence-enabled approaches to accelerate scientific discovery and advance our understanding of healthy and resilient living systems. We seek a researcher with interests that encompass two or more aspects of plant biology. Topics representing possible synergistic opportunities include molecular and cellular biology, plant biochemistry and natural product formation, developmental biology, physiology, genetics and genomics, evolution, plant–microbe and plant–insect interactions, plant–environment interactions, ecology, and ecosystem science. Candidates are encouraged to integrate artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning, foundation models, computational modeling, autonomous experimentation, and other data-driven approaches to analyze complex biological data, generate and test hypotheses, reveal biological mechanisms, and predict biological responses across scales. Building on Purdue’s strengths in agriculture, engineering, artificial intelligence, data science, and health sciences, successful candidates will help establish a globally distinctive platform for AI-enabled discovery, prediction, and understanding of living systems. We particularly seek scientists whose research expands the frontiers of knowledge in plant biology, preferentially by spanning biological scales and disciplines, while contributing to Purdue’s leadership in One Health and healthy and resilient living systems. Purdue's One Health Initiative This strategic recruitment will help advance Purdue’s One Health initiative ( https://www.purdue.edu/onehealth/ ) which seeks to tackle complex challenges with real-world impact at the intersection of human, animal, and plant health. This recruitment initiative builds on previous strategic faculty recruitment initiatives in: (1) Integrated Health; (2) AI-Driven Biomolecular Design, and (3) Advanced Chemistry. In addition, a parallel strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Intelligent Medicines is ongoing. Through academic programs, research, facility infrastructure and industry partnerships, Purdue’s One Health efforts are making giant leaps in improving health outcomes for all living things and driving economic growth regionally and globally.  This strategic faculty recruitment initiative focused on Healthy and Resilient Living Systems is expected to build on prior recruitment initiatives and existing Purdue research and academic strengths, to transform research and impact human, animal and environmental health by bridging silos and fostering collaboration across disciplines. The health and prosperity of society depend upon resilient living systems that connect ecosystems, plants, animals, insects, microbes, and people. Emerging and chronic diseases, food insecurity, environmental degradation, climate change, nutrient deficiencies, invasive species, and ecosystem disruption are increasingly interconnected global challenges that require integrated approaches across biological scales and disciplinary boundaries. This strategic recruitment initiative will help establish Purdue as a national leader in predicting, designing, and improving living systems that support health, sustainability, and economic vitality. Working with existing campus experts, this cluster would develop innovative solutions that enhance health resilience from genes and microbiomes to organisms, food systems, populations, and ecosystems. By integrating strengths in agriculture, engineering, artificial intelligence, data science, and health sciences, Purdue aims to create a globally distinctive platform for addressing complex challenges at the intersection of food systems, environmental stewardship, animal and human health, and economic prosperity. The College Purdue University’s College of Agriculture is one of the world’s leading colleges of agricultural, food, life, and natural resource sciences. The College is ranked third in the U.S. and sixth in the world in the 2026 QS World University Rankings. The College is deeply committed to the three land-grant missions (teaching, research, and extension), to international activities and perspectives that span all missions, and to excellence in all we do. The College has 10 academic departments, 294 faculty, 2842 undergraduate students, and 694 graduate students. Qualifications Ph.D. degree in plant sciences, biochemistry, computer science or related discipline by start date A record of research excellence and productivity commensurate with career stage Demonstrated potential or record of interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship Commitment to teaching and student mentorship Faculty Responsibilities Establish a vigorous, externally funded research program Contribute to the education and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students. Teach undergraduate and/or graduate level courses. Course modality is generally in person. The potential may exist for teaching online/distance courses during the academic year. Collaborate across disciplines to solve complex global One Health challenges Integration within the Purdue One Health Community Collectively, the strategic faculty recruitment initiatives represent a forward-thinking investment in Purdue’s research infrastructure and academic excellence. Faculty hired as part of these One Health strategic faculty recruitment initiatives will be supported as part of the overall One Health community. Together, these faculty members are expected to work across diverse disciplines, enhance Purdue’s external funding potential, and drive innovation at the intersection of health, environment, food, and economics. In addition to joining an academic unit, faculty hired through this initiative will have the opportunity to join a vibrant ecosystem of interdisciplinary centers and institutes, that span the hard-tech corridor between Indianapolis and West Lafayette including: Center for Plant Biology (CPB) Institute for Plant Sciences (IPS) Institute for Digital Forestry Institute for Digital and Advanced Agricultural Systems Furthermore, with Purdue's expanding presence in Indianapolis, including Purdue University in Indianapolis and the surrounding hard tech corridor, faculty will have additional opportunities for collaboration with clinical, industry, and translational partners. The integrated, cross-disciplinary nature of One Health is essential for addressing today’s most urgent One Health challenges and ensuring Purdue’s continued leadership in research, education, and community impact. Application Process To apply, please submit a cover letter indicating the top two preferred departments, CV, research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Application materials must be combined into a single pdf and submitted electronically in the CV field on the application site. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/28/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor%2C-Strategic-Management/44036-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Strategic Management",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Strategic Management Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44036 Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor, Strategic Management City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Mitch Daniels School of Business at Purdue University is seeking a faculty member in the Strategic Management Department at the Clinical Assistant Professor rank to begin August 16, 2027. Qualified candidates must have: Ph.D. in strategic management or related field, either completed or expected to be completed by August 16, 2027. Research and teaching expertise in strategic management or closely related topics, such as entrepreneurship, technology commercialization, manufacturing strategy, management of innovation, consulting or global strategy. Experience in supervising projects linking management and engineering topics is also desirable. Experience in residential MBA and online teaching at MBA level is also desirable. A successful candidate will teach strategic management or related courses and also likely supervise projects linking management and engineering topics in our Integrated Business and Engineering undergraduate program or masters or MBA programs. Application Process Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applicants should provide a cover letter, curriculum vitae, evidence of teaching performance if available, evidence of engagement with companies,  any research papers if available, and three letters of recommendation. Please use the following link to upload the names and email addresses of your letter writers; https://apps.it.purdue.edu/KARS/Apply/fHW472YBiN Questions should be addressed to the search committee chair, Professor Thomas Brush, by email to: brusht@purdue.edu A background check will be required for employment in the position. About the Organization For more information on the Strategic Management Dept , our programs, and our distinguished faculty, and selected research please visit: https://business.purdue.edu/academics/strategic-management/ https://business.purdue.edu/academics/strategic-management/programs.php https://business.purdue.edu/academics/strategic-management/home.php As Indiana’s land grant institution established in 1869, Purdue is one of the nation’s leading public research universities. Located in West Lafayette, IN, Purdue offers faculty a great work and non-work environment. Recently recognized as one of the safest cities in Indiana, West Lafayette is centrally located to a number of major business centers including Chicago (2 hours), Indianapolis (1 hour), Cincinnati (3 hours), Louisville (3 hours), Columbus (3.5 hours), and St. Louis (4 hours). Purdue’s Research Park is home to over 200 business start-ups, many which originated from faculty innovations. The Krannert School of Management offers undergraduate programs, executive, online, and weekend MBA programs, numerous specialized Master’s programs, and doctoral programs . For a complete list of benefits, please visit our website at: https://www.purdue.edu/hr/Benefits/ Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/25/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor%2C-Finance/44035-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Finance",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Finance Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44035 Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor, Finance City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Daniels School of Business at Purdue University invites applications for Clinical Assistant Professor position in Finance for an August 2027 start date. About the Clinical Assistant Professor Position The program has significant resources and is seeking people with an innovative, mission-driven, and collaborative mindset. The Clinical Professor will: Teach in multiple areas of finance at the undergraduate and graduate level. Serve as a faculty/academic advisor for academies/clubs/programs within the area(s) of finance that are most relevant to the candidate’s experience and interests. Assist with events and programming as needed to advance the finance program. Qualified candidates must have: A Ph.D. degree in Finance or related field by start date. Demonstrates strong and effective communication across diverse audiences The ideal candidate will have: Evidence of past collaborations between industry and academia Some industry experience at financial institutions Prior teaching, mentorship, or training experience that translates well to the classroom. Shows initiative in maintaining up-to-date knowledge with the latest finance industry practices and relevant academic research. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin October 23, 2026 and will continue until the positions are filled. For full consideration, please apply by October 23, 2026. A background check is required for employment in this position. Applicants should submit the following: Cover letter CV or resume Teaching statement that addresses how your background, experiences, and vision might add value to the finance area in the classroom. Three names to provide letters of recommendation here: https://apps.it.purdue.edu/KARS/Apply/NcX9c6AETM About the College The newly launched Daniels School of Business is built upon Purdue’s mission as a land-grant university to provide affordable and accessible education while combining technological excellence and business expertise. There are many opportunities to collaborate with the nation’s 4th-ranking Purdue Engineering and the top-ranking Purdue Computes disciplines in research as well as curriculum development. Purdue University and the Daniels School of Business are committed to free and open inquiry in all matters. Candidates are encouraged to address in their cover letter how they are prepared to contribute to a climate that values free inquiry and academic freedom. A background check will be required for employment in the position. For a complete list of benefits, please visit our website at: https://www.purdue.edu/hr/Benefits/ . Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/25/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Automotive-Engineering-&-Transportation/44023-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Automotive Engineering & Transportation",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Automotive Engineering & Transportation Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44023 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Automotive Engineering & Transportation City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary Purdue University's School of Mechanical Engineering invites applications for a tenured/tenure track Assistant/Associate Professor position in the broad area of Automotive Engineering & Transportation. Successful candidates must hold a Ph.D. degree in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related discipline by the start of the employment. Early-career applicants should show evidence of initiating independent research, while mid-career applicants should demonstrate a sustained record of independent research within academic or industrial organizations, and contributions to education and/or mentoring. The successful candidate will conduct original research, advise graduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate level courses, and perform service at the School, College, and University levels. The location of this position, including teaching responsibilities, is in Indianapolis. School and College The School of Mechanical Engineering at Purdue University is ranked 8th nationally for undergraduate programs, 8th for graduate programs, and 1st for online graduate programs by U.S. News and World Report. The School of ME is the largest ME program in the nation, with approximately 3400 undergraduate students, 1250 graduate students, 125 faculty, and 70 staff. The position is based at Purdue University in Indianapolis, the flagship campus’ urban extension launched in 2024, which places School of ME faculty at the center of Indiana’s automotive and motorsports ecosystem. Purdue’s Motorsports Engineering program, the only ABET-accredited program of its kind in the nation, is housed in the Dallara IndyCar Factory in Speedway, less than a mile from the Indianapolis Motor Speedway, providing classroom, hands-on, and diagnostic testing space alongside the chassis supplier for the IndyCar Series. Central Indiana is home to IndyCar, IMSA, and NHRA, and to major propulsion and vehicle manufacturers, including Rolls-Royce (with which Purdue holds a 10-year, $75 million strategic alliance), Allison Transmission, and Cummins, with Stellantis, Subaru, Toyota, Honda, and GM vehicle and battery plants across the state. Faculty in Indianapolis also have full access to the School’s research infrastructure in West Lafayette, about an hour away, including Ray W. Herrick Labs, Maurice Zucrow Labs, and Maha Fluid Power Labs. The School of ME is an integral part of Purdue’s College of Engineering. Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 9 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering continues to remain a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit applications to this site including (1) a cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a 2-page teaching plan, (4) a 3-page research plan, and (5) names and contact information for at least 5 references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For information/questions regarding applications, contact Engineering Academic Affairs, Purdue Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 25th, 2026. Applications received by December 25th, 2026 will be given full consideration. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/24/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Professor-ClinicalProfessional-Assistant/43975-en_US": {
      "title": "Professor Clinical/Professional Assistant",
      "description": "Professor Clinical/Professional Assistant Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 43975 Job Title: Professor Clinical/Professional Assistant City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Purdue University’s Department of Political Science is seeking to hire a teaching-focused faculty member in state and local political institutions at the rank of clinical (non-tenure track) assistant professor, to be based in Indianapolis. Principal Duties The successful candidate will teach primarily undergraduate courses on state and local political institutions and play a key role in developing and implementing the department’s academic programs at Purdue in Indianapolis, an extension of the West Lafayette campus. In addition to courses on state politics, local government, and Indiana politics, the ability to teach upper-level courses in political institutions and public policy making is particularly welcome. Purdue-Indianapolis faculty will collaborate with West Lafayette faculty to ensure curricular alignment and program excellence, contributing to a collegial, innovative academic environment that prioritizes experiential learning and public engagement in Indianapolis. Thus, this faculty member will have the benefit of joining a large Political Science department with the opportunity to contribute to the expansion of Purdue’s land-grant mission, potentially including the new Professional MA in Applied Governance, Technology, and Ethics. The standard teaching load is four courses per semester; a portion of the workload may be fulfilled through administrative or engagement roles such as managing the Department’s internships or other similar programs . Qualifications The candidate must have completed all requirements for the Ph.D. in political science or a related field by the date of employment and have expertise in state and local government.  All candidates must demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and mentoring. The College and University Purdue University is a public research university leading with excellence at scale. Ranked among top 10 public universities in the United States, Purdue discovers, disseminates and deploys knowledge with a quality and at a scale second to none. More than 107,000 students study at Purdue across multiple campuses, locations and modalities, including more than 58,000 at our main campus locations in West Lafayette and Indianapolis. Committed to affordability and accessibility, Purdue’s main campus has frozen tuition 14 years in a row. See how Purdue never stops in the persistent pursuit of the next giant leap — including its integrated, comprehensive Indianapolis urban expansion; the Mitch Daniels School of Business; Purdue Computes; the One Health initiative — at https://www.purdue.edu/president/strategic-initiatives/ . Application Procedures To apply, please visit careers.purdue.edu (Req #43975). Applications must be submitted online and include: 1) Curriculum Vitae, 2) Cover letter of interest that includes a statement describing how the applicant’s fit the principal duties of the position, and 3) confidential letters of recommendation from three academic references must be sent to politicalscienceamerican@purdue.edu . Screening of applicants will begin on October 24, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. For additional information, contact search committee chair Logan Strother at lstrothe@purdue.edu or politicalscienceamerican@purdue.edu . Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/24/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor%2C-Management-Information-Systems/44041-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Management Information Systems",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Management Information Systems Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44041 Job Title: Assistant Professor, Management Information Systems City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Daniels School of Business (DSB) at Purdue University invites applications for the assistant professor position beginning in Fall 2027. The primary responsibilities will be to conduct impactful high-quality research at the intersection of business and technology, teach at the undergraduate and graduate level, participate in course/curriculum development, and provide service to DSB, the University, and the Information Systems academic community.  Qualified candidates must: Complete a Ph. D. in Information Systems (IS), Economics, Computer Science, or a related discipline by the starting date Demonstrate potential for conducting impactful research and publishing in top-tier business journals Demonstrate evidence of teaching excellence We seek candidates whose research enhances our existing strengths while advancing new and impactful areas of inquiry. We particularly encourage applications from scholars with expertise in the economics of information systems, including digital transformation, the digital economy, and artificial intelligence (AI). Additional areas of interest include trustworthy AI, emerging technologies and business models, and the governance and regulation of digital technologies. Application process Applicants should submit the following: cover letter CV research statement teaching statement and teaching evaluations (if available) two writing samples three names for recommendation letter writers submitted here:  https://apps.it.purdue.edu/KARS/Apply/h763mw1dsU Questions and correspondences should be addressed to Mohammad Rahman, Chair of MIS Faculty Recruiting Committee. Review of applications will begin October 17, 2026 and the position will remain open until filled. The Faculty Recruiting Committee can be reached at mis-recruiting@purdue.edu . The Daniels School of Business is built upon Purdue’s mission as a land-grant university to provide affordable and accessible education while combining technological excellence and business expertise. There are many opportunities to collaborate with the nation’s 4th-ranking Purdue Engineering and the top-ranking Purdue Computes disciplines in research as well as curriculum development. Purdue University and the Daniels School of Business are committed to free and open inquiry in all matters. Candidates are encouraged to address in their cover letter how they are prepared to contribute to a climate that values free inquiry and academic freedom. A background check will be required for employment in the position. About the Organization As Indiana’s land grant institution established in 1869, Purdue is one of the nation’s leading public research universities. Located in West Lafayette, IN, Purdue offers faculty a great work and non-work environment. Recently recognized as one of the safest cities in Indiana, West Lafayette is centrally located to a number of major business centers including Chicago (2 hours), Indianapolis (1 hour), Cincinnati (3 hours), Louisville (3 hours), Columbus (3.5 hours), and St. Louis (4 hours). Purdue’s Research Park is home to over 300 business start-ups, many of which originated from faculty innovations. DSB offers undergraduate programs, executive, online, and hybrid Master of Business and Technology (MBT) programs, numerous specialized Master’s programs, and doctoral programs. For a complete list of benefits, please visit our website at: https://www.purdue.edu/hr/Benefits/ . Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/24/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-of-Sustainability-Engineering/44028-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Sustainability Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Sustainability Engineering Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44028 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Sustainability Engineering City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The School of Sustainability Engineering and Environmental Engineering (SEE) at Purdue University invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. Purdue University seeks to attract exceptional candidates with interests and expertise in sustainability engineering. Specific topics of interest include but are not limited to energy and resource efficiency, recycling/remanufacturing, sustainable manufacturing, green design, and life cycle engineering. Successful candidates must hold a Ph.D. degree in Sustainability Engineering, Environmental Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Materials Engineering, or a closely related discipline by the employment start date. Early-career applicants should show evidence of initiating independent research, while mid-career applicants should demonstrate a sustained record of independent research within academic or industrial organizations, and contributions to education and/or mentoring. The successful candidate will conduct original research, advise graduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate level courses, and perform service at the School, College, and University levels. School and College The School of Sustainability Engineering and Environmental Engineering (SEE) at Purdue University embraces both classic environmental engineering and sustainability engineering. The research of SEE embraces issues related to legacy, existing, and potential environmental challenges/opportunities. The SEE discovery mission is positioned to respond to society’s need to understand the world we live in, and to develop strategies for sustainably managing Earth’s limited resources and ecosystems so that they will be available for generations to come. SEE students learn systems engineering techniques to proactively avoid environmental problems to ensure that engineering systems are created that can exist in harmony with the natural world and serve society. SEE is an integral part of Purdue’s College of Engineering. Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 9 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering continues to remain a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process Applications must be submitted electronically via this site, and include: (1) cover letter, (2) complete curriculum vitae, (3) teaching plan up to 2 pages, (4) research plan up to 4 pages, and (5) names and contact information for at least four references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For information/questions regarding applications contact the Office of Academic Affairs, College of Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 24, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-One-Health-Intelligent-Medicines-College-of-Engineering/44246-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in One Health - Intelligent Medicines - College of Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in One Health - Intelligent Medicines - College of Engineering Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44246 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in One Health - Intelligent Medicines - College of Engineering City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Strategic Faculty Recruitment Initiative in One Health – Intelligent Medicines – College of Engineering Purdue University Main Campus | Indianapolis and West Lafayette, IN Tenure-Track/Tenured Faculty Positions at Assistant and Associate Ranks As part of Purdue University’s strategic investment in One Health – Intelligent Medicines, the College of Engineering invites applications for up to two tenure-track or tenured faculty positions at the Assistant or Associate Professor levels. Areas of Interest While all areas within the Intelligent Medicine theme are of interest, we are particularly focused on attracting candidates who specialize in: Advanced Manufacturing, Therapeutics Development, and Non-animal Models of Disease. Intelligent Production and Supply Chain Systems and Human Factors in Healthcare, Medicine and Pharmaceutical Manufacturing. Candidates whose research integrates emerging technologies and methodologies, including, but not limited to, artificial intelligence (AI), digital twins, reconfigurable systems, and novel experimental platforms are particularly encouraged to apply. Applicants should indicate in their application materials whether a primary appointment in Industrial Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, or Chemical Engineering would be most appropriate. Joint appointments across the College and University are possible for all candidates. Purdue's One Health Initiative This strategic recruitment will help advance Purdue’s One Health initiative ( https://www.purdue.edu/onehealth/) which seeks to tackle complex challenges with real-world impact at the intersection of human, animal, and plant health. This recruitment initiative builds on previous strategic faculty recruitment initiatives in: (1) Integrated Health; (2) AI-Driven Biomolecular Design, and (3) Advanced Chemistry. In addition, a parallel strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Healthy and Resilient Living Systems is ongoing. Through academic programs, research, facility infrastructure and industry partnerships, Purdue is making giant leaps in improving health outcomes for all living things and driving economic growth regionally and globally. This strategic faculty recruitment initiative focused on Intelligent Medicines is expected to build on prior recruitment initiatives and existing Purdue research and academic strengths, to transform research and impact human, animal, and environmental health by bridging silos and fostering collaboration across disciplines. The Intelligent Medicines theme seeks to create a framework that improves human, animal, and environmental health through the integration of technology, data, and systems thinking. This faculty recruitment initiative is disease agnostic and aims to establish new capabilities in AI-enabled therapeutic development, non-animal models of disease, advanced manufacturing, intelligent health systems, digital twins, robotics, human factors, supply chain resilience, and health technology innovation. By combining strengths in device innovation, computational intelligence, manufacturing systems, and healthcare operations, Purdue intends to create a highly visible flagship that strengthens industry engagement, expands workforce development opportunities, and attracts significant external funding. Qualifications A Ph.D. degree by employment start date in industrial engineering, chemical engineering, biomolecular engineering, mechanical engineering, chemistry, biology, computer science, systems engineering, operations research, statistics, or a related discipline A record of research excellence and productivity commensurate with rank Demonstrated potential or record of interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship Commitment to teaching and student mentorship Faculty Responsibilities Establish a vigorous, externally funded research program Contribute to the teaching and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students Collaborate across disciplines to solve complex global one health challenges Integration within the Purdue One Health Community Collectively, the strategic faculty recruitment initiatives represent a forward-thinking investment in Purdue’s research infrastructure and academic excellence. Faculty hired as part of these One Health strategic faculty recruitment initiatives will be supported as part of the overall One Health community. Together, these faculty members are expected to work across diverse disciplines, enhance Purdue’s external funding potential, and drive innovation at the intersection of health, environment, food, and economics. In addition to joining an academic unit, faculty hired under this initiative will have the opportunity to join a vibrant ecosystem of interdisciplinary centers and institutes, that span the hard tech corridor between Indianapolis and West Lafayette including: Regenstrief Center for Healthcare Engineering Lilly Purdue Innovation Institute Purdue Institute for Healthcare Systems Innovation Crossroads Pediatric Device Consortium COOK-Purdue Partnership The integrated, cross-disciplinary nature of One Health is essential for addressing today’s most urgent health challenges and ensuring Purdue’s continued leadership in research, education, and community impact. Application Process To apply, please submit a cover letter, CV, research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin on October 24, 2026, and continue until positions are filled. Applications should be submitted to this site. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-National-Defense-&-Security-Engineering/44145-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in National Defense & Security - Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in National Defense & Security - Engineering Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44145 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in National Defense & Security - Engineering City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Purdue Engineering invites applications for tenure/tenure-track positions at Assistant or Associate ranks in all engineering disciplines. Purdue University seeks to attract multiple exceptional candidates with interests and expertise related to relevant Defense and security related fields, including but not limited to directed energy, hypersonics, integrated sensing, electronic warfare, energetic materials, propulsion, space technology, microelectronics, cybersecurity, biotechnology, quantum science, future generation wireless technology, advanced materials, trusted AI and autonomy, integrated network systems-of-systems, human-machine interfaces, supply-chain logistics, and manufacturing. Successful candidates will be expected to collaborate across disciplines in the defense or security area. US citizenship is not required to apply for this position; however, many of the externally funded national defense-related research opportunities require US citizenship. Successful candidates must hold a Ph.D. degree in Aeronautics and Astronautics, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Materials Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or a closely related discipline by the employment start date. Early-career applicants must show evidence of initiating independent research, while mid-career applicants should demonstrate a sustained record of independent research within academic or industrial organizations, and contributions to education and/or mentoring. Successful candidates will conduct original research, advise graduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate level courses, be active in professional organizations, and perform service at the School/Department, College, and University levels. While the focus in this search is on candidates with potential tenure homes appointments in the Schools of Aeronautics and Astronautics, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Materials Engineering, Chemical Engineering, and Mechanical Engineering, applicants interested in other Purdue engineering schools are welcome to apply. College of Engineering Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 9 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering furthermore continues to be a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, and remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and remarkable facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit application to this site including (1) cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) teaching plan (2 pages), (4) research plan (2 pages), and (5) names and contact information for at least 5 references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For information/questions regarding applications contact the Office of Academic Affairs, College of Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 24, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Experimental-Semiconductor-Innovation-Engineering/44086-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Experimental Semiconductor Innovation - Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Experimental Semiconductor Innovation - Engineering Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44086 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Experimental Semiconductor Innovation - Engineering City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Purdue Engineering invites applications for multiple tenure-track positions at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in experimental semiconductor research. We seek exceptional candidates pursuing experimental research across the breadth of semiconductor science and engineering. Research areas may include, but are not limited to, semiconductor materials and processing; materials and device characterization; logic and memory technologies; advanced interconnects, heterogeneous integration and packaging; power and wide-bandgap semiconductor devices; integrated devices and circuits; and emerging semiconductor technologies. Successful candidates will have access to the Birck Nanotechnology Center, Purdue’s hub for advanced semiconductor research, fabrication, and characterization. Recent investments have expanded Birck’s capabilities for wafer-scale semiconductor research, including fabrication at up to 8-inch wafer scale. This is aiming in particular at translational research, especially with semiconducting companies in the vicinity to Birck. The 25,000-ft.2 Scifres Nanofabrication Laboratory is among the largest academic cleanrooms in the United States and houses more than 200 state-of-the-art tools, complemented by extensive capabilities for semiconductor characterization. Together, these resources support experimental research spanning materials science, process development, device fabrication, and integrated semiconductor technologies. Successful candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Materials Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, or a closely related discipline by the employment start date. The ideal candidate should possess a basic working knowledge of artificial intelligence and machine learning principles. Early-career applicants should show evidence of initiating independent research, while mid-career applicants should demonstrate a sustained record of independent research within academic or industrial organizations, and contributions to education and/or mentoring. The successful candidate will conduct original research, advise graduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, and contribute service at the School, College, and University levels. Applicants interested in a position in any of Purdue’s engineering schools are welcome to apply. College of Engineering Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 9 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering continues to remain a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit the following materials through the Purdue Careers site: (1) a cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vita, (3) a statement of research plans (no more than two pages), (4) a statement of teaching interests and plan (no more than two pages), and (5) names and contact information for at least five references. The search committee may contact references to request letters of recommendation. Questions regarding the application process may be directed to Engineering Academic Affairs, Purdue Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 24, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering offer a Concierge Program that provides dual-career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssociateFull-Professor%2C-MIS/44026-en_US": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor, MIS",
      "description": "Associate/Full Professor, MIS Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44026 Job Title: Associate/Full Professor, MIS City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Daniels School of Business (DSB) at Purdue University invites applications for the tenured associate/full professor position beginning in Fall 2027. The primary responsibilities will be to conduct impactful high-quality research at the intersection of business and technology, teach at the undergraduate and graduate level, participate in course/curriculum development, and provide service to DSB, the University, and the Information Systems academic community.  Qualified candidates must have: A Ph. D. in Information Systems (IS), Economics, Computer Science, or a related discipline by the starting date Excellent record of published research in top-tier business journals and recognition in the Information Systems academic community, commensurate with the rank Evidence of teaching excellence We seek candidates whose research enhances our existing strengths while advancing new and impactful areas of inquiry. We particularly encourage applications from scholars with expertise in the economics of information systems, including digital transformation, the digital economy, and artificial intelligence (AI). Additional areas of interest include trustworthy AI, emerging technologies and business models, and the governance and regulation of digital technologies. Application Process Applicants should submit the following: cover letter CV research statement teaching statement and teaching evaluations two writing samples three names for recommendation letter writers submitted here: https://apps.it.purdue.edu/KARS/Apply/8i9uReqScT Questions and correspondences should be addressed to Mohammad Rahman, Chair of MIS Faculty Recruiting Committee. Review of applications will begin October 17, 2026 and the position will remain open until filled. The Faculty Recruiting Committee can be reached at mis-recruiting@purdue.edu . About the Organization The Daniels School of Business is built upon Purdue’s mission as a land-grant university to provide affordable and accessible education while combining technological excellence and business expertise. There are many opportunities to collaborate with the nation’s 4th-ranking Purdue Engineering and the top-ranking Purdue Computes disciplines in research as well as curriculum development. Purdue University and the Daniels School of Business are committed to free and open inquiry in all matters. Candidates are encouraged to address in their cover letter how they are prepared to contribute to a climate that values free inquiry and academic freedom. A background check will be required for employment in the position. As Indiana’s land grant institution established in 1869, Purdue is one of the nation’s leading public research universities. Located in West Lafayette, IN, Purdue offers faculty a great work and non-work environment. Recently recognized as one of the safest cities in Indiana, West Lafayette is centrally located to a number of major business centers including Chicago (2 hours), Indianapolis (1 hour), Cincinnati (3 hours), Louisville (3 hours), Columbus (3.5 hours), and St. Louis (4 hours). Purdue’s Research Park is home to over 300 business start-ups, many of which originated from faculty innovations. DSB offers undergraduate programs, executive, online, and hybrid Master of Business and Technology (MBT) programs, numerous specialized Master’s programs, and doctoral programs. For a complete list of benefits, please visit our website at: https://www.purdue.edu/hr/Benefits/ . Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-AssociateFull-Professor%2C-Finance/44129-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Associate/Full Professor, Finance",
      "description": "Clinical Associate/Full Professor, Finance Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44129 Job Title: Clinical Associate/Full Professor, Finance City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Daniels School of Business at Purdue University invites applications for Clinical Associate/Full Professor position in Finance for an August 2027 start date. About the Clinical Associate/Full Professor Position The program has significant resources and is seeking people with an innovative, mission-driven, and collaborative mindset. The Clinical Professor will: Teach in multiple areas of finance at the undergraduate and graduate level. Serve as a faculty/academic advisor for academies/clubs/programs within the area(s) of finance that are most relevant to the candidate’s experience and interests. Assist with events and programming as needed to advance the finance program. Qualified candidates must have: A Ph.D. degree in Finance or related field by start date. Experience communicating finance-related concepts to students, academic colleagues, and/or professional audiences through teaching, presentations, publications, or professional activities. The ideal candidate will have: Evidence of past collaborations between industry and academia Some industry experience at financial institutions Prior teaching, mentorship, or training experience that translates well to the classroom. Shows initiative in maintaining up-to-date knowledge with the latest finance industry practices and relevant academic research. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin October 23, 2026 and will continue until the positions are filled. For full consideration, please apply by October 23, 2026. A background check is required for employment in this position. Applicants should submit the following: Cover letter CV or resume Teaching statement that addresses how your background, experiences, and vision might add value to the finance area in the classroom. Three names to provide letters of recommendation here: https://apps.it.purdue.edu/KARS/Apply/C3ZfJ0gTq1 About the College The newly launched Daniels School of Business is built upon Purdue’s mission as a land-grant university to provide affordable and accessible education while combining technological excellence and business expertise. There are many opportunities to collaborate with the nation’s 4th-ranking Purdue Engineering and the top-ranking Purdue Computes disciplines in research as well as curriculum development. Purdue University and the Daniels School of Business are committed to free and open inquiry in all matters. Candidates are encouraged to address in their cover letter how they are prepared to contribute to a climate that values free inquiry and academic freedom. A background check will be required for employment in the position. For a complete list of benefits, please visit our website at: https://www.purdue.edu/hr/Benefits/ . Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor%2C-Quantitative-Methods/44130-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Quantitative Methods",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Quantitative Methods Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44130 Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor, Quantitative Methods City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Daniels School of Business at Purdue University invites applications for a clinical assistant faculty position in the Department of Quantitative Methods beginning in Fall 2027. The position is non-tenure track and promotable to higher academic ranks. The successful candidate’s responsibilities will include a combination of the following: Developing instructional materials and teaching and coordinating undergraduate courses in data and analytics, such as Business Statistics, Management Science, Data Mining, Machine Learning, Predictive Analytics, Advanced Spreadsheet Modeling, and emerging AI topics including generative AI, large language models, and agentic AI. Developing and supervising experiential learning courses and projects for students in the undergraduate programs, and representing the Department of Quantitative Methods in existing program management and new program development within the school. Developing and teaching graduate-level quantitative methods and analytics courses for residential master’s programs and the Online Master of Science in Business Analytics (Online MSBA) program. Mentoring students in their academic and professional development , including the development of analytical capabilities and preparation for careers in business analytics and related fields. Engaging with academic and business communities to stay current with emerging developments in business analytics and AI; collaborating with relevant professionals and organizations; and translating these developments into timely and relevant curricula and student learning experiences. The position carries an annual workload of 18 credit hours of teaching (approximately six undergraduate sections or nine master’s sections) and 9 credit hours of service . Service responsibilities may contribute to the administration, operation, and development of the department, the Daniels School of Business, Purdue University, and the profession. Clinical faculty are also expected to engage proactively with businesses, professional organizations, and other external communities relevant to their disciplines. Salary and compensation are highly competitive and commensurate with the candidate’s experience and accomplishments. Additional information is available through Purdue University Human Resources Minimum Requiremements A Ph.D. or M.A./M.S. in Quantitative Methods or a related field, with demonstrated teaching experience at the college level. The degree must be completed before the first day of Purdue University’s Fall 2027 semester. Evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as student course evaluations or other documentation of successful college-level instruction. Evidence of experience developing, organizing, and/or supervising experiential learning projects, programs, or events. Familiarity with current AI methods and tools and an interest in incorporating emerging AI capabilities into analytics education. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with students, faculty colleagues, program administrators, and external stakeholders. Application adn Review Process Applications should include a curriculum vitae, a teaching statement, and available evidence of teaching effectiveness. Applicants should also submit the names and email addresses of three references through https://apps.it.purdue.edu/KARS/Apply/bxGmTu2K1K Review of applications will begin January 8, 2027 , and will continue until the position is filled. Inquiries may be directed to Professor Zhiwei Zhu ( zhu816@purdue.edu ) or Professor Yichen Zhang ( zhang@purdue.edu ), Daniels School of Business, Purdue University, 403 Mitch Daniels Blvd., West Lafayette, IN 47907, USA. A background check is required for employment in this position. About Purdue University As Indiana's land grant institution established in 1869, Purdue is one of the nation's leading public research universities. Located in West Lafayette, IN, Purdue offers a great work and living environment. As a college town, West Lafayette is centrally located to several major business centers including Indianapolis (1 hour), Chicago (2 hours), Cincinnati (3 hours), Louisville (3 hours), Columbus (3.5 hours), and St. Louis (4 hours). Purdue's Research Park is home to over 200 business start-ups, many of which originated from faculty innovations. Purdue University's vision is to be at the forefront of advancing Data Science-underpinned research and education by providing faculty and students with an integrated, Data Science-fluent campus ecosystem. It is home to a large number of world-class faculty engaged in fundamental research and applications of Data Science, Machine Learning, and Artificial Intelligence. Please visit https://www.purdue.edu/ to learn more about Purdue University. About Daniels School of Business Among a wide range of graduate and undergraduate degree programs, the Daniels School of Business has a very successful and highly rated master's program in Business Analytics & Information Management (MS BAIM) and an online Master of Science in Business Analytics. These programs are directed by faculty members from the Department of Quantitative Methods. The department also collaborates with the Krenicki Center for Business Analytics & Machine Learning. Please visit https://business.purdue.edu/ for more information about the Daniels School of Business and the Department of Quantitative Methods. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/22/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Visiting-Assistant-Professor-in-Higher-Education/44090-en_US": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor in Higher Education",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor in Higher Education Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44090 Job Title: Visiting Assistant Professor in Higher Education City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Position Visiting Assistant Professor of Educational Studies in Higher Education Job Position Description The Department of Educational Studies ( http://www.edst.purdue.edu ) within the College of Education at Purdue University invites applications for a 9-month position, Visiting Assistant Professor of Higher Education to begin no later than August 16, 2027. The Higher Education program has delivered a redesigned, research-intensive, and successful Ph.D. program since 2019. In Spring 2025, the program area began offering an online Master’s degree in Educational Studies with a concentration in Higher Education Systems, Policy, and Leadership. The faculty are dedicated to preparing future administrators and faculty members in the field of higher education. This position will serve both the Ph.D. and Masters level degree programs and is set for an initial term of one year, with a potential second, mutually agreed upon year. Responsibilities The successful candidate is expected to: Engage in scholarship with Ph.D. students, serving as research mentor for student peer-reviewed research papers Help coordinate support services for the new Master’s program Teach a variety of courses in both the Higher Education PhD and the Higher Education Systems, Policy, and Leadership Master’s program, 2 classes in Fall and 2 classes in Spring semesters Guide doctoral students in their area of research and/or practice expertise Contribute to and engage in service to the program, department, college, and profession . Required Qualifications Hold a Ph.D. or Ed.D. with a concentration in higher education or related field by the position start date. ABD with a completion date before August 2027 may be considered. A strong record or demonstrated potential of research productivity in peer-reviewed high quality journals. Ability to teach courses in both the Ph.D. and Master’s programs in higher education. Ability to work in the U.S. without immigration sponsorship from Purdue University. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of teaching excellence. Strong consideration for applicants with expertise and/or experience teaching higher education law, finance, assessment & program evaluation, and/or organizational administration & theory. Strong methodological experience in one or more areas of inquiry (e.g., experimental research, survey, case-study, phenomenological, systematic literature review). Salary Salary and benefits commensurate with qualifications and experience. Starting Date No later than August 16, 2027 Application Procedure This position is a 9-month, visiting assistant professor position with a starting date no later than August 16, 2027. Review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications must include all of the following : A cover letter outlining the applicant’s qualifications and experience addressed to the search committee chair(s), A research statement, A teaching statement addressing teaching experience, and/or graduate student mentorship, A curriculum vitae, Three letters of reference, including contact information . (Note: complete letters required;  a list of references will not meet this requirement) All materials must be submitted through SuccessFactors , and addressed to Dr. Lisa Lambert Snodgrass and Dr. Terron Phillips, Search Committee Co-Chairs, Department of Educational Studies, 100 North University Street, West Lafayette, IN 47907 . Review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Direct questions about the position to the Search Committee Chairs at lsnodgra@purdue.edu and phill350@purdue.edu . Candidate must have the ability to work in the US without immigration sponsorship from Purdue University. Background Check A background check will be required for employment in this position. Equal Opportunity Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/21/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Lecturer-in-Finance/44016-en_US": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Finance",
      "description": "Lecturer in Finance Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44016 Job Title: Lecturer in Finance City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Job Description The Finance Area at the Mitch Daniels School of Business , Purdue University, invites candidates to apply for multiple full-time lecturer positions. Lecturers teach courses in multiple areas of finance at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Although teaching is the main activity, the new hire would be expected to engage in some service activities (e.g., course development or coordination across sections). Job Qualification Candidates must have a Master’s degree in Finance or a related field at the time of application. Candidates should provide evidence that they can successfully teach undergraduate or graduate classes. Application Procedure To apply for this position, candidates are to directly apply here and submit the following documents as PDF files: Vita Statement describing how you meet the job qualifications Names of 3 references or letters of reference entered here Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. What We'd Like You to Know Learn more about Purdue’s benefits summary https://bit.ly/3sHGbls Candidates must have the ability to work in the US without immigration sponsorship (such as, but not limited to H-1B, TN, E-3 or O-1 visa status) from Purdue University. A Background Check is required for employment in this position FLSA: Exempt (Not Eligible For Overtime) Retirement Eligibility: Defined Contributions Waiting Period Purdue University is an EO/EA University. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/10/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Golomb-Visiting-Assistant-Professor/43948-en_US": {
      "title": "Golomb Visiting Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Golomb Visiting Assistant Professor Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 43948 Job Title: Golomb Visiting Assistant Professor City: WEST LAFAYETTE Job Description: Job Summary Purdue University Department of Mathematics Position Title: Golomb Visiting Assistant Professor The Department of Mathematics in the College of Science at Purdue University invites applications from recent Ph.D.s for multiple three-year positions as Golomb Visiting Assistant Professor. These positions come at a time of dynamic leadership and with significant investment in the College of Science - Purdue’s second-largest college, comprising the mathematical, physical, and life sciences. For information about our department, see www.math.purdue.edu . Qualifications: The positions are open to mathematicians who will have completed their Ph.D. (or its equivalent) in mathematics or in a closely related field by August 16, 2027.  Candidates must have a strong research record in mathematics, as evidenced by papers and preprints, and a record of teaching accomplishments. Duties include continued research production, engagement with faculty and students, and teaching of undergraduate mathematics courses. Applications should be submitted online through www.mathjobs.org and should include (1) a cover letter, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a research statement, (4) a teaching statement, and (5) three letters of recommendation, one of which discusses the candidate’s teaching qualifications. In addition, for purposes of equity, to be considered for the position, applicants will also need to create a profile in Purdue SuccessFactors. Reference letter writers should be asked to submit their letters online through www.mathjobs.org . Direct all inquiries to mathexec@purdue.edu. All applications received by November 30, 2026, will be given full consideration. Some offers will be made before the end of January 2027. A background check is required for employment in these positions. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/9/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-of-Experimental-Relativistic-Heavy-Ion-Physics/43899-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Experimental Relativistic Heavy-Ion Physics",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Experimental Relativistic Heavy-Ion Physics Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 43899 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Experimental Relativistic Heavy-Ion Physics City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Physics & Astronomy at Purdue University invites applications for a faculty position in Experimental Relativistic Heavy-Ion Physics to begin August 2027. The current relativistic heavy-ion efforts in the department involve physics analyses of the RHIC/STAR/sPHENIX and LHC/CMS experiments, detector design and simulation works on the ePIC experiment at the Electron-Ion Collider (EIC), and AI-facilitated research on the EIC under the DOE's Genesis Mission. The successful candidate will establish a vibrant, externally funded research program, driving cutting-edge science in existing experiments while maintaining a strong leadership presence, and spearheading new hardware, software, and/or physics initiatives for EIC. The candidate will mentor graduate students and postdocs and contribute to teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Qualifications Candidates must have a PhD i n Nuclear Physics or a closely related field by the start of the appointment. ( Postdoctoral experience is highly desirable.) Demonstrated record of research accomplishments in nuclear physics, evidenced by publications and presentations at leading conferences. Experience and expertise in experimental nuclear physics, with an emphasis on relativistic heavy-ion physics or related areas. The Department, College, and University The Department of Physics and Astronomy has 60 tenured and tenure-track professors, 200 graduate students, and 280 undergraduates. It is engaged in research in astrophysics, atomic-molecular-optical physics, biophysics, condensed matter, high-energy physics, nuclear physics, physics education, and quantum information science. More information is available at https://www.physics.purdue.edu/ . The College of Science, encompassing the physical, computing, and life sciences at Purdue, is home to over 350 faculty and more than 6000 students. More information can be found at https://www.purdue.edu/science/ . Purdue University is one of the nation’s leading land-grant universities, with an enrollment of over 52,000 students primarily focused on STEM subjects. The university hosts the Rosen Center for Advanced Computing, which provides faculty and students with access to diverse high-performance computing resources ( https://www.rcac.purdue.edu ). Application Procedure Application materials must be submitted through https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-of-Experimental-Relativistic-Heavy-Ion-Physics/43899-en_US/ and include: (1) Cover letter, (2) Curriculum vitae with a list of publications, (3) Statement of present and future research plans (4-page limit), (4) Statement of teaching philosophy. In addition, candidates should arrange for at least 3 letters of reference to be sent to nuclearsearch@purdue.edu . Questions regarding the positions and the search may also be directed to nuclearsearch@purdue.edu . Applications completed by December 4th, 2026, will be given full consideration, although the search will continue until the position is filled.  A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/9/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate/43836-en_US": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Associate Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 43836 Job Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Position POSTDOCTORAL RESEARCH ASSOCIATE Job Position Description The Department of Educational Studies within the College of Education at Purdue University is seeking applicants for a Postdoctoral Research Associate, in the Gifted Education Research & Resource Institute (GER ² I). GER²I’s mission is to promote the holistic growth of giftedness, creativity, and talents in individuals throughout their lives. We offer enrichment programs for talented youth, graduate programs for future leaders, professional development for educators, and conduct innovative research in related fields. Responsibilities T he Postdoctoral Research Associate will work with the GER ² I Executive Director and his team to: Design, implement, and manage research studies related to gifted education, talent development, and related areas Conduct quantitative, qualitative, and mixed-methods data collection, analysis, interpretation, and dissemination Lead and contribute to the preparation of scholarly publications, technical reports, conference presentations, and grant proposals Develop and implement program evaluation plans for GER ² I programs and initiatives, including the collection and analysis of outcome data and the communication of findings to stakeholders Collaborate with GER ² I staff to support the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of educational programs Mentor graduate and undergraduate students involved in research and evaluation projects, as appropriate Engage with school, community, and university partners to support research-practice partnerships and outreach activities Contribute to the mission of GER ² I through service, collaboration, and participation in strategic initiatives Required Qualifications PhD in Education, Educational Psychology, Psychology, Gifted Education, or related area completed by the start of the employment Demonstrated experience conducting research, including study design, data collection, analysis, and interpretation Experience with qualitative, quantitative, and/or mixed-methods research methodologies Strong written and verbal communication skills Additional Desired Qualifications Ability to work collaboratively with a research team Experience managing multiple projects Knowledge of gifted education Experience with program evaluation Experience writing or contributing to grant proposals and externally funded projects Experience mentoring graduate or undergraduate students Experience with out-of-school educational programs Additional Information Purdue will not sponsor employment authorization for this position Remote work may be available for this position with the expectation to travel to Purdue University occasionally Salary Salary and benefits commensurate with qualifications and experience Starting Date November 1, 2026 or as soon as the position is filled Application Procedure This position is a 12-month, Postdoctoral Research Associate position with a starting date of November 1, 2026 or as soon as the position is filled. Review of applications will begin immediately, and continue until the position is filled. Applications must include: a cover letter outlining the applicant’s qualifications, relevant experience, and research experience a current curriculum vitae names and contact information of three references, and a writing sample (preferably a manuscript published in a peer-reviewed, scholarly journal) All materials must be submitted through Success Factors , but addressed to Nielsen Pereira, Executive Director, Gifted Education Research & Resource Institute, Department of Educational Studies, BRNG,100 N. University Street, West Lafayette, IN 47907 . Direct questions about the positions to npereira@purdue.edu . Background Check A background check will be required for employment in this position Equal Opportunity Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university Apply now Posting Start Date: 8/31/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-or-Tenure-AssistantAssociate-Professor%2C-Large-Animal-Surgery/41347-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical or Tenure Assistant/Associate Professor, Large Animal Surgery",
      "description": "Clinical or Tenure Assistant/Associate Professor, Large Animal Surgery Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 41347 Job Title: Clinical or Tenure Assistant/Associate Professor, Large Animal Surgery City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Purdue University College of Veterinary Medicine (PVM), Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences (VCS), invites applications for a full-time (12 month) Tenure-track or Clinical-track position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in Large Animal Surgery.  PVM is highly supportive of individual faculty career growth and development.  A formal faculty mentoring program is in place. Qualifications Qualifications for the position include a DVM or equivalent degree, and completion of a residency program registered by the American College of Veterinary Surgeons (ACVS), or board certification by the ACVS. Job Responsibilities The clinical responsibility will be caring for all large animal species with a predominant focus on large animal surgery. Salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. A background check is required for employment by the University. The successful candidate should possess excellent interpersonal, communication and teaching skills, and be able to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, house officers and clientele. They will actively participate in the discovery, learning and engagement missions of the PVM and VCS department. Important activities include: Discovery : All faculty are expected to collaborate on clinical research projects.  Tenure track faculty are expected to develop an independent research program. Research that complements the interests and strengths of current faculty is ideal but can also be tailored to the candidate’s specific background and interests. Collaborative research opportunities are also available with the Weldon School of Biomedical Engineering, the College of Health and Human Science, and the College of Agriculture among others. Learning: Excellent clinical, didactic and laboratory instruction of veterinary students, veterinary nursing students, house officers, and graduate students. Service and Engagement: Participation in committee work, professional organizations, delivery of continuing education, and other applicable activities. Clinical Service: Providing clinical service to patients of the Purdue Veterinary Hospital (typical time commitment: 30 -50% Tenure Track and 60-70% Clinical Track); instructing veterinary students, veterinary nursing students, and house officers; and building strong relationships with referring veterinarians. The successful candidate will participate in a shared on-call emergency service that is shared with other faculty. College and Department The Purdue University Veterinary Hospital recently completed a major expansion project. The new David and Bonnie Brunner Purdue Veterinary Medical Hospital Complex includes: 1) The David and Bonnie Brunner Equine Hospital, a state-of-the-art facility covering over 73,000 square feet, including an outpatient center, intensive care unit, advanced imaging (standing CT, MRI, nuclear medicine and radiology), surgical and theriogenology facilities; and 2) The David and Bonnie Brunner Farm Animal Hospital, a 24,000-square-foot building offering comprehensive farm animal medical and surgical care. The new complex provides state-of-the-art teaching facilities dedicated to educating the next generation of veterinary professionals, enabling faculty to provide top quality compassionate animal health care, and serve as a catalyst for interdisciplinary clinical research. Commitment to the College and Departmental missions of learning, discovery, and engagement, and support of the College and Departmental strategic plans are essential. The College of Veterinary Medicine at Purdue University values, nurtures, and respects all members of its community and ensures an environment of excellence where all students, faculty, and staff are inspired and empowered to achieve their full potential. Applications Review of applications will begin on September 25, 2026, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should provide a letter of intent describing professional goals, and teaching philosophy; a curriculum vitae; and the names and contact information of three professional references via the provided link: Current employees apply via this provided link: Equal Opportunity Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access employer. Apply now Posting Start Date: 8/24/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Actuarial-Science/42428-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Actuarial Science",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Actuarial Science Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 42428 Job Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Actuarial Science City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The College of Science at Purdue University invites applications for a tenure-track/tenured position in Actuarial Science, a program jointly managed by the Mathematics Department and Statistics Department. This appointment will be at the level of Assistant Professor. The College of Science is committed to further enhancing Purdue’s top-ranked Actuarial Science program, with the intent to create a globally leading research program that simultaneously best prepares strong undergraduate and graduate students for the actuarial profession. Job overview continued Purdue University in Indianapolis is a new, fully integrated expansion of the West Lafayette campus, extending to central Indiana the academic rigor and accessible excellence for which Purdue is known. As the state’s only public top 10 university, most trusted university and most innovative university, Purdue is focused and committed to strengthening its presence in Indiana’s industrial and technological center. Purdue in Indianapolis is creating an innovative, STEM-based collegiate experience by connecting future-ready Purdue students and faculty in Indianapolis to local businesses to accelerate Indiana’s STEM pipeline and tech ecosystem, fueling impact for our region and the world. Learn more about Purdue’s latest giant leap at: https://www.purdue.edu/campuses/indianapolis/ . Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in mathematics, statistics, or actuarial science and have demonstrated excellence in research and a strong commitment to teaching. Outstanding applicants in all areas of actuarial science will be considered, including but not limited to probability, risk measurement, stochastic modeling, data science, and the broader mathematical and computational sciences. Preference will be given to candidates who are willing to acquire, or already possess, experience with the exam system that governs the actuarial profession. Duties Successful candidates will be expected to develop research programs in their fields of expertise, teach courses in mathematical or statistical areas underpinning actuarial science with some semesters at the West Lafayette campus and some semesters at the Indianapolis campus, develop an external funding portfolio, build connections with the actuarial profession, and participate in the program, college, and broader university activities. Program Information The Actuarial Science program is recognized as a Center of Actuarial Excellence by the Society of Actuaries. The program offers a stimulating academic environment which connects a variety of research programs and areas with the actuarial profession. With over 300 undergraduate students and a thriving partnership with Purdue’s Data Mine learning community, the program is also tightly coupled with some of Purdue’s fastest-growing majors, such as Data Science. Actuarial Science is part of the College of Science, which comprises the mathematical, computational, physical, and life sciences at Purdue. It is the second-largest college at Purdue with over 350 faculty and more than 7,000 students. The College is pursuing significant new initiatives that complement campus-wide plans, including data science as a strategic priority. Opportunities for collaboration exist across mathematics, probability, statistics, the physical and life sciences, and in particular both a newly reimagined School of Business and a burgeoning campus presence in the center of Indianapolis. Purdue itself is one of the nation’s leading land-grant universities, with an enrollment of over 50,000 students primarily focused on STEM subjects. For more information about Purdue’s Actuarial Science program, https://www.science.purdue.edu/actuarial-science/ What We Want You to Know Learn more about Purdue’s benefits summary: https://bit.ly/3sHGbls Candidates must have the ability to work in the US without immigration sponsorship (such as, but not limited to, H-1B, TN, E-3, or O-1 visa status) from Purdue University. A Background Check is required for employment in this position FLSA: Exempt (Not Eligible For Overtime) Retirement Eligibility: Defined Contributions Waiting Period Purdue University is an EO/EA University. Apply now Posting Start Date: 8/4/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor-of-Agricultural-Education/42250-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 42250 Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education City: West Lafayette Job Description: The College The Department is an integral part of the College of Agriculture, one of the world’s leading colleges of agricultural, food, life, and natural resource sciences. The College is ranked third in the U.S. and sixth in the world in the 2026 QS World University Rankings. The College is deeply committed to the three land-grant missions (teaching, research, and extension), to international activities and perspectives that span all missions, and to excellence in all we do. The College has 11 academic departments, 279 faculty, 2896 undergraduate students, and 640 graduate students. Job Summary The Agronomy Department in the College of Agriculture at Purdue University is seeking applications for a Clinical Assistant Professor (full time, academic year appointment with some summer support available) with primary teaching responsibilities in School-Based Agricultural Education teacher preparation. The expected start date is August 17, 2026. This position will be joint with the Department of Curriculum and Instruction in the College of Education. The successful candidate will lead an innovative teaching, engagement and research program focused on the scholarship of teaching and learning.  The successful candidate will develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the Agricultural Education teacher preparation program, contribute to the scholarship of teaching and learning, and mentor graduate students in this space.  They will provide service to the program, department, college, and university, and engage with stakeholders at all levels. We welcome applications from candidates with classroom experience, and a strong vision for teaching and mentoring. Qualifications Applicant must possess a PhD or EdD in agricultural education or closely related field by the start of the appointment. A minimum three years of successful middle and/or high school agriculture teaching experience is required.  Strong written and oral communication and interpersonal skills are also required. Candidates must be eligible for Instructional License in CTE: Agriculture. Experience in college-level School-Based Agricultural Education teacher preparation instruction is desired. Job Responsibilites The successful candidate is expected to develop a nationally recognized teaching, research and engagement program focused on preparing future teachers of School-Based Agricultural Education. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the Agricultural Education teacher preparation program, mentor and serve as career advisor for undergraduate students, develop curriculum, serve as the university student teacher supervisor for Agricultural Education student teachers, and assist with the teacher education licensure accreditation process for Agricultural Education. Course modality is generally in person. The potential may exist for teaching online/distance courses during the academic year. The successful candidate will contribute to the scholarship of teaching and learning, and mentor graduate students in this space.  They will provide service to the program, school, college, and university through committee participation, stakeholder collaboration, co-advisor of the IAAE-Purdue student organization, exploration of re-establishing Purdue’s Alpha Tau Alpha Honorary Agricultural Education student organization, and engage with stakeholders at all levels. Application Instructions Interested applicants must submit an application packet that includes a cover letter that speaks to the candidate’s qualifications for and interests in the position with contact information, a curriculum vitae that includes a summary of academic and other professional experiences, a statement of Teaching Philosophy including teaching and research interests and the names and contact information for three professional references. All materials must be submitted electronically via this site. Address questions to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Bruce Erickson ( berickso@purdue.edu ). A background check will be required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 6/8/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assoc_Full-Professor-of-Engineering-Practice-for-Executive-MS-in-AI-Engineering-Leadership-Program/39966-en_US": {
      "title": "Assoc./Full Professor of Engineering Practice for Executive MS in AI Engineering Leadership Program",
      "description": "Assoc./Full Professor of Engineering Practice for Executive MS in AI Engineering Leadership Program Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 39966 Job Title: Assoc./Full Professor of Engineering Practice for Executive MS in AI Engineering Leadership Program City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Purdue University’s College of Engineering invites applications for a Professor of Engineering Practice (PEP) position at the Associate/Full level in the Elmore Family School of Electrical and Computer Engineering with a rare opportunity: to help build a new graduate program from the ground up. We seek exceptional candidates with deep experience in (a) one or more technical areas including Artificial Intelligence, Physical AI, the AI Tech Stack, advanced computing, AND (b) technical organizational leadership and management, who are excited by the challenge of launching and shaping something entirely new. A Professor of Practice is a non-tenure-track faculty member with extensive real-world professional experience, bringing industry expertise to the classroom. The successful candidate will be both a founding faculty member and the inaugural Program Director for Purdue’s new Executive MS in AI Engineering Leadership, a forward-leaning program designed to prepare mid-career engineers and technology professionals not only to understand advanced technologies, but to lead people, organizations, and innovation efforts in an accelerating AI-driven world. Students will choose between two high-demand tracks: Physical AI and the AI Tech Stack. Based in Silicon Valley at Playground Global in Palo Alto, California, the program is anchored in online instruction, with optional in-person enrichment and experiential opportunities in Palo Alto designed to extend learning beyond the virtual classroom. These activities may include workshops, guest lectures, networking events, site visits and other immersive experiences, bringing together Purdue’s engineering excellence, cutting-edge industry expertise, and the energy of the world’s most influential technology ecosystem. This role offers the chance to work closely with tech leaders, shape curriculum, and develop experiences that reflect real-world AI innovation organizational leadership, and the management capabilities required to guide technical teams and enterprises. Primary Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: • Teach graduate-level courses in the Executive MS in AI Engineering Leadership program, spanning technical foundations and organizational leadership topics. • Serve as the inaugural Program Director , providing academic and strategic leadership for the program. • Lead the development and continuous refinement of curriculum across the Physical AI and AI Tech Stack tracks, ensuring alignment with industry needs and emerging technologies. • Build and maintain partnerships with industry leaders, alumni, and external stakeholders, particularly within the Silicon Valley ecosystem. • Initiate and guide programmatic activities that enhance student learning, professional development, and industry engagement. • Mentor students and emerging leaders , drawing on professional experience to support career growth and leadership development. We are looking for someone with a PhD degree in electrical engineering, computer engineering, computer science, or a related discipline, or an MS degree in any of the above-mentioned disciplines plus a minimum of 10 years of experience along with extensive professional networks in one or more of the following technical areas: physical AI, AI infrastructure, and robotics and autonomy industries, by the employment start date. While deep technical expertise in AI is not required, the successful candidate must have significant organizational leadership and management experience, including leading technical teams, shaping organizational strategy, developing talent, and delivering products or programs at scale. This is a position for a builder—someone who thrives in dynamic environments, understands the complexities of managing technical organizations, and sees opportunity in the space between academia and industry. Application Process Purdue Engineering is one of the largest and most highly ranked engineering colleges in the nation. With four disciplines ranked in the top four and nine in the top ten (U.S. News & World Report), and the nation’s #2 online graduate engineering program, Purdue is expanding that excellence to meet the moment in AI and leadership development. To apply, please submit an application to this site, including: (1) cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae or résumé, (3) statement of teaching philosophy, including your approach to working with technical professionals (max. 3 pg.), (4) statement on what emerging leaders in AI, the AI Tech Stack, and Physical AI need to know and how you would prepare them (max. 1 pg.), (5) Names and contact information of at least three references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For questions regarding the position or the application process, contact Engineering Academic Affairs, Purdue Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on June 8, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 5/7/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Tenure-or-Clinical-Track-AssistantAssociate-Professor-Veterinary-Anatomic-Pathology/40468-en_US": {
      "title": "Tenure or Clinical Track Assistant/Associate Professor - Veterinary Anatomic Pathology",
      "description": "Tenure or Clinical Track Assistant/Associate Professor - Veterinary Anatomic Pathology Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 40468 Job Title: Tenure or Clinical Track Assistant/Associate Professor - Veterinary Anatomic Pathology City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Position: The Department of Comparative Pathobiology (CPB) and the Animal Disease Diagnostic Laboratory (ADDL) at Purdue University – College of Veterinary Medicine (PVM) is seeking a full-time (12-month) Veterinary Anatomic Pathologist. Academic rank and compensation will be commensurate with academic record and experience. Tenure or clinical track Assistant/Associate professor position Qualifications DVM or equivalent degree Board certification or eligibility by the American or European College of Veterinary Pathologists (ACVP or ECVP) Proven ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues, laboratory staff, and other stakeholders aligned with the mission of the diagnostic laboratory and department. For tenure track, PhD in a related field is required Responsibilities Diagnostic Service – Perform diagnostic pathology duties including necropsies and biopsies with histopathologic examinations of these cases, writing reports, and consultation and advice to clinical veterinarians, producers and owners. Teaching – Contribute to the teaching mission of the college. Opportunities exist to teach in the DVM program, Veterinary Technology program, and the anatomic pathology, clinical pathology, microbiology, poultry, and laboratory animal medicine residency programs. Research – Maintain a program of scholarly activities, which may include independent research or participation in collaborative research, providing continuing education/outreach to ADDL constituencies, presentations at local, regional and/or national meetings, and publication in peer-reviewed journals. Academic service is expected to include but is not limited to, departmental, college, and university committees; professional organizations; and editorial or grant review panels. College and University The Indiana Animal Disease Diagnostic Laboratory at Purdue University is a key component of Indiana’s animal health infrastructure and serves as a regional and national leader in veterinary diagnostics, disease surveillance, and emergency response. The ADDL’s mission is to provide reliable, innovative, and vigilant services to veterinarians, animal producers, and regulatory agencies. With a skilled and dedicated workforce delivering services that meet all current standards, the ADDL plays an integral role in animal health by coordinating diagnostic strategies and delivering timely test results to partners in multiple sectors of veterinary medicine. The AAVLD is fully accredited by the American Association of Veterinary Laboratory Diagnosticians. Indiana Animal Disease Diagnostic Laboratory - College of Veterinary Medicine - Purdue University The mission of the Department of Comparative Pathobiology is to understand the causes and pathogenesis of diseases of animals, and to apply this knowledge to improve the health of people and animals. CPB faculty support the teaching mission of the college by participating in the DVM and Veterinary Technology programs, graduate student training, and residencies in Anatomic Pathology, Clinical Pathology, Microbiology, Poultry, and Laboratory Animal Medicine. CPB is home to the Center for Animal Welfare Science and the Center for the Human Animal Bond. Comparative Pathobiology - College of Veterinary Medicine - Purdue University The Purdue College of Veterinary Medicine focuses on globally advancing animal and human health and well-being through excellence in learning, discovery, and engagement, as the leading veterinary college for comprehensive education of the veterinary team, and for discovery and engagement in selected areas of veterinary and comparative biomedical sciences. Purdue University College of Veterinary Medicine - College of Veterinary Medicine - Purdue University Purdue University is a public land-grant research university in West Lafayette, Indiana, United States, and the flagship campus of the Purdue University system. Purdue University is famous for its world-class engineering, agriculture, and technology programs, consistently ranking among the nation's best public universities. Purdue University Application Process To be considered, each application should include: Curriculum vitae Summary/statement of teaching philosophy and experience Summary/statement of diagnostic service experience and vision Summary/statement of research experience, interests and vision Names and contact information of three professional references Review of applications is ongoing and will continue until the position is filled.  Start date will be negotiable.  A background check is required for employment in this position.  Applicants needing more information are encouraged to contact Dr. Steve Hooser, Chair of the Search Committee at shooser1@purdue.edu. EEO/AA Statement Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 4/1/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-or-Tenure-Professor%2C-Cardiology/40356-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical or Tenure Professor, Cardiology",
      "description": "Clinical or Tenure Professor, Cardiology Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 40356 Job Title: Clinical or Tenure Professor, Cardiology City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Purdue University College of Veterinary Medicine, Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, invites applications for a full-time (12-month) Clinical or Tenure-Track position in Cardiology at the Assistant or Associate Professor level.  The successful candidate will join an established clinical service, which includes one tenured faculty, one tenure-track faculty, three nurses, and four cardiology residents. Details Our comparative cardiovascular medicine and interventional cardiology service is equipped with state-of-the-art technology, including digital ECG, GE Vivid E95 echocardiography with a digital database and three review stations, portable GE Vivid iq, pediatric and adult 4D TEE probes, and Medtronic and St. Jude/Abbott pacemaker programmers. We also offer hemostatic assays, including thromboelastography and platelet aggregometry. The service operates a dedicated 650 ft² stand-alone interventional catheterization lab with advanced technology, such as an invasive hemodynamic recording system, cardiac output computers, and a Philips Zenition 70 Pulsera digital flat panel detector C-arm. Recently, we upgraded to a state-of-the-art cardiac EP lab featuring the Abbott EnSite System, which includes a next-generation 3D mapping platform and in-person support from mappers and collaborating MDs in Indianapolis. We handle a high volume of interventional cases, approximately 70-100 annually. Our strong relationships with local referring veterinarians, breeders and rescue groups lead to a significant caseload focused on screening, diagnosing, and managing animals with congenital cardiac defects. The Purdue University Veterinary Hospital has completed a major expansion project. Encompassing 162,500 square feet, the new David and Bonnie Brunner Purdue Veterinary Medical Hospital Complex includes three components located just east of the existing Lynn Hall of Veterinary Medicine: • The David and Bonnie Brunner Small Animal Hospital (adding 65,000 square feet to the existing small animal hospital facilities in Lynn Hall) • The David and Bonnie Brunner Equine Hospital • The David and Bonnie Brunner Farm Animal Hospital The new complex provides state of the art teaching facilities dedicated to educating the next generation of veterinary professionals, enabling faculty to provide top quality compassionate animal health care, and serve as a catalyst for interdisciplinary clinical research. Qualifications Qualifications for the position include a DVM or equivalent degree and board certification or completion of a cardiology residency program registered by the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (ACVIM) or the European College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (ECVIM). Individuals currently in an ACVIM or ECVIM approved training program and with an interest in an academic career are encouraged to apply. Salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. A background check will be required for employment in this position. Job Responsibilities The successful candidate will actively participate in the learning, discovery and engagement activities of the College and Department. These activities include: Service and Engagement : Clinical duties will include primary case responsibility, training of cardiology residents, teaching of veterinary and veterinary nursing students, provision of consultation to other services within the hospital, and participation in the extension cardiology service. Learning : Emphasis will be on clinical training of DVM students, house officers, and veterinary nursing students. Participation in didactic teaching is also expected. Discovery : Clinical track faculty are expected to participate in and contribute to collaborative research that complements and builds on current interests and strengths of the cardiovascular medicine service, department, and College.  Tenure track faculty are expected to develop an independent research program in cardiology. The College is highly supportive of individual faculty career growth and development and there is a formal faculty mentoring program in place. College and Department Commitment to the College and Departmental missions of learning, discovery, and engagement, and support of the College and Department strategic plans are essential. The College of Veterinary Medicine at Purdue University values, nurtures, and respects all members of its community and ensures an environment of inclusive excellence where all students, faculty, and staff are inspired and empowered to achieve their full potential. Applications Review of applications will begin on March 9, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should provide a letter of intent describing professional goals (including teaching philosophy), curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information of three professional references via the provided link: Current employees apply via the provided link: Equal Opportunity Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 2/10/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Department-Head-CPB/39757-en_US": {
      "title": "Department Head CPB",
      "description": "Department Head CPB Job Details | Purdue University Department Head CPB By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 39757 Job Title: Department Head CPB City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Purdue University College of Veterinary Medicine (PVM) invites applications for the position of Department Head, Comparative Pathobiology. The department seeks a dynamic leader with creative vision and an outstanding record of research, administration, and teaching. Reporting to the Dean of Veterinary Medicine, the successful applicant will work alongside talented faculty, promote collaboration across disciplines, and play a crucial role in shaping the future of veterinary and graduate education and research in the college. The position comes with several open faculty lines with an opportunity to shape the research and academic environment of the department. Department of Comparative Pathobiology Overview Our faculty and staff educate professional and graduate students in pathology, microbiology, virology, parasitology, immunology, toxicology, epidemiology and animal welfare science. Collaborative and cutting-edge research in the department is broadly aligned with Purdue’s One Health initiative ( https://www.purdue.edu/onehealth ) that addresses challenges at the intersection of veterinary, human, and environmental health. The department has a strong record of federal funding and innovative research in the areas of antimicrobial resistance, vaccine development, host-pathogen interactions, drug discovery, epidemiology and animal welfare science. Interdisciplinary, collaborative research is supported and encouraged both within the department and the university. Many departmental faculty members play leading roles in Purdue’s interdisciplinary Life Sciences Institutes, including the Purdue Institute of Inflammation, Immunology and Infectious Diseases, and the Purdue Institute for Drug Discovery. The interdisciplinary Center for Animal Welfare Science and Center for the Human-Animal Bond are housed in the department. Our faculty engage in diagnostic service through the Indiana Animal Disease Diagnostic Laboratory and the Clinical Pathology laboratory in the Purdue University Veterinary Hospital. Pathology support for research projects is provided through the Histology Research Laboratory. College of Veterinary Medicine Overview The Department of Comparative Pathobiology is one of three departments in the College of Veterinary Medicine at Purdue University . The College is home to the Purdue Veterinary Hospital and the Indiana Animal Disease Diagnostic Laboratory . Our college prides itself on its welcoming environment that values individuals who bring passion and vision to their work. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Leadership & Strategic Vision: Provide dynamic and forward-thinking leadership in support of existing research programs and developing new growth areas; Lead the recruitment, mentoring and retention of high-achieving faculty; Develop and implement strategic goals in alignment with the school’s mission and long-term objectives. Advocate for the department’s priorities and needs to internal and external stakeholders; Promote an environment of collaboration, academic excellence, and innovation. Departmental Administration: Oversee day-to-day operations, including managing the department’s faculty, staff, and budget; Ensure efficient faculty workload distribution and optimize teaching assignments. Academic Leadership & Curriculum Development: Contribute to the implementation and evaluation of a high-quality veterinary curriculum; Lead periodic curriculum reviews, ensuring alignment with accreditation standards and student needs; Lead and support the department graduate program. Support faculty and staff providing veterinary diagnostic services. Faculty Development & Recruitment Hire, mentor, and evaluate faculty, fostering a culture of professional growth and academic success; Facilitate faculty success through targeted professional development and leadership opportunities; Foster faculty professional development through mentoring, evaluations, and promotion and tenure processes. Required Qualifications A doctoral degree (DVM, PhD, or equivalent) in a field aligned with the research interests in the department; An outstanding record of scholarly achievement and extramural funding commensurate with the rank of full professor at Purdue; Proven leadership abilities in a DVM program or related field; Commitment to excellence in professional and graduate education; Strong interpersonal and communication skills with dedication to building an inclusive and vibrant scientific community; An inspiring vision for the department. Applications We encourage qualified candidates to submit application materials online at https://vet.purdue.edu/about/careers.php , including a letter of application that describes qualifications for the position, curriculum vitae, names of three references, and statement of administrative philosophy. Review of applications will occur on a rolling basis and will continue until the position is filled. Questions should be directed to CPB Head Search Committee, Department of Comparative Pathobiology, Purdue University, 725 Harrison Street, West Lafayette, IN 47907 or anscheur@purdue.edu. A background check is required for employment in this position. EEO/AA Statement Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 12/18/25 Search Jobs Job Alerts Link Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Visiting-Assistant-Professor-of-Computer-Science/36772-en_US": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Computer Science",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Computer Science Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 36772 Job Title: Visiting Assistant Professor of Computer Science City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary AI Forge, Purdue University’s new initiative in generative artificial intelligence (GenAI), seeks a highly dynamic Visiting Faculty to join our interdisciplinary team for a transformative one-year term. This role is tailored for scholars passionate about shaping the future of AI through research, education, and collaboration at one of the nation’s leading institutions. As a Visiting Faculty member, you will architect curricula and teach courses that inspire the next generation of AI leaders, mentor students on groundbreaking research projects with access to state-of-the-art GPU hardware, forge partnerships with industry and academia, and contribute to AI Forge’s mission of advancing GenAI across disciplines. Your work will bridge theory and practice, driving impactful discoveries while nurturing a vibrant intellectual community. To apply, submit a cover letter, CV, teaching philosophy, and up to three references. Applications will be reviewed starting 11/17/2025 (November 17th, 2025) and on an ongoing basis until the position is filled. Eligible for a one-year renewal term. A background check is required for employment in this position. Education We invite applications from individuals with a Ph.D. in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, or related fields, completed by the start date. Experience A strong foundation in core AI methodologies—machine learning, deep learning, NLP—coupled with hands-on expertise in Python, PyTorch, and large language model pipelines is essential. Exceptional communication skills and a commitment to fostering interdisciplinary innovation are paramount. Prior teaching, mentoring, or project leadership experience, while not required, will strengthen your application. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access institution. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/4/25 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Director-All-American-Marching-Band%2C-Clinical-Associate-or-Clinical-Full-Professor-of-Bands/38301-en_US": {
      "title": "Director \"All-American\" Marching Band, Clinical Associate or Clinical Full Professor of Bands",
      "description": "Director \"All-American\" Marching Band, Clinical Associate or Clinical Full Professor of Bands Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 38301 Job Title: Director \"All-American\" Marching Band, Clinical Associate or Clinical Full Professor of Bands City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Position: Clinical Associate or Clinical Full Professor. (or) Associate or Full Professor with Tenure Title: Director “All-American” Marching Band Term: FY 12 month contract. Start Date: 7/1/2026 Salary Range: $92,000-$120,000 About the position: Purdue University’s Department of Bands and Orchestras invites applications for the position of the 6th Director of the Purdue “All-American” Marching Band at the rank of Clinical Associate or Full Professor. If the applicant has achieved tenure at their current institution, employment may be offered at tenure-track Associate or Full Professor, depending on the candidate’s qualification. This faculty member will serve as Director of the “All-American” Marching Band and will be responsible for total administration of the organization. Candidates will demonstrate a strong background in music, music education and a passion for college marching band. They must also demonstrate a strong commitment to creating a student-centered environment. Successful candidates will show a willingness to maintain the rich traditions of the Purdue “All-American” Marching Band while sharing their vision for elevating the program. The ideal candidate must also demonstrate the appropriate personality, charisma, and media awareness required as the forward-facing leader of Purdue University’s most visible ensemble to the university community, prospective students, alumni, parents, and friends. Primary Responsibilities Direct the “All-American” Marching Band. The flagship ensemble of Purdue Bands and Orchestras is wholly inclusive of all performing instrumentalists, the “World’s Largest Bass Drum” Crew, Golduster Dance Team, Golden Silks Color Guard, and “All-American” Twirling program Administrate all activities of the “All-American” Marching Band, including Band Camp, rehearsals, performances, Homecoming Alumni Marching Band, yearly rehearsal/performance calendar, travel, extra performances (Indianapolis 500) and more Work cohesively with all “All-American” Marching Band faculty/staff to coordinate activities related to the band and its auxiliary organizations Coordinate show selection, drill design, music arrangements, and licensing Work closely with Purdue Athletics to coordinate activities during home game days Contribute to departmental and university service, including recruiting marching and athletic band members Develop and implement strategies for recruitment and retention of marching and athletic band participants Supervise student leadership team for the logistical operation of the marching band Additional Responsibilities Direct one of three pep bands Conduct a concert band(s) during the second semester Additional responsibilities as assigned by chair Education Masters Required (doctorate preferred) Experience Successful marching band teaching experience at the college/university level Minimum of 5 years of full-time college/university teaching experience Minimum 3 years of public school teaching experience Applicants will submit the following through Successfactors: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Complete contact information for three current professional references Review of Applications: Screening of applicants will begin September 8, 2025 and continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. For additional information or if you have further questions, contact the search committee chair, Dr. David Blon, via email at dblon@purdue.edu FLSA Status Exempt Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 8/20/25 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Professor-Research-Assistant/36790-en_US": {
      "title": "Professor Research Assistant",
      "description": "Professor Research Assistant Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 36790 Job Title: Professor Research Assistant City: West Lafayette Job Description: Position Summary: The Department of Entomology at Purdue University invites applications for a non-tenure track Assistant/Associate Research Professor, Biology and Management of Urban Pests. The successful candidate will engage with the national pest management industry and conduct high-impact research in one or more areas of basic and applied urban pest management , with an emphasis on pests of built environments such as cockroaches and bed bugs. Research could encompass the biology and behavior of pests, their response to pesticides, including physiological and genetic mechanisms of resistance, innovations in applied pest management research ( e.g., molecular, computational modeling, or artificial intelligence based approaches) and the development of sustainable pest management technologies. The successful candidate will become an integral member of the Center for Urban and Industrial Pest Management ( CUIPM ) which is nationally recognized for leadership in urban entomology. The position will synergize a number of related urban entomology faculty and programs at Purdue and engage with stakeholder groups to address pressing issues associated with urban pests. This is a nine-month appointment with a focus on research and minor instructional responsibilities. The position may contribute to undergraduate learning through research experiential courses (ENTM 39300 Insect Biology Practicum and ENTM 49300 Insect Biology Capstone) , and training and mentorship of graduate students, postdoctoral and visiting scientists. Start date may be as early as 1 June, 2025. Responsibilities: Lead a nationally recognized research program focused on the basic biology of urban pests and advancement of modern, sustainable pest management solutions and technologies. Secure external funding through grants, industry contracts and partnerships to support ongoing research Publish research findings in peer-reviewed journals and present results at national and international conferences. Organize and lead seminars, workshops and industry-specific training sessions to disseminate research findings and best practices for indoor pest management. Maintain ongoing communication with stakeholders to foster collaborations, gather feedback on research priorities and ensure that research is aligned with industry needs and challenges. Represent the CUIPM at industry meetings and conferences to promote research capabilities and develop new collaborations. Work synergistically with faculty from within the department of entomology and across the university to further elevate discovery. Mentor graduate students, postdoctoral scientists and visiting scholars and contribute to the achievement of instructional outcomes by supporting undergraduate student training. Qualifications Ph.D. and minimum one year postdoctoral training in entomology or related discipline. Experience in computational modeling and artificial intelligence is desirable. Records of excellence in research, publication, project management, and mentoring required. Inter-disciplinary research experience, the ability to interact with a broad spectrum of researchers and clientele groups, and willingness to engage the urban pest management industry are highly desirable. Salary and Benefits: This is a 9-month non-tenure track position with a focus on research. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Excellent fringe benefit package that includes Fidelity retirement program, medical, and life and disability insurance. Opportunities for promotion within the research faculty are available, and more information can be found in the Procedures for Research Faculty Appointment, Review, and Promotion linked here: Office of the Provost - Purdue University https://www.purdue.edu/provost/policies/promotion-research.html . To Apply: Applications should include a cover letter addressing the applicant’s qualifications and experience, a statement of research goals, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. All materials must be combined into one PDF and submitted electronically via this site: https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Professor-Research-Assistant/36790-en_US/ Application review will begin May 12th and continue until a successful candidate is identified. For more information, please contact the Search Committee Chairs, Dr. Jose Pietri ( jpietric@purdue.edu ) and Dr. Douglas Richmond ( drichmond@purdue.edu ). The Department is an integral part of the College of Agriculture, one of the world’s leading colleges of agricultural, food, life, and natural resource sciences and ranked fifth in the world in the 2024 QS World University Rankings. The College is deeply committed to the three land-grant missions (teaching, research, and extension), to international activities and perspectives that span all missions, and to excellence in all we do.  The College has 11 academic departments, 290 faculty, 2984 undergraduate students, and 690 graduate students. A background check is required for employment in this position Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 4/14/25 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/SoET-Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor-One-Health-Cluster-Hire/44427-en_US": {
      "title": "SoET Tenure-Track Assistant Professor One Health Cluster Hire",
      "description": "SoET Tenure-Track Assistant Professor One Health Cluster Hire Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44427 Job Title: SoET Tenure-Track Assistant Professor One Health Cluster Hire City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary As part of a transformative, university-wide initiative in One Health - Healthy and Resilient Living Systems , the School of Engineering Technology (SoET) in the Purdue Polytechnic Institute invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. Specifically, SoET seeks candidates to design, integrate and deploy intelligent physical and digital technologies into scalable systems for health. The successful candidate will complement SoET's strengths in intelligent manufacturing, sensing, electronics, artificial intelligence, automation and robotics, and industrial systems.  Applications from individuals with cross-cutting industry experience in healthcare, manufacturing, embedded systems and robotics are welcome. Areas of Research Interest Research Areas of interest include, but are not limited to the following: Intelligent manufacturing of medical and health technologies. Automation and robotics for healthcare, laboratory and pharmaceutical processes. Digital twins and cyber-physical systems for health applications. Intelligent sensors including wireless technologies for physiological monitoring, communication and power for wearable/implantable devices. AI-enabled health monitoring, diagnostics and decision-support systems including Human-machine interaction and human factors in health systems. Low-power and embedded systems for health applications, Therapeutic devices and systems. Smart Assistive Robotics. Smart Wearables & Flexible Biosensors. Human-Collaborative Clinical Devices. Ambient & Passive Monitoring Devices. About the School The School of Engineering Technology (SoET) at Purdue University is home to approximately 1500 students, as well as more than 70 faculty and 20 staff members across West Lafayette, Indianapolis and Purdue Polytechnic Statewide. The School prepares students to design, integrate and deploy solutions that work in the real world, with strengths in electrical, mechanical, manufacturing and industrial engineering technology. Through applied engineering education, translational research, advanced laboratories and industry partnerships, SoET is building a distinctive environment focused on intelligent manufacturing and industrial systems. Purdue's One Health Initiative This strategic recruitment will help advance Purdue’s One Health initiative ( https://www.purdue.edu/onehealth/ ) which seeks to tackle complex challenges with real-world impact at the intersection of human, animal, and plant health. This recruitment initiative builds on previous strategic faculty recruitment initiatives in: (1) Integrated Health; (2) AI-Driven Biomolecular Design, and (3) Advanced Chemistry. In addition, a parallel strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Intelligent Medicines is ongoing. Through academic programs, research, facility infrastructure and industry partnerships, Purdue’s One Health efforts are making giant leaps in improving health outcomes for all living things and driving economic growth regionally and globally. This strategic faculty recruitment initiative focused on Healthy and Resilient Living Systems is expected to build on prior recruitment initiatives and existing Purdue research and academic strengths, to transform research and impact human, animal and environmental health by bridging silos and fostering collaboration across disciplines. The health and prosperity of society depend upon resilient living systems that connect ecosystems, plants, animals, insects, microbes, and people. Emerging and chronic diseases, food insecurity, environmental degradation, climate change, nutrient deficiencies, invasive species, and ecosystem disruption are increasingly interconnected challenges that require integrated approaches across biological scales and disciplinary boundaries. This strategic recruitment initiative will help establish Purdue as a national leader in predicting, designing, and improving living systems that support health, sustainability, and economic vitality. Working with existing campus experts, this cluster would develop innovative solutions that enhance health resilience from genes and microbiomes to organisms, food systems, populations, and ecosystems. By integrating strengths in agriculture, engineering, artificial intelligence, data science, and health sciences, Purdue aims to create a globally distinctive platform for addressing complex challenges at the intersection of food systems, environmental stewardship, animal and human health, and economic prosperity. Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D. in engineering technology, engineering, computer science, or a related discipline. Faculty Responsibilities Establish a vigorous, externally funded research program Contribute to the education and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students Teach graduate and undergraduate courses Collaborate across disciplines to solve complex global one health challenges Integration within the Purdue One Health Community Collectively, the strategic faculty recruitment initiatives represent a forward-thinking investment in Purdue’s research infrastructure and academic excellence. Faculty hired as part of these One Health strategic faculty recruitment initiatives will be supported as part of the overall One Health community. Together, these faculty members are expected to work across diverse disciplines, enhance Purdue’s external funding potential, and drive innovation at the intersection of health, environment, food, and economics. In addition to joining an academic unit, faculty hired under this initiative will have the opportunity to join a vibrant ecosystem of interdisciplinary centers and institutes, that span the hard tech corridor between Indianapolis and West Lafayette. Furthermore, with Purdue's expanding presence in Indianapolis, including Purdue University in Indianapolis, faculty will have additional opportunities for collaboration with clinical, industry, and translational partners. The integrated, cross-disciplinary nature of One Health is essential for addressing today’s most urgent One Health challenges and ensuring Purdue’s continued leadership in research, education, and community impact. Application Process All candidates must apply through SuccessFactors and include: 1) a cover letter, 2) a resume or CV, 3) a clear statement of teaching and research interests, and 4) a list of five professional references with contact information. Screening will begin November 13, 2026 and conclude when the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/16/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Biomedical-Engineering-%28Indianapolis%29/44402-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Biomedical Engineering (Indianapolis)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Biomedical Engineering (Indianapolis) Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44402 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Biomedical Engineering (Indianapolis) City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The Weldon School of Biomedical Engineering at Purdue University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. The successful candidate will join the Weldon School of Biomedical Engineering in Indianapolis, Indiana. This position represents an exciting opportunity to contribute to the expansion of Purdue Engineering in Indianapolis at the heart of Indiana's life sciences ecosystem, where engineering, medicine, and translational research converge. Successful candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Materials Science and Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or another closely related discipline, by the employment date. Candidates should have expertise in one or more areas related to musculoskeletal health, biomechanics, tissue engineering, neural engineering, neurotechnology, imaging, sports engineering and human performance engineering .  Early-career applicants should show evidence of initiating independent research, while mid-career applicants should demonstrate a sustained record of independent research within academic or industrial organizations, and contributions to education and/or mentoring. Individuals working at the interface of engineering and medicine - particularly those who can bridge disciplines and approaches (e.g. computational modeling, imaging, and experimental or clinical applications) - are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate is expected to develop and sustain an independent, externally funded research program, mentor graduate and undergraduate students, teach courses at both levels, and contribute to service at the School, College, and University levels. Collaboration with clinical partners at the Indiana University School of Medicine and industry partners in the One Health Innovation District is highly encouraged and supported. School and College Biomedical engineering at Purdue has a 50+ years of history, beginning with the Biomedical Engineering Center in 1974. The program became the Department of Biomedical Engineering in 1998 and was elevated to the Weldon School of Biomedical Engineering in 2004. The Weldon School is now home to over 700 students, 45 primary faculty, 100 affiliated faculty, 2,300 alumni, and more than 100,000 ft² of laboratory space. Annual research expenditures exceed $20 million, with sustained support from NIH, NSF, DoD, and industry sponsors. The School has a strong record of translation and innovation , with over 100 U.S. patents, $35+ million in licensing royalties, and more than 30 startup companies that have impacted millions of patients worldwide. As part of Purdue Engineering , one of the nation’s largest and top-ranked colleges of engineering, the Weldon School benefits from the University’s major investments in initiatives such as One Health, Purdue Computes, the Institute for Physical AI, the Daniels School of Business and Purdue University in Indianapolis —a fully integrated extension of the West Lafayette flagship campus. These initiatives provide unprecedented opportunities for translational biomedical research through proximity to hospitals, medical research facilities, and Indiana’s vibrant biotechnology and medical device industries. Our growing Indianapolis presence also offers opportunities to collaborate with emerging and thriving College of Engineering programs in Gaming and Interactive Systems Engineering, Motorsports Engineering, and Human Performance Engineering. Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 8 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering continues to remain a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world. More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Purdue Engineering in Indianapolis serves as a hub for interdisciplinary collaboration focused on improving human health through highly innovative and multidisciplinary research and educational programs. The college and the Weldon School’s strategic partnerships with IU School of Medicine, Eli Lilly and Company, Zimmer Biomet, Cook and BioCrossroads advance the state’s leadership in biomedical devices and health innovation. Application Process To apply, please submit an application to this site including (1) cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a research plan of up to 3 pages, (4) a teaching plan of up to 2 pages, and (5) names and contact information for at least four references. For questions regarding applications, contact Engineering Academic Affairs, Purdue Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on Nov 16, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/15/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Energy-&-Environment-Engineering-%28Indianapolis%29/44400-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Energy & Environment - Engineering (Indianapolis)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Energy & Environment - Engineering (Indianapolis) Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44400 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Energy & Environment - Engineering (Indianapolis) City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary Purdue University invites applications for multiple tenured/tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor positions in energy and environment through a cluster search involving the School of Mechanical Engineering (ME), the Elmore Family School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE), and the School of Sustainability Engineering and Environmental Engineering (SEE). Successful candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Environmental Engineering, or a closely related discipline by the employment start date. Early-career applicants should show evidence of initiating independent research, while mid-career applicants should demonstrate a sustained record of independent research within academic or industrial organizations and contributions to education and/or mentoring. The successful candidate will conduct original research, advise graduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, and perform service at the School, College, and University levels. Applicants interested in a position in any of Purdue’s engineering schools are welcome to apply. The location of this position, including teaching responsibilities, is in Indianapolis. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: thermal management, heat and mass transport phenomena, energy conversion, renewable and sustainable energy systems,  and energy storage and batteries (ME); power electronics, electric machines and drives, electrification, renewable energy integration, and modeling, optimization, and control of resilient electric grids and distributed energy resources (ECE); and life cycle engineering and assessment, sustainable energy and industrial systems, environmental impacts of energy technologies, circular materials and resource recovery, end-of-use product value recovery, carbon management, and technologies addressing the energy-water-environment nexus (SEE). Across all three schools, we welcome expertise addressing the energy and environmental challenges of data centers and semiconductor technologies, including thermal management and cooling, power delivery and energy efficiency, water use and reuse, and sustainable semiconductor manufacturing, including process chemistry and materials recovery. Research that connects these areas across the participating schools is encouraged. Purdue University in Indianapolis anchors the southern end of Indiana’s Hard-Tech Corridor , connecting Indianapolis and West Lafayette. Purdue’s expansion in Indianapolis is guided by a 50-year campus master plan to provide new academic and research facilities, industry collaboration, and experiential learning. Faculty in Indianapolis are part of Purdue’s broader research community, with opportunities for collaboration across facilities including the Ray W. Herrick Laboratories, Maurice J. Zucrow Laboratories, Maha Fluid Power Research Center, Center for Advances in Resilient Energy Storage (CARES), FLEX Lab, Grainger Energy Conversion and Microgrid Laboratory, and Birck Nanotechnology Center. Purdue's Institute for Energy Innovation (IEI) brings together faculty, students, and industry partners to advance abundant, reliable, and affordable energy through interdisciplinary research, education, and the translation of discoveries into practical technologies. Purdue University's Institute for a Sustainable Future (ISF) promotes interdisciplinary research, partnership, and engagement to solve global sustainability challenges. College of Engineering Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 8 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering is a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit applications to this site including (1) a cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a 2-page teaching plan, (4) a 3-page research plan, and (5) names and contact information for at least 5 references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For information/questions regarding applications, contact the Office of Academic Affairs, College of Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026. Applications received by December 20, 2026, will be given full consideration. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/15/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Biological-Sciences/44500-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Biological Sciences Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44500 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Biological Sciences City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Description Strategic Faculty Recruitment Initiative in One Health - Healthy and Resilient Living Systems - Quantitative Neuroscience, Department of Biological Sciences Purdue University Main Campus | Indianapolis and West Lafayette, IN Tenure-Track/Tenured Faculty Positions at Assistant and Associate Ranks As part of a transformative, university-wide initiative in One Health - Healthy and Resilient Living Systems, the Purdue University Department of Biological Sciences invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level with a focus on Quantitative Neuroscience. We seek an innovative experimental neuroscientist who uses scalable approaches to generate and computationally analyze rich, high-dimensional measurements of neural phenotypes. The ideal candidate will investigate how the nervous system maintains, adapts, or loses resilience during development, physiological stress, aging, or disease. We welcome applications from scientists using diverse, scalable experimental strategies to measure neural phenotypes across spatial and organizational scales, from molecules and synapses to cells, circuits, and intact nervous systems. Biological models may include single cells, primary neuronal cultures, three-dimensional organoids, or in vivo preparations. Areas of Research Interest Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: •    High-throughput phenotyping using automated microscopy, image-based profiling, or optical pooled screening. •    Advanced functional imaging of neural activity in live cells, deep tissues, or intact circuits. •    Multimodal and spatial omics linked to cellular phenotypes or states. •    Novel tool development, including optical, molecular, or screening tools that enable scalable quantitative measurement and perturbation of neural cells and systems. Opportunities for Synergy and Collaboration The Department of Biological Sciences is the largest department in the Life Sciences at Purdue, with a strong neuroscience and physiology community and research spanning biological scales from molecules to ecosystems. This position builds on Purdue’s established leadership in artificial intelligence, computational biology, and neuroscience; world-leading expertise in quantitative imaging and image-based profiling, including the Cells to Cures Engine; and the Department’s recent expansion in multi-omics and human stem cell biology. The successful candidate will join a highly dynamic and collaborative community of researchers with access to world-class core facilities, including those at the Bindley Bioscience Center. Purdue’s One Health Initiative This strategic recruitment will help advance Purdue’s One Health initiative ( https://www.purdue.edu/onehealth/) which seeks to tackle complex challenges with real-world impact at the intersection of human, animal, and plant health. This recruitment initiative builds on previous strategic faculty recruitment initiatives in: (1) Integrated Health; (2) AI-Driven Biomolecular Design, and (3) Advanced Chemistry. In addition, a parallel strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Intelligent Medicines is ongoing. Through academic programs, research, facility infrastructure and industry partnerships, Purdue’s One Health efforts are making giant leaps in improving health outcomes for all living things and driving economic growth regionally and globally. This strategic faculty recruitment initiative focused on Healthy and Resilient Living Systems is expected to build on prior recruitment initiatives and existing Purdue research and academic strengths, to transform research and impact human, animal and environmental health by bridging silos and fostering collaboration across disciplines. The health and prosperity of society depend upon resilient living systems that connect ecosystems, plants, animals, insects, microbes, and people. Emerging and chronic diseases, food insecurity, environmental degradation, climate change, nutrient deficiencies, invasive species, and ecosystem disruption are increasingly interconnected challenges that require integrated approaches across biological scales and disciplinary boundaries. This strategic recruitment initiative will help establish Purdue as a national leader in predicting, designing, and improving living systems that support health, sustainability, and economic vitality. Working with existing campus experts, this cluster would develop innovative solutions that enhance health resilience from genes and microbiomes to organisms, food systems, populations, and ecosystems. By integrating strengths in agriculture, engineering, artificial intelligence, data science, and health sciences, Purdue aims to create a globally distinctive platform for addressing complex challenges at the intersection of food systems, environmental stewardship, animal and human health, and economic prosperity. Qualifications A PhD degree in Biological Sciences or related field by the employment start date A record of research excellence and productivity commensurate with rank Demonstrated potential or record of interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship Commitment to teaching and student mentorship Faculty Responsibilities Establish a vigorous, externally funded research program Teach undergraduate and/or graduate level courses in Biological Sciences. Mentor graduate and undergraduate students Participate in service at the departmental, college, and university level Collaborate across disciplines to solve complex global one health challenges Integration within the Purdue One Health Community Collectively, the strategic faculty recruitment initiatives represent a forward-thinking investment in Purdue’s research infrastructure and academic excellence. Faculty hired as part of these One Health strategic faculty recruitment initiatives will be supported as part of the overall One Health community. Together, these faculty members are expected to work across diverse disciplines, enhance Purdue’s external funding potential, and drive innovation at the intersection of health, environment, food, and economics. In addition to joining an academic unit, faculty hired under this initiative will have the opportunity to join a vibrant ecosystem of interdisciplinary centers and institutes, that span the hard tech corridor between Indianapolis and West Lafayette including: Translational Neurocircuitry Initiative Purdue Institute for Physical Artificial Intelligence , Purdue Institute for Drug Discovery Center for Aging and the Life Course (CALC) Furthermore, with Purdue's expanding presence in Indianapolis, including Purdue University in Indianapolis and the surrounding hard tech corridor, faculty will have additional opportunities for collaboration with clinical, industry, and translational partners. The integrated, cross-disciplinary nature of One Health is essential for addressing today’s most urgent One Health challenges and ensuring Purdue’s continued leadership in research, education, and community impact. Application Process To apply, please submit a cover letter, CV, research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin by November 15, 2026, and continue until positions are filled. Applications should be submitted at: Application link to apply . A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/15/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Actuarial-Sciences/44027-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Actuarial Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Actuarial Sciences Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44027 Job Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Actuarial Sciences City: INDIANAPOLIS Job Description: Job Summary The College of Science at Purdue University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Actuarial Science at the assistant or associate professor level, based at Purdue’s Indianapolis campus. Purdue’s Actuarial Science program, jointly administered by the Department of Mathematics and the Department of Statistics, is nationally recognized for excellence in actuarial education. This position is part of an initiative to expand the program to the Indianapolis campus, including the recruitment of additional instructional faculty to support and advance the program’s teaching mission. Purdue University in Indianapolis is a new, fully integrated expansion of the West Lafayette campus, extending to central Indiana the academic rigor and accessible excellence for which Purdue is known. As the state’s only public top-10 university, most trusted university, and most innovative university, Purdue is focused on strengthening its presence in Indiana’s industrial and technological center. Purdue in Indianapolis is creating an innovative, STEM-based collegiate experience by connecting future-ready students and faculty with local businesses to accelerate Indiana’s STEM pipeline and technology ecosystem, fueling impact for our region and the world. Learn more about Purdue’s latest giant leap at: https://www.purdue.edu/campuses/indianapolis/ . Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in actuarial science, mathematics, statistics, or a closely related field by August 16, 2027, and have demonstrated excellence in research and a strong commitment to teaching. Outstanding applicants in all areas of actuarial science will be considered, including, but not limited to, probability, risk measurement, stochastic modeling, data science, and the broader mathematical and computational sciences. Preference will be given to candidates who are willing to acquire experience with, or who already have experience with, the examination system that governs the actuarial profession. Principal Duties Successful candidates will be expected to develop research programs in their fields of expertise, teach courses in actuarial science, develop an external funding portfolio, build connections with the actuarial profession, and participate in the program, college, and broader university activities. The Program and College Purdue’s Actuarial Science program is recognized as a Center of Actuarial Excellence by the Society of Actuaries. The program offers a stimulating academic environment that connects research areas with the actuarial profession. With over 300 undergraduate students and a thriving partnership with Purdue’s Data Mine learning community, the program is also tightly coupled with some of Purdue’s fastest-growing majors, such as Data Science. Actuarial Science is part of the College of Science, which encompasses the mathematical, computational, physical, and life sciences at Purdue. The College is the second-largest at Purdue with over 350 faculty members and more than 7,000 students. The College is pursuing significant new initiatives that align with campus-wide plans, with data science among its strategic priorities. Opportunities for collaboration span mathematics, probability, statistics, the physical and life sciences, as well as the newly reimagined School of Business and Purdue’s burgeoning campus presence in the center of Indianapolis. For more information about Purdue’s Actuarial Science program, see https://www.science.purdue.edu/actuarial-science/ . Application Procedure Applications should be submitted online through www.mathjobs.org and should include (1) a cover letter, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a research statement, (4) a teaching statement, and (5) four letters of recommendation, one of which should address the candidate’s teaching qualifications. Reference letter writers should submit their letters online through www.mathjobs.org . Inquiries may be directed to Dr. Haibo Liu at haiboliu@purdue.edu. Applications will be considered on a continuing basis, but candidates are encouraged to apply by January 10, 2027, for full consideration. A background check will be required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/28/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice/44633-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Practice Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44633 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Practice City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The Bowen School of Construction | Purdue Polytechnic (BSC) at Purdue University in Indianapolis invites applications for a full-time appointment at either the Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice level in the area of Interior Architecture. The Professor of Practice position is contractual non-tenure accruing, but renewable, with the position holder having voting faculty status and potential for promotion through established policies. This position will be at the Indianapolis, Indiana campus beginning in August 2027. Teaching Expectations BSC resides in Purdue Polytechnic at Purdue University (PPI), one of the 10 academic colleges. Polytechnic uses innovative learning methods, real-world experiences, and industry partnerships to produce graduates uniquely qualified for technology-driven careers. This position requires faculty to have both high technical competence and the ability and desire to teach in active classrooms. We are looking for a candidate to teach students in our Interior Architecture degree program. The primary assignment focuses on instruction and industry engagement, with a secondary role that interfaces with external clients to establish relationships with companies that will engage our students at some level. In addition to teaching, the candidate will be expected to aid in curriculum development for the Interior Architecture program. The candidate may also participate and integrate their professional experience with architecture and interior design associations, industry activities, service and engagement, and participate in scholarly activities of engagement and learning. The School The Bowen School of Construction (BSC) is celebrating over 60 years of construction education excellence and Purdue University was recently ranked #7 among public institutions in the U.S. by the Wall Street Journal. BSC has campuses in both West Lafayette and Indianapolis Indiana.  The school has a vibrant research and teaching culture with over 500 undergraduate students and over 100 graduate students.  Undergraduate programs include degrees in construction management, design and construction integration, virtual design and construction, and interior architecture. The school resides in the Purdue Polytechnic Institute that recently transformed undergraduate curriculums to incorporate innovative learning environments, strong industry involvement, and team teaching in active learning classrooms. Education & Experience Applicants must have a minimum of an M.S. in Architecture, Interior Design, or a related discipline. Applicants must also have documented, full-time, industry experience which must include a minimum of 4 years in the U.S. architecture or interior design industries. Preferred candidates will be ARE or NCIDQ certified as well as retain previous teaching experience. The successful applicant will have expertise in some (but not necessarily all) of the following core course areas: software applications for the built environment which include AutoCAD, Revit, Sketchup and associated design visualization programs, residential construction, commercial construction, interior materials, three-dimensional design, building systems, and sustainable design. Application Procedure All candidates must apply through SuccessFactors and include: 1) a cover letter, 2) a resume or CV, 3) a clear statement of teaching, and 4) a list of names and contact information for three potential reviewers. Job Link: https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice/44633-en_US/ Screening will begin on December 1, 2027, and conclude when the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. This position will be based in Indianapolis, IN. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/26/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor%2C-MIS/44668-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, MIS",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor, MIS Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44668 Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor, MIS City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Daniels School of Business (DSB) at Purdue University invites applications for a Clinical Assistant Professor position beginning in Fall 2027. The primary responsibilities will be teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in the business applications of information technology, including artificial intelligence (AI) and technology transformation. Qualified candidates must: demonstrate preparation to teach business applications of information technology through relevant academic training, teaching experience, or professional experience. hold a master’s degree or higher in information systems, computer science, or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment. demonstrate subject-matter knowledge relevant to the courses to be taught, including business applications of AI or digital technology. The successful candidate will teach courses related to business applications of AI and information technology. Depending on departmental needs, course topics may include digital transformation, technology governance and regulation, the digital economy, and emerging technologies and business models. The position may also involve developing experiential learning opportunities and collaborating with external organizations on student projects. Relevant industry experience may inform these activities but is not a minimum qualification. In addition to teaching, the successful candidate will be expected to contribute service to the Department, School, and University through committee work, administrative support, leadership activities, and other forms of academic and institutional engagement. Application instruction Applicants should submit the following: cover letter highlighting specific strengths relative to the position and areas of opportunity identified above CV evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., course evaluations, teaching awards, etc.), if available statement of teaching philosophy list of recently taught courses three names for recommendation letter writers submitted here: https://apps.it.purdue.edu/KARS/Apply/HNoUdIm1KR Questions and correspondences should be addressed to Joe Mazur at mazur3@purdue.edu .  Review of applications will begin December 1, 2026 and the position will remain open until filled. About the organization The Daniels School of Business is built upon Purdue’s mission as a land-grant university to provide affordable and accessible education while combining technological excellence and business expertise. There are many opportunities to collaborate with the nation’s 4th-ranking Purdue Engineering and the top-ranking Purdue Computes disciplines. Purdue University and the Daniels School of Business are committed to free and open inquiry in all matters. Candidates are encouraged to address in their cover letter how they are prepared to contribute to a climate that values free inquiry and academic freedom. A background check will be required for employment in the position. For a complete list of benefits, please visit our website at: https://www.purdue.edu/hr/Benefits/ . Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Computational-Agricultural-and-Natural-Systems-Modeling/44631-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Computational Agricultural and Natural Systems Modeling",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Computational Agricultural and Natural Systems Modeling Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44631 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Computational Agricultural and Natural Systems Modeling City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Purdue University College of Agriculture seeks applicants for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Computational Agricultural and Natural Systems Modeling.  This is a full-time (9-month) position with an appointment in research and teaching. The successful candidate will be appointed in an appropriate academic department within the College of Agriculture, based on their disciplinary expertise and research program. The position is intended for a scholar who can develop and lead a rigorous computational research program to improve the performance and resilience of agricultural, food, biological, environmental, and natural-resource systems. We seek candidates whose research advances the understanding, prediction, design, or management of complex systems through mechanistic, statistical, data-driven, or hybrid modeling approaches and advanced computational methods. The successful candidate should be able to develop new models, computational methods, data integration pipelines, and decision-support frameworks for agricultural and related systems. The candidate's program should draw on quantitative methods such as modeling, optimization, decision science, artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning, bioinformatics, or related computational approaches. Within the context of agricultural, biological, environmental, food, and natural-resource systems, we are looking for candidates with experience in one or more of the following areas: Modeling and predictive science Mechanistic, statistical, and hybrid modeling Machine learning and AI Mathematical and computational biology Complex systems, network science, and uncertainty quantification Systems design and decision science Optimization and operations research Decision analysis and risk assessment Digital twins as a decision/optimization framework Scenario analysis and robust decision-making Computational integration and scale Geospatial and spatiotemporal analytics for systems-level decision-making/resource allocation High-performance, cloud computing, and computational/software infrastructure Integration of diverse and large-scale datasets from precision farms Reproducible computational workflows Interoperable models, data, and software architecture Applications of the work could relate to agricultural production and natural systems, plant or animal breeding and genetics, soil health, animal agriculture, insect and disease systems, water resources, forestry, microbiomes, food systems, conservation planning, supply chains, logistics, transportation systems, rural and agricultural communities, agricultural policy, and regional or global food systems. We expect the candidate to build a nationally and internationally recognized research program that advances discovery and delivers robust, decision-ready modeling and computational tools for agricultural, environmental and natural-resource systems. The successful candidate will teach graduate and/or undergraduate courses in areas such as systems modeling, computational science, scientific machine learning, decision analysis, optimization, reproducible computation, or data-model integration. Course modality is generally in person. The potential may exist for teaching online/distance courses during the academic year. The candidate will also mentor students from disciplinary backgrounds who need advanced computational preparation to address agricultural and life-science problems. The College The College of Agriculture is one of the world's leading colleges of agricultural, food, life, and natural-resource sciences. The College is ranked third in the United States and sixth in the world in the 2026 QS World University Rankings. The College is deeply committed to the three land-grant missions of teaching, research, and Extension, to international activities and perspectives that span all missions, and to excellence in all we do. The College has 10 academic departments, 294 faculty, 2,842 undergraduate students, and 694 graduate students. The successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate with faculty affiliated with interdisciplinary initiatives and centers including the Institute for Digital and Advanced Agricultural Systems, Institute for Plant Sciences, Center for Plant Biology, Institute for Digital Forestry, Institute for a Sustainable Future, Indiana Water Resources Research Center, Institute for Physical Artificial Intelligence (IPAI), Purdue Computes, Purdue's One Health Initiative, and a growing ecosystem of AI, computing, sustainability, and resilient systems programs. Qualifications Applicants must possess a Ph.D. degree by the start of appointment in agriculture, animal sciences, forestry and natural resources, biology, bioinformatics, ecology, environmental science, food science, engineering, computer science, data science, robotics, statistics, economics, applied mathematics, operations research, systems science, geography, computational science, quantitative social science, or a related discipline. A record of research excellence and productivity commensurate with rank is required, as well as demonstrated potential for interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship. Optimization, decision science, bioinformatics, quantitative data and statistical methods, systems modeling, and/or computational science should represent a primary thread of the candidate’s research program. Candidates must demonstrate commitment to teaching and student mentorship and show potential to establish an externally funded research program that addresses important agricultural, environmental, biological, food, or natural-resource challenges. Applicants will be evaluated on the significance and originality of their computational scholarship, the strength of their connection to one or more College mission areas, and their potential for collaboration, teaching, mentorship, and external funding—not on coverage of every method or application listed above. Ideal qualifications include experience integrating models, data, software, or computational workflows across disciplines or scales; expertise in biological, agricultural, environmental, economic, social, or engineered systems; and experience working in interdisciplinary teams. Experience with high-performance or cloud computing, optimization methods, and/or decision-analytic frameworks will be also highly valued. Application Process Interested applicants must submit a cover letter indicating the top two preferred department homes in the College of Agriculture (click https://ag.purdue.edu, then departments), curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin on November 30, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications should be submitted at https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Computational-Agricultural-and-Natural-Systems-Modeling/44631-en_US/ . Application materials must be combined into a single PDF and submitted electronically in the CV field on the application site. Contact Matt Ginzel ( mginzel@purdue.edu ) if you have questions. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor-of-Animal-Sciences/44742-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Animal Sciences",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Animal Sciences Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44742 Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor of Animal Sciences City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor of Animal Sciences – Applied Animal Sciences Position The Department of Animal Sciences at Purdue University invites applications for a Clinical Assistant Professor (100% teaching; non-tenure track) with teaching and mentoring responsibilities in applied animal sciences. This is a nine-month appointment, with opportunities for additional compensated summer teaching or instructional activities. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate instruction in one or more areas of departmental need, with particular emphasis on animal products/meat science and/or animal physiology/reproductive management. Additional opportunities may exist in animal behavior and well-being, animal health, and other areas of the Animal Sciences curriculum. The position offers an opportunity to take a leadership role in experiential education and contribute to the continued development of the largest undergraduate program in Purdue's College of Agriculture. Responsibilities Clinical faculty are primarily responsible for leading and supporting the program’s needs in student instruction (9 – 12 credit hours/semester depending on laboratory sections), engagement, and/or professional development. Students may include both residential students on the West Lafayette campus and students enrolled in online or other non-residential programs. The successful candidate will be expected to: Develop, implement, and teach undergraduate courses in areas aligned with the candidate's expertise and departmental instructional needs, particularly animal products/meat science and/or animal physiology and reproductive physiology; Contribute to foundational Animal Sciences instruction and provide hands-on laboratory and experiential learning opportunities appropriate to the candidate's disciplinary expertise; Mentor undergraduate students in their academic and professional development and contribute to experiential and career-readiness opportunities; Contribute to departmental strategic initiatives to improve teaching approaches and delivery methodologies across teaching modalities in support of curricular outcomes, including career readiness and data literacy; and Engage in service and outreach responsibilities within and outside the Department. Qualifications PhD in animal sciences, meat science, reproductive physiology, animal physiology, animal behavior/welfare, or a closely related field, or a DVM; degree requirements must be completed by the start of the appointment. Candidates must demonstrate disciplinary expertise relevant to one or more of the Department's instructional needs and the ability to contribute effectively to undergraduate teaching. Preferred qualifications include experience teaching applied animal science courses, experience with hands-on laboratory or experiential instruction, and demonstrated ability to mentor undergraduate students. Candidates with expertise that enables them to contribute across multiple areas of the undergraduate curriculum are particularly encouraged to apply. Rank and Appointment Clinical Assistant Professor appointment (9-month, non-tenure track). Salary will be commensurate with qualifications. A background check will be required for employment. About the Department of Animal Sciences The Department of Animal Sciences offers the largest undergraduate major (Animal Sciences) in the Purdue University College of Agriculture, and its faculty and staff are highly committed to the learning outcomes of its 844 undergraduate students. The Department includes 22 faculty, 28 professional staff, 55 graduate students and is housed in the Hobart and Russell Creighton Hall of Animal Sciences, a 90,000-square-foot state-of-the-art facility for teaching, Extension, and research. Connected to Creighton Hall is the Land O'Lakes, Inc. Center for Experiential Learning and Purina Pavilion, which provides an abattoir, meats and sensory laboratories, and a 7,800-square-foot livestock pavilion. In addition, animal research and teaching facilities for beef, dairy, poultry, sheep, and swine are located 11 miles from campus. The Department of Animal Sciences is an integral part of the College of Agriculture, one of the world’s leading colleges of agricultural, food, life, and natural resource sciences, ranked third in the country and sixth in the world in the 2026 QS World University Rankings. Application Process All materials must be combined into one PDF and submitted on the application site at: https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor-of-Animal-Sciences/44742-en_US/ . Application materials must include: cover letter that describes the candidate’s qualifications for and interests in the position with contact information; a detailed curriculum vitae; a teaching philosophy, including examples of teaching approaches or methodologies; a mentoring philosophy, including examples of mentoring; and a list of three professional references with contact information. Screening of applicants begins November 30, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. For additional information, contact Dr. Ryan Cabot, Search Committee Chair, at rcabot@purdue.edu. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Associate-Professor-of-Management-Information-Systems/44734-en_US": {
