      "description": "Clinical Associate Professor of Management Information Systems Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44734 Job Title: Clinical Associate Professor of Management Information Systems City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Daniels School of Business (DSB) at Purdue University invites applications for the Clinical Associate Professor position beginning in Fall 2027. The primary responsibilities will be to teach at the undergraduate and graduate level.  Qualified candidates must: complete a Ph.D. in Information Systems (IS), Economics, Computer Science, or a related discipline by the starting date demonstrate teaching effectiveness through prior teaching experience, course evaluations, teaching awards, or other documented evidence of instructional effectiveness The successful candidate will teach courses in information systems and business applications of artificial intelligence (AI) at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Teaching areas may include the economics of technology, technology governance and regulations, digital transformation, the digital economy, and emerging technologies and business models. In addition to teaching, the successful candidate will be expected to contribute service to the Department, School, and University through committee work, administrative support, leadership activities, and other forms of academic and institutional engagement. Application Process Applicants should submit the following: cover letter highlighting specific strengths relative to the position and areas of opportunity identified above CV evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., course evaluations, teaching awards, etc.) statement of teaching philosophy list of recently taught courses three names for recommendation letter writers submitted here: https://apps.it.purdue.edu/KARS/Apply/nSYOWp3wQT Questions and correspondences should be addressed to Joe Mazur at mazur3@purdue.edu .  Review of applicants will begin November 30, 2026 and the position will remain open until filled. About the School The Daniels School of Business is built upon Purdue’s mission as a land-grant university to provide affordable and accessible education while combining technological excellence and business expertise. There are many opportunities to collaborate with the nation’s 4th-ranking Purdue Engineering and the top-ranking Purdue Computes disciplines. Purdue University and the Daniels School of Business are committed to free and open inquiry in all matters. Candidates are encouraged to address in their cover letter how they are prepared to contribute to a climate that values free inquiry and academic freedom. A background check will be required for employment in the position. For a complete list of benefits, please visit our website at: https://www.purdue.edu/hr/Benefits/ . Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-in-Translational-Pharmacogenomics/44536-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Translational Pharmacogenomics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Translational Pharmacogenomics Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44536 Job Title: Assistant Professor in Translational Pharmacogenomics City: Indianapolis Job Description: FLSA Status Exempt Job Summary Department of Pharmacy Practice College of Pharmacy | Purdue University Academic year appointment | Indianapolis, Indiana As part of Purdue University’s strategic investment in “One Health – Intelligent Medicines”, the Department of Pharmacy Practice in the College of Pharmacy invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant Professor level with a focus on pharmacogenomics research. Areas of Interest Areas of research interest include, but are not limited to: Clinical and translational pharmacogenomics and/or precision medicine Implementation of clinical pharmacogenomic testing and decision support in health care settings Computational genomics, multiomics, bioinformatics, artificial intelligence, and data-driven therapeutics Pharmacogenomics across diverse populations, with attention to access, validity, clinical utility, and health outcomes Genotype-guided drug development, drug response, adverse-event prevention, or individualized dosing Purdue One Health Initiative This strategic recruitment will help advance Purdue’s One Health initiative ( https://www.purdue.edu/onehealth/ ) which seeks to tackle complex challenges with real-world impact at the intersection of human, animal, and plant health.  This recruitment initiative builds on previous strategic faculty recruitment initiatives in: (1) Integrated Health; (2) AI-Driven Biomolecular Design, and (3) Advanced Chemistry. In addition, a parallel strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Healthy and Resilient Living Systems is ongoing. Through academic programs, research, facility infrastructure and industry partnerships, Purdue is making giant leaps in improving health outcomes for all living things and driving economic growth regionally and globally. This strategic faculty recruitment initiative focused on Intelligent Medicines is expected to build on prior recruitment initiatives and existing Purdue research and academic strengths, to transform research and impact human, animal and environmental health by bridging silos and fostering collaboration across disciplines. The Intelligent Medicines theme seeks to create a framework that improves human, animal, and environmental health through the integration of technology, data, and systems thinking. This faculty recruitment initiative is disease agnostic and aims to establish new capabilities in AI-enabled therapeutic development, non-animal models of disease, advanced manufacturing, intelligent health systems, digital twins, robotics, human factors, supply chain resilience, and health technology innovation. By combining strengths in device innovation, computational intelligence, manufacturing systems, and healthcare operations, Purdue intends to create a highly visible flagship that strengthens industry engagement, expands workforce development opportunities, and attracts significant external funding. Qualifications Required qualifications PhD, PharmD, MD, or equivalent doctoral degree with training and research experience in pharmacogenomics, precision or genomic medicine, or a closely related field. A record of research and productivity commensurate with rank. Demonstrated potential or record of interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship. A commitment to student teaching and mentorship. Faculty Responsibilities Establish and sustain a vigorous, nationally recognized, externally funded research program in pharmacogenomics and/or precision medicine. Contribute to the teaching and mentoring of undergraduate, graduate, and professional pharmacy students along with postdoctoral scholars and other trainees in areas aligned with the candidate's expertise and departmental needs. Contribute service to the Department, College, University, profession, and broader community. Collaborate across disciplines to translate pharmacogenomic discovery to solve complex global health challenges. Integration within the Purdue One Health Community Collectively, the strategic faculty recruitment initiatives represent a forward-thinking investment in Purdue’s research infrastructure and academic excellence. Faculty hired as part of these One Health strategic faculty recruitment initiatives will be supported as part of the overall One Health community. Together, these faculty members are expected to work across diverse disciplines, enhance Purdue’s external funding potential, and drive innovation at the intersection of health, environment, food, and economics. In addition to joining an academic unit, faculty hired under this initiative will have the opportunity to join a vibrant ecosystem of interdisciplinary centers and institutes, that span the hard tech corridor between Indianapolis and West Lafayette including: Lilly Purdue Innovation Institute Indiana University Division of Clinical Pharmacology Purdue University Institute for Cancer Research Indiana University Melvin and Bren Simon Comprehensive Cancer Center Regenstrief Institute Indiana Institute for Personalized Medicine Indiana Clinical and Translational Science Institute Purdue Institute for Healthcare Systems Innovation Purdue Institute for Physical Artificial Intelligence Indiana Biosciences Research Institute AnalytixIN The integrated, cross-disciplinary nature of One Health is essential for addressing today’s most urgent health challenges and ensuring Purdue’s continued leadership in research, education, and community impact. Application Process To apply, please submit a cover letter, CV, research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin on November 30, 2026, and continue until positions are filled. Applications should be submitted via SuccessFactors at careers.purdue.edu. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Teaching-Professor-of-Computer-Science-Indy/44410-en_US": {
      "title": "Teaching Professor of Computer Science [Indy]",
      "description": "Teaching Professor of Computer Science [Indy] Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44410 Job Title: Teaching Professor of Computer Science [Indy] City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Computer Science in the Colleges of Science and Engineering at Purdue University solicits applications for multiple teaching faculty positions for Purdue’s Indianapolis campus at the Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor level. Teaching faculty participate in departmental, college, and university-level activities and have professional development opportunities. The positions are non-tenure track faculty positions. The Department of Computer Science is part of the College of Science and the College of Engineering. Purdue is one of the nation's leading land-grant universities, with an enrollment of over 50,000 students, primarily majoring in STEM subjects, and ranks among the top 10 public universities nationally. Purdue University launched a major initiative, Purdue Computes, consisting of three dimensions (Computing, Physical Artificial Intelligence, and Semiconductors) that connect faculty and students from across the institution and enable the university to advance to the forefront with unparalleled excellence at scale. As part of this initiative, Computing is on track to add 50 new faculty positions by 2030. Purdue Computes imparts a stimulating academic environment with active research programs in most areas of computing. The Department of Computer Science offers undergraduate degree programs in Computer Science, Data Science, and Artificial Intelligence, as well as graduate MS and PhD programs. Opportunities for collaboration exist across the university: department faculty collaborate with colleagues in every college in the university. The Department of Computer Science has a robust instructional staff and IT staff support team for its growing body of teaching faculty. Our highly ranked undergraduate and graduate programs consistently attract driven and enthusiastic students. The department currently enrolls over 3500 undergraduates (increasing from last year) and over 500 graduate students. With CS students averaging scores of 33.4 and 1476 on the ACT and SAT, faculty can interact with many persistent and focused students while working in a space known for its innovative academic environment, fostering a collaborative and enriching experience for educators and students alike. The Computer Science department has computer science and artificial intelligence majors at Purdue University in Indianapolis.This new city campus extends Purdue’s mission and impact with a first-of-its-kind Hard-Tech Corridor, stretching between Indianapolis and West Lafayette. We’re building the future by linking industry to our world-class educators, researchers and students. For more information, see https://www.cs.purdue.edu . Purdue University in Indianapolis is a new, fully integrated expansion of the West Lafayette campus, extending to central Indiana the academic rigor and accessible excellence for which Purdue is known. As the state’s only public top-10 university, most-trusted university and most-innovative university, Purdue is focused and committed to strengthening its presence in Indiana’s industrial and technological center. Purdue in Indianapolis is creating an innovative, STEM-based collegiate experience by connecting future-ready Purdue students and faculty in Indianapolis to local businesses to accelerate Indiana’s STEM pipeline and tech ecosystem, fueling impact for our region and the world. Learn more about Purdue’s latest giant leap at: https://www.purdue.edu/campuses/indianapolis Education Applicants must hold a PhD in computer science or a related field by the employment start date. Experience Applicants must have a documented history of teaching and demonstrate mastery of subject matter sufficient to teach a range of courses in the Computer Science department curriculum. This includes traditional teaching instruction (lecture courses, lab courses), management of teams of teaching assistants, development of course content, participation in course and curriculum development, interaction with students and student teams, and delivery of online courses. Purdue University in Indianapolis is a new, fully integrated expansion of the West Lafayette campus, extending to central Indiana the academic rigor and accessible excellence for which Purdue is known. As the state’s only public top-10 university, most-trusted university and most-innovative university, Purdue is focused and committed to strengthening its presence in Indiana’s industrial and technological center. Purdue in Indianapolis is creating an innovative, STEM-based collegiate experience by connecting future-ready Purdue students and faculty in Indianapolis to local businesses to accelerate Indiana’s STEM pipeline and tech ecosystem, fueling impact for our region and the world. Learn more about Purdue’s latest giant leap at: https://www.purdue.edu/campuses/indianapolis Short Description Job Duties Once hired, the successful candidate will teach Computer Science Department courses, advise students, and perform service at the School, College, and University levels.  These duties include traditional teaching instruction (lecture courses, lab courses), management of teams of teaching assistants, development of course content, participation in course and curriculum development, interaction with students and student teams, and delivery of online courses if needed . To Apply Submit your application to this site and upload your application material (cover letter, CV, teaching statement, and optional research statement). The teaching statement should include previous teaching experiences and highlight undergraduate courses of interest for teaching in the CS, DS, and AI majors. Information about our courses and degree requirements are here: https://www.cs.purdue.edu/undergraduate/index.html . Application review will begin November 23, 2026, and continue until positions are filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Inquiries may be sent to mailto:tf-search@cs.purdue.edu Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/23/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
