    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-of-Computer-Science/44401-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Computer Science",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Computer Science Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44401 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Computer Science City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Computer Science in the Colleges of Science and Engineering at Purdue University invites applications for multiple Tenure-Track Faculty positions at the Assistant or Associate Professor level at our West Lafayette and Indianapolis campuses. Purdue University has launched a new major initiative, Purdue Computes, with three dimensions (Computing, Physical Artificial Intelligence, and Semiconductors) that connect faculty and students across the institution and enable the university to advance to the forefront with unparalleled excellence at scale. As part of this initiative, Computing is on track to add 50 new positions by 2030. Purdue Computes offers a stimulating academic environment with active research programs in almost all areas of computing. The Department of Computer Science offers undergraduate programs in Computer Science, Data Science, and Artificial Intelligence, in both our West Lafayette and Indianapolis campuses, as well as graduate MS and PhD programs. For more information, see https://www.cs.purdue.edu . Opportunities for collaboration exist across the university, and our faculty collaborate with every college. While we are interested in hiring in all areas of Computer Science, we are particularly focused on areas that can drive as well as benefit from the AI revolution. Domains of particular interest include Computational Biology, Bioinformatics, Computer Vision and Computer Graphics; Natural Language Processing and Large Language Models; all aspects of Quantum Computing; explainable and ethical AI; scientific machine learning; and programming languages and formal methods for AI systems. We are also interested in systems that can drive scalable infrastructure for modern machine Learning and AI, including OS, networking, mobile computing, databases, distributed systems, as well as the interplay between AI systems and security and privacy. Application Process Applications need to be submitted to this site and must include (1) a cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a statement of research, (4) a statement of teaching, and (5) names and contact information of at least three references. Please ensure that your Google Scholar profile is up to date, although this is not required. The cover letter should clearly indicate which of the above areas is the most suitable for the applicant’s consideration. The cover letter should also include the preferred campus (West Lafayette or Indianapolis). Applications will be considered beginning November 23, 2026, and will be reviewed until the positions are filled. A background check will be required for employment in this position. Inquiries may be sent to head-assistant@cs.purdue.edu. Qualifications & Job Duties Candidates must hold a Ph.D. degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related discipline by the employment start date, and demonstrate potential to build an independent research program, as well as the potential to educate and mentor students. A successful candidate will conduct original research, advise graduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses, and perform service at the School, College, and University levels. Reference Collection For submitting letters of reference, you will receive an email from system@successfactors.com titled \"Follow-up to your application.\" Please follow the instructions in the email to submit your references. Purdue's campuses are in West Lafayette and Indianapolis, Indiana, rapidly growing and welcoming communities with wide varieties of cultural activities, events, and industries. Purdue has a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/22/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Practice-of-Chemistry/44561-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice of Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice of Chemistry Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44561 Job Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice of Chemistry City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice in Chemistry The Department of Chemistry in the College of Science at Purdue University solicits applications for a Professor of Practice position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level for the Purdue University Indianapolis location, to begin in August 2027. Education Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in chemistry or a related field by the start of the appointment and should be committed to excellence in teaching.  Instructional experience with undergraduate organic chemistry or biochemistry courses is expected. The ability to teach a range of undergraduate chemistry courses is desirable. Candidates should have an interest in working with undergraduate students, in particular students with pre-medicine and health career goals. Responsibilities include assisting with the coordination and teaching of organic and biochemistry chemistry curriculum across the West Lafayette and Indianapolis locations and working directly with interdisciplinary faculty and staff who comprise the pre-medicine and heath initiative in Indianapolis.  We welcome candidates with interest in conducting chemistry research at the undergraduate level.  Professor of Practice faculty are expected to be actively involved in departmental educational activities, have professional development opportunities, and may direct, supervise, practice, and conduct research and outreach activities. The position is a non-tenure track faculty position with multi-year contracts. Salary and benefits are competitive. Purdue University Chemistry Department Information Purdue Chemistry The James Tarpo Jr. and Margaret Tarpo Department of Chemistry is internationally acclaimed for its excellence in chemical education and innovation, boasting two Nobel laureates in organic chemistry, the #1 ranked analytical chemistry program, and a highly successful drug discovery initiative.  Faculty and students benefit from state-of-the-art facilities that include the Jonathan Amy Facility for Chemical Instrumentation, NMR and X-ray Crystallography Facilities, the Research Instrumentation Center, the AI Guided Drug Discovery and Automation Center, the High Throughput Experimentation Catalysis Center, the Center for Autonomous Materials Discovery, and the High Throughput DESI Facility.  The Department is also actively involved in the Purdue Lilly 360 initiative, the largest academic-industry partnership in the US. As of Fall 2026, the Department includes 57 faculty, 70 staff members, 7 lecturers, 62 postdoctoral researchers, 437 graduate students, and 485 undergraduate majors. The Department is a key contributor to the educational mission of Purdue University. Additional information is available at https://www.chem.purdue.edu/ . Purdue University in Indianapolis Purdue University in Indianapolis is a new, fully integrated expansion of the West Lafayette campus, extending to central Indiana the academic rigor and accessible excellence for which Purdue is known. As the state’s only public top 10 university, most trusted university and most innovative university, Purdue is focused and committed to strengthening its presence in Indiana’s industrial and technological center. Purdue in Indianapolis is creating an innovative, STEM-based collegiate experience by connecting future-ready Purdue students and faculty in Indianapolis to local businesses to accelerate Indiana’s STEM pipeline and tech ecosystem, fueling impact for our region and the world. Learn more about Purdue’s latest giant leap at: https://www.purdue.edu/indianapolis/ Applicant Information Application Process To apply, internal applicants will submit an application to https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Practice-of-Chemistry/44561-en_US/?isInternalUser=true. External candidates please submit your application via this link: https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Practice-of-Chemistry/44561-en_US/ .  Along with your application, please include: (1) a cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a statement of teaching philosophy and optionally any supporting documents that show effective instruction (nor more than five pages), (4) a statement on conducting research with undergraduate students, and (5) names and contact information for at least three references.  Questions about the search can be sent to chempop-search@purdue.edu.  Review of applications will begin November 23, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/21/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Industrial-Design/44543-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Industrial Design",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Industrial Design Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44543 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Industrial Design City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Assistant Professor in Industrial Design, Tenure Track Start date: August 16, 2027 Purdue University invites applications for a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Industrial Design to join our community of practitioners, scholars, and students in the Patti and Rusty Rueff School of Design, Art, and Performance. We welcome applicants with a design practice and/or research agenda in one or more of the following areas: industrial design, interaction design, interactive prototyping, or user experience design. We seek applicants who can demonstrate their potential to develop a distinguished record of applied design production and innovation and/or original high-impact research within their area of focus. We encourage applicants who strive to integrate scholarship and applied practice. In addition to industrial design courses, the successful candidate will have opportunities to contribute to design education across the curriculum through the development and teaching of new courses in design thinking for the nationally recognized Cornerstone Integrated Liberal Arts program. The candidate may also have opportunities for teaching graduate courses in a cross-disciplinary context. Program Overview Housed within the Patti and Rusty Rueff School of Design, Art, and Performance in the College of Liberal Arts, Industrial Design is a practice-based, hands-on program with a placement rate in industry of more than 90%. At the undergraduate level, we offer a rigorous NASAD-accredited 4-year BFA professional program with approximately 140 students. We also offer a 3-year MFA with concentrations in Industrial Design and Interaction Design. As “thinkers, innovators, and makers” Purdue’s Industrial Design program constituents value direct connections with industry, entrepreneurship, and the contributions of scholarship. Responsibilities •    Teach and mentor students through 4 courses per academic year: 2 in Industrial Design, and 2 in the Cornerstone Integrated Liberal Arts program. •    Develop and maintain an active design practice and/or research program with national and international impact through juried awards, patents, conferences, peer-reviewed publications, exhibitions or other dissemination venues appropriate to area of expertise. •    Contribute to departmental, school, and college service through committee work, curriculum development, faculty meetings, recruitment efforts, and other appropriate service activities. Required Qualifications Terminal degree such as MFA, MID, MS or PhD in Industrial Design, or in a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of teaching effectiveness at the university level, or comparable instructional and mentoring experience in a professional setting. Salary and Benefits Salary commensurate with experience and qualifications. The successful candidate will be eligible for health, retirement, and life insurance benefits. Purdue University’s benefit package is summarized at: www.purdue.edu/hr/Benefits/ . Procedure Candidates should submit application materials electronically via https://careers.purdue.edu/44543 . Review of applications will begin on January 6, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. For questions about the application procedure, contact: Rachel Weaver, Assistant to the Head Rueff School of Design, Art, and Performance rrweaver@purdue.edu For questions about the position, contact: Steve Visser, Professor of Industrial Design, Search Committee Chair Department of Art and Design svisser@purdue.edu Required Application Materials 1.    Letter of Interest (cover letter): The letter should include candidate’s design and/or research focus, teaching areas, industry-related experience and perceived fit for the Industrial Design program. 2.    Current Resume or Curriculum Vitae (CV) – PDF format. 3.    Names and Contact Information for Three References – please include each reference’s name, title, email address, and phone number. 4.    Research or Design/Creative Statement – PDF format. 5.    Teaching Statement – PDF format. Please upload the following materials into the “Additional Documents” section: 6.    Portfolio of academic and or professional work with a corresponding list with titles, dates, role in collaborative projects, and other pertinent information or a link to a personal website. 7.    Portfolio of student/mentee work (if applicable) and a corresponding list with titles, courses and dates, and other pertinent information or a link to a personal teaching website. 8.    Unofficial transcript for terminal degree. Official transcript will be required, if invited for an interview. All non-English transcripts must be accompanied by an official English translation  – PDF format. Employment Requirement A background check is required for employment in this position. Equal Opportunity Statement Purdue University is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access University. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/20/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Professor-ClinicalProfessional-Assistant/44340-en_US": {
      "title": "Professor Clinical/Professional Assistant",
      "description": "Professor Clinical/Professional Assistant Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44340 Job Title: Professor Clinical/Professional Assistant City: WEST LAFAYETTE Job Description: Job Summary Clinical Assistant Professor in Audiology The Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences (SLHS) at Purdue University-West Lafayette invites applications and nominations of candidates holding an AuD, CCC-A or PhD, CCC-A for the position of Clinical Assistant Professor in Audiology. The position is a full-time, 12-month appointment with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. SLHS is a national leader in clinical education and research and offers an undergraduate degree (BS) and graduate degrees (AuD, MS-SLHS, and PhD). The Department houses highly ranked graduate programs in Audiology (AuD, 6th) and Speech-Language Pathology (MS-SLHS, 3rd) , according to U.S. News and World Report.  SLHS is a diverse and collegial department with 17 tenure-track and 14 clinical faculty members.  Our large on-campus audiology clinic serves the community with services that include: pediatric and adult diagnostic and intervention services, vestibular evaluations, a cochlear implant clinic, a central auditory processing disorder clinic, and a hearing conservation program.  SLHS enjoys excellence and distinction in all programs, supports faculty development through scholarship, and promotes engagement statewide, nationally, and internationally. The Department houses a thriving interdisciplinary community where interprofessional education/practice and research-clinical collaborations are encouraged. http://www.purdue.edu/hhs/slhs/ Clinical faculty are full members of the SLHS faculty and are expected to demonstrate excellence in the areas of clinical practice and clinical education. Primary responsibilities include providing clinical education and mentorship to students, classroom teaching, and direct clinical services to clients and their families. Opportunities exist for interprofessional education and practice, clinical research, and collaboration with academic faculty. Two years of clinical experience and ASHA CCC-A are required at the time of employment. Three years of clinical experience and clinical supervision experience are preferred. Must be eligible for Indiana Audiology licensure and Indiana early intervention certification (First Steps). To be assured full consideration, complete applications should be received by November 20, 2026. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit their curriculum vitae, a letter of interest indicating relevant experience and qualifications, and a list of the names of three references.  Materials should be submitted through this link: ( https://careers.purdue.edu/job-invite/44340/ ). Questions regarding this position may be directed to the chair of the search committee, Clinical Professor Shannon Van Hyfte, AuD CCC-A ( svanhyff@purdue.edu ). A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Professor-ClinicalProfessional-Assistant/44567-en_US": {
      "title": "Professor Clinical/Professional Assistant",
      "description": "Professor Clinical/Professional Assistant Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44567 Job Title: Professor Clinical/Professional Assistant City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Description Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice, Purdue Indianapolis, Biological Sciences The College of Science at Purdue University invites applications for a non-tenure-track Professor of Practice (PoP) in Biological Sciences at our Purdue University Indianapolis campus, beginning in Fall 2027. This appointment is available at the Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice level. Designed for educators dedicated to exceptional teaching, engagement, and student success, this position offers multi-year rolling contracts, a clear and supported promotion track, and full faculty integration. The successful candidate will focus on excellence in teaching, strategic program development, and impactful scholarship centering on pedagogical innovation, transformational learning, and community engagement. Experience Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in biology or a related field by the start of the appointment and should be committed to excellence in teaching.  We particularly encourage candidates with a demonstrated history of evidence-based teaching and innovation as well as scholarship in biology education in a higher education setting. Instructional experience with undergraduate biology-related courses is expected, as well as the ability to teach a range of courses in an undergraduate biology major curriculum. Candidates should have an interest in mentoring undergraduate students, in particular students with pre-medicine and health career goals.  Experience or interest in designing, delivering, and managing high-quality online courses for working professionals is welcomed. Responsibilities Responsibilities include coordination and teaching of introductory biology curriculum in the Indianapolis location and working directly with interdisciplinary faculty and staff who will support the pre-medicine and heath initiative in Indianapolis.  We welcome candidates with interest in conducting biology-related research at the undergraduate level. The successful candidate will also have opportunities to teach within or contribute to the development and growth of our online and residential master’s degree professional programs. Purdue University in Indianapolis is a new, fully integrated expansion of the West Lafayette campus, extending to central Indiana the academic rigor and accessible excellence for which Purdue is known. Biological Sciences at Purdue in Indianapolis is creating an innovative, STEM-based collegiate experience by connecting health-focused Purdue students and faculty in Indianapolis to local health and medical centers. Learn more about Purdue’s latest giant leap at https://www.purdue.edu/campuses/indianapolis/ . For more information about our department, see https://www.bio.purdue.edu/ Application Procedure Applications should be submitted through Click to Apply and should include: Cover letter that describes their qualifications and experience relevant to this job opportunity Curriculum vitae with detailed information on previous teaching and mentoring experience Statement of teaching and mentoring philosophy that describes previous teaching and mentoring experience, impact, and innovation Three letters of reference that speak to the candidate’s teaching qualifications to be sent to Apopfacsearchbio@purdue.edu . All applications received by November 20, 2026 will be given full consideration. Inquiries can be directed to Apopfacsearchbio@purdue.edu . A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Space-Engineering/44507-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Space Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Space Engineering Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44507 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Space Engineering City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary Purdue Engineering invites applications for multiple tenured/tenure track positions at assistant and associate ranks in Space Engineering . We seek exceptional candidates pursuing innovative research across the breadth of this interdisciplinary area supporting sustained, resilient, and scalable operations and habitation in orbital, cislunar, and extraterrestrial environments. Research in sub-areas may include, but are not limited to, the following: Space Systems, Astrodynamics and Operations : Astrodynamics & space mission design; innovative spacecraft and space mission architecture; spacecraft guidance, navigation, control & autonomy; space situational awareness & space domain awareness; space sensing & communications; advanced materials & structures for space environment; and planetary entry, descent & landing. Propulsion and Power : Leveraging world-class experimental infrastructure of Zucrow Labs , in-space and launch propulsion; and space power & energy systems. Microgravity Engineering and In-Space Manufacturing : Exploiting microgravity and space environments to advance physical, chemical, biological, & pharmaceutical manufacturing processes for in-space, orbital, extraterrestrial, and terrestrial applications. In-Space Logistics and Supply Chain : Addressing the design, optimization, and resilience of Earth-to-space and in-space logistics networks; transportation; resource utilization and distribution; and point-of-need production and sustainment. Successful candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Materials Engineering, Civil Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, or a closely related discipline by the employment start date. Early-career applicants should show evidence of initiating independent research, while mid-career applicants should demonstrate a sustained record of independent research within academic or industrial organizations, and contributions to education and/or mentoring. The successful candidate will conduct original research, advise graduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, and contribute service at the School, College, and University levels. Applicants interested in a position in any of Purdue’s engineering schools are welcome to apply. College of Engineering Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand and have 8 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering is a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit the following materials through this site: (1) a cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vita, (3) a statement of research plans (no more than two pages), (4) a statement of teaching interests and plan (no more than two pages), and (5) names and contact information for at least five references. The search committee may contact references to request letters of recommendation. Questions regarding the application process may be directed to Engineering Academic Affairs, Purdue Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on November 20, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering offer a Concierge Program that provides dual-career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-of-Engineering-Practice-in-Computer-Engineering-%28Indianapolis%29/44508-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Engineering Practice in Computer Engineering (Indianapolis)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Engineering Practice in Computer Engineering (Indianapolis) Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44508 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Engineering Practice in Computer Engineering (Indianapolis) City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The Elmore Family School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) at Purdue University invites applications for a non-tenure track Faculty of Engineering Practice position based in Indianapolis at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. Purdue University seeks to attract exceptional candidates with interests and expertise in Computer Engineering areas related to embedded software systems, high-performance systems or computer graphics, particularly in the context of gaming and interactive systems. The position includes opportunities to build and lead Purdue ECE’s initiatives in gaming and interactive systems. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. or M.S. degree in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a related discipline by the employment start date, combined with at least 5 years of industry experience. The successful candidate will be teaching and actively involved in the undergraduate curriculum, including traditional instruction (lecture courses, lab courses), management of large teams of teaching assistants, development of course contents, participation in the course and curriculum development, interaction with students and student teams, delivery of online courses, and working with gaming industry partners. Candidates should also integrate their professional practice with the Elmore Family School of Electrical and Computer Engineering’s research, education, and/or engagement/outreach programs. The successful candidate will also perform service at the School, College, and University levels. School and College The Elmore Family School of Electrical and Computer Engineering is the largest academic unit at Purdue University and one of the largest in the nation with more than 130 faculty members (7 NAE members, more than 40 Fellows in multiple societies,) 2,500 undergraduate students (sophomores-seniors) and 1,700 graduate students. In Indianapolis, ECE is home to the Transportation and Autonomous Systems Institute (TASI) which collaborates closely with industry partners in developing and testing cutting-edge vehicle autonomy systems, as well as the newly launched Intelligent Software & Systems Center, which is re-envisioning the software lifecycle in the age of agentic AI and the impact on AI-native systems. These institutions will provide a strong foundation to new faculty joining in Indianapolis. ECE’s curriculum provides broad-based programs in electrical and computer engineering, including a concentration in software engineering. ECE’s undergraduate programs in Electrical Engineering and Computer Engineering are ranked 10th and 9th, respectively. Its graduate programs are ranked 8th and 9th, respectively. And its online MS in ECE is ranked 1st in the nation. The School is an integral part of Purdue’s College of Engineering. Purdue Engineering is renowned for top-notch faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand and have 8 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering is a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . Application Process To apply, please submit application to this site including (1) cover letter (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) 2-page teaching plan, (4) 2-page research/engagement/outreach plan, and (5) names and contact information for at least 3 references, and, if applicable (6) verifiable teaching evaluations from prior teaching experiences. The search committee may contact references to request letters. For information/questions regarding applications contact the Office of Academic Affairs, College of Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on November 20, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-of-Engineering-Practice-in-Aeronautics-and-Astronautics/44538-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Engineering Practice in Aeronautics and Astronautics",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Engineering Practice in Aeronautics and Astronautics Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44538 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor of Engineering Practice in Aeronautics and Astronautics City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The School of Aeronautics and Astronautics (AAE) at Purdue University invites applications for a non-tenure-track Professor of Engineering Practice position at the Assistant or Associate rank. These positions connect aerospace practice with aerospace education, preparing the next generation of engineers for the realities of engineering careers. Expertise in any area of aeronautics and astronautics will be considered. Positions are full-time, three-year, renewable appointments with an anticipated start date of August 2027. The position requires full-time presence on the West Lafayette campus. Professors of Engineering Practice bring their experience into the classroom. They teach undergraduate and graduate AAE courses, which may include hybrid and fully online instruction. Each professor also develops an area of excellence: a sustained body of work beyond classroom teaching that grows out of their professional background and advances AAE’s mission. Current AAE Professors of Engineering Practice lead work in integrating digital engineering into the undergraduate curriculum, program assessment and accreditation, industry engagement, the scholarship of teaching and learning, and developing new undergraduate and graduate programs and certificates. Candidates must hold a mster's degree (MS or MSE) in aerospace engineering or a closely related discipline by the start date, with a doctoral degree (PhD or DEng) preferred. Candidates must also have at least five years of relevant post-baccalaureate professional experience, which may include any combination of engineering practice in industry, government or national laboratories, federally funded research and development centers, military service, or academic appointments. Time spent as a student, including co-ops, internships, and graduate research or teaching assistantships, does not count toward this requirement. About AAE and Purdue Engineering AAE is consistently recognized as an international leader for the quality of its educational programs, the innovation and depth of its research, and its impact on aerospace technology and workforce. It is one of the largest aerospace engineering programs in the US by degrees granted, with more than 1,300 undergraduate and 650 graduate students, and is ranked 3rd (undergraduate) and 5th (graduate) nationally. Additional information about AAE is available at https://engineering.purdue.edu/AAE . Purdue Engineering is renowned for excellent faculty and students, unique research facilities and innovations, and a culture of collegiality and persistent pursuit of preeminence. As one of the top ranked and largest engineering colleges in the nation, we are the first among U.S. engineering colleges in annual graduates and market demand, and have 8 degree programs ranked in the top 10 nationally. Purdue Engineering is a top-ranked college for patents and translation of our research activities to practice in the state, nation, and world.  More than 70 Purdue Engineering faculty and alumni are National Academy of Engineering members, and we look to continue bringing outstanding faculty to campus, remaining the leader in affordable excellence at scale by guiding strategic growth through investment in people, exciting initiatives , and facilities . How to Apply Submit an application at this site that includes: (1) A cover letter, (2) a complete CV or resume. (3) A teaching statement (two pages maximum) describing your teaching interests and approach. Candidates without formal teaching experience may draw on experience mentoring, training, or leading engineers. (4) An area of excellence statement (two pages maximum) describing where your professional background positions you to make a sustained contribution to AAE’s mission, and what you would aim to accomplish in your first three to five years. (5) Names and contact information for at least three references. The search committee may contact references to request letters. Review of applications will begin on November 20, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required for employment. For questions, contact Academic Affairs, College of Engineering, at coeacademicaffairs@purdue.edu . Purdue and the College of Engineering have a Concierge Program that provides dual career assistance and relocation services. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Health-Sciences/44588-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Health Sciences Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44588 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Health Sciences City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The School of Health Sciences in the College of Health and Human Sciences at Purdue University invites applications for two anticipated full-time, academic-year, tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Health Sciences, based at Purdue’s Indianapolis campus. The successful candidates will lead an independent research program with preference in the following areas: Toxicology focusing on mechanistic discoveries that can be leveraged to improve health and treat disease; Occupational and Environmental Health Sciences focusing on molecular epidemiology to identify modifiable protective and risk factors of human disease; Medical Physics focusing on cancer diagnosis, treatment, or prognosis biomarker discovery; Health Physics focusing on radiopharmaceutical or biomedical research. In all cases, Purdue University seeks to attract candidates with expertise and interest in the integration of AI/machine learning with their research. These positions are part of an initiative to expand programs to the Indianapolis campus, including the recruitment of additional faculty to support and advance the School’s teaching and research missions. As such candidates will be expected to seek out opportunities with partners in Indianapolis. Responsiblities Successful candidates will be expected to develop research programs in their fields of expertise, develop an external funding portfolio, build connections with their profession, and contribute to the education and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students. Successful candidates will teach courses in the Biomedical Health Sciences Pre-professional program. Course modality is generally in person. The potential may exist for teaching online/distance courses during the academic year. Moreover, successful candidates perform service at the School, College, and University levels. The position is competitive with regard to salary, start-up funds, and laboratory space. Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in biology, biomedical science, bioengineering, occupational or environmental health sciences, physics, toxicology, radiological health, or a closely related field by the start of employment, demonstrate potential to build an independent research program, exhibit potential to educate and mentor students, and possess a strong commitment to teaching. Outstanding applicants in all areas of health sciences will be considered, including, but not limited to, biomedical engineering, health physics, imaging sciences, industrial hygiene, medical physics, public health, radiochemistry, toxicology, and the broader biomedical health sciences. Application Process Applications must include (1) cover letter, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) description of current and future research (3 page maximum), (4) teaching statement (2 page maximum), (5) names and contact information for at least three references. Inquiries and materials will be treated confidentially. Any interested candidate should apply here (internal candidate) or here (external candidate).  References will only be contacted at the final stage when campus visits occur. About the School The School of Health Sciences at Purdue University is home to over 20 core faculty members, approximately 50 graduate students and over 1000 undergraduate students, and has internationally recognized research and educational programs in Biomedical Health Sciences, Medical Physics, Health Physics, Imaging Sciences, Occupational and Environmental Health Sciences, Toxicology, and Medical Laboratory Sciences. Faculty lead active research programs in these areas, with substantial funding from NIH and other agencies. The School is an integral part of the College of Health and Human Sciences, which aims to bring together scholars in the health sciences and human sciences to strategically address issues vital to enhancing quality of life. The College is pursuing significant new initiatives that align with campus-wide plans, with data science and One Health among its strategic priorities. Opportunities for collaboration span the physical and life sciences, mathematics, engineering, as well as the newly reimagined School of Business. For more information about Purdue’s School of Health Sciences, see https://hhs.purdue.edu/hsci/ . About the University Purdue University is one of the nation’s leading land grant universities with a full range of academic majors, over 50,000 students, more than 10,000 employees, and ranked among the leading research institutions in the country. Purdue is located in West Lafayette, Indiana within easy driving distance of both Indianapolis and Chicago. The diverse greater Lafayette/West Lafayette community ( http://www.homeofpurdue.com ) has a population of approximately 200,000, and a low cost of living. Purdue University in Indianapolis is a new, fully integrated expansion of the West Lafayette campus, extending to central Indiana the academic rigor and accessible excellence for which Purdue is known. As the state’s only public top 10 university, most trusted university, and most innovative university, Purdue is focused on strengthening its presence in Indiana’s industrial and technological center. Purdue in Indianapolis is creating an innovative, STEM-based collegiate experience by connecting future-ready students and faculty with local businesses to accelerate Indiana’s STEM pipeline and technology ecosystem, fueling impact for our region and the world. Learn more about Purdue’s latest giant leap at: https://www.purdue.edu/campuses/indianapolis/ . Review Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The appointment is set to begin August 2027. A background check is required for employment in this position. Questions regarding these positions may be directed to Dr. Jason Harris, Chair of the Search Committee jtharris@purdue.edu . Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor/44003-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44003 Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor City: West Lafayette Job Description: Job Summary The School of Nursing at Purdue University West Lafayette Campus is seeking to fill an Assistant Clinical Professor position. The position is a full-time academic year position with a desired start date of August 23, 2027. Individuals in this role will contribute to the clinical teaching, engagement and service missions of the University, College of Health and Human Sciences, and School of Nursing. Depending on departmental needs, this posting may be used to fill multiple positions. Individuals in this role will contribute to the clinical teaching, engagement and service missions of the University, College of Health and Human Sciences, and School of Nursing. Purdue School of Nursing graduates impact health and influence health care delivery around the world. The School of Nursing (SON) is a leader in clinical education, with undergraduate (BS) and graduate degree (MS, DNP, PhD, Post-Master’s Certification) programs. The School’s undergraduate program is ranked in the top 4% of programs nationally, with the MS program in the top 15% and the DNP in the top 25% according to the U.S. News and World Report. The SON has a diverse faculty which includes 40 clinical and 14 research/tenure-track faculty members, who are leaders in the use of innovative educational approaches including high-fidelity and virtual reality simulation and active learning strategies. Our faculty leads research dedicated to advancing evidence-based care and providing transformative learning opportunities for students. By working alongside experts from multiple disciplines within the College of Health and Human Sciences and across Purdue, students and faculty benefit from a collaborative environment that further distinguishes Purdue’s School of Nursing. The SON nursing clinics, which include one campus based and four community-based locations, provide affordable primary healthcare and support education of future healthcare professionals.  In 2027, the SON will move into a new state of the art building which will enable Purdue to offer the next generation of healthcare providers access to a robust collection of spaces that facilitate success in learning, discovery and engagement. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in nursing At least 4 years clinical experience National certification in area of expertise within one year of start date RN licensure in the US; Indiana RN licensure by start of appointment Application Procedure: Any interested candidate should apply here: https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor/44003-en_US/ Applicants must submit: A letter expressing your interest in a Clinical Assistant Professor position and describing relevant experience and qualifications Teaching statement Curriculum Vitae or Resume Names and contact information for three potential references In the cover letter, candidates should describe how they are prepared to contribute to a climate that values free inquiry and academic freedom. A background check is for employment in the position. Application review will begin November 20 , 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position may be sent to M. Erin Hoying, Chair of the Search Committee (mhoying@purdue.edu). This job posting represents three (3) vacancies. Job Duties: The successful candidate will help contribute to the development of clinical nurse leaders who can transform healthcare.  Responsibilities may include: Delivering lectures and facilitating learning in undergraduate and/or graduate nursing courses, ensuring students meet learning objectives. Overseeing students during clinical rotations, ensuring they apply theoretical knowledge in real-world healthcare settings. Teaching hands-on nursing skills in simulation labs, focusing on patient care, procedures, and clinical decision-making. Evaluating student performance through exams, assignments, clinical assessments, and practical evaluations. Fostering interprofessional education opportunities to promote teamwork and collaboration with other disciplines. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Biological-Sciences/44498-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Biological Sciences Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44498 Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Biological Sciences City: WEST LAFAYETTE Job Description: Position Description Intelligent Medicines – Structural Biology, Department of Biological Sciences, Purdue University Position Description As part of a transformative, university-wide initiative in One Health- Intelligent Medicines , the Purdue University Department of Biological Sciences invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level with a focus on Structural Biology for the development of next generation therapeutics. This position builds on the world-renowned legacy of innovation in structural and computational biology and biophysics at Purdue aiming to bridge next-generation structure determination with advanced computational workflows to accelerate molecular insights and therapeutic discovery. We seek a forward-thinking, experimental researcher who integrates advanced physical and biophysical techniques with modern computational tools (including artificial intelligence and machine learning) to resolve impactful biological functions of complex macromolecular structures, dynamic assemblies, and cellular machinery. Areas of Research Interest We welcome candidates specializing in any of the following or related areas: Biomolecular Design & Therapeutics: Leveraging structure determination (e.g. via X-ray crystallography) and computational/AI workflows to design novel biologics, study drug-target interactions, or pioneer therapeutic innovations. Computational & Predictive Biochemistry: Developing or leveraging advanced tools for macromolecular modeling, biological image analysis , or AI-driven functional genomics . Next-Generation Structural Approaches: Pushing the boundaries of cryo-electron microscopy/tomography (cryo-EM/ET), in situ structural biology, or multi-modal scaling. The Department of Biological Sciences is the largest department in the Life Sciences at Purdue, with a longstanding legacy of excellence and international leadership in structural and computational biology and biophysics and research spanning biological scales f rom molecules to ecosystems . The successful candidate will join a vibrant, highly collaborative community of researchers with access to state-of-the-art cryo-EM and X-ray crystallography facilities and extensive high-performance computing resources via Purdue Computes and the Purdue Institute for Physical AI . Purdue's One Health Initiative This strategic recruitment will help advance Purdue’s One Health initiative ( https://www.purdue.edu/onehealth/ ) which seeks to tackle complex challenges with real-world impact at the intersection of human, animal, and plant health. This recruitment initiative builds on previous strategic faculty recruitment initiatives in: (1) Integrated Health; (2) AI-Driven Biomolecular Design, and (3) Advanced Chemistry. In addition, a parallel strategic faculty recruitment initiative in Healthy and Resilient Living Systems is ongoing. Through academic programs, research, facility infrastructure and industry partnerships, Purdue is making giant leaps in improving health outcomes for all living things and driving economic growth regionally and globally. This strategic faculty recruitment initiative focused on Intelligent Medicine s is expected to build on prior recruitment initiatives and existing Purdue research and academic strengths, to transform research and impact human, animal and environmental health by bridging silos and fostering collaboration across disciplines. The Intelligent Medicines theme seeks to create a framework that improves human, animal, and environmental health through the integration of technology, data, and systems thinking. This faculty recruitment initiative is disease agnostic and aims to establish new capabilities in AI-enabled therapeutic development, non-animal models of disease, advanced manufacturing, intelligent health systems, digital twins, robotics, human factors, supply chain resilience, and health technology innovation. By combining strengths in device innovation, computational intelligence, manufacturing systems, and healthcare operations, Purdue intends to create a highly visible flagship that strengthens industry engagement, expands workforce development opportunities, and attracts significant external funding. Qualifications A PhD degree in a field related to the research scope described above by the employment start date A record of research excellence and productivity commensurate with rank Demonstrated potential or record of interdisciplinary collaboration and impactful scholarship Commitment to teaching and student mentorship Faculty Responsibilities Establish a vigorous, externally funded research program Contribute to the education and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students Collaborate across disciplines to solve complex global one health challenges Integration within the Purdue One Health Community Collectively, the strategic faculty recruitment initiatives represent a forward-thinking investment in Purdue’s research infrastructure and academic excellence. Faculty hired as part of these One Health strategic faculty recruitment initiatives will be supported as part of the overall One Health community. Together, these faculty members are expected to work across diverse disciplines, enhance Purdue’s external funding potential, and drive innovation at the intersection of health, environment, food, and economics. In addition to joining an academic unit, faculty hired under this initiative will have the opportunity to join a vibrant ecosystem of interdisciplinary centers and institutes, including the Purdue Institute for Cancer Research and the Purdue Institute for Drug Discovery. Furthermore, with Purdue's expanding presence in Indianapolis, including Purdue University in Indianapolis and the surrounding hard tech corridor, faculty will have additional opportunities for collaboration with clinical, industry, and translational partners. Application Process To apply, please submit a cover letter, CV, research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for at least three references. Review of applications will begin by November 16, 2026 and continue until positions are filled. Applications should be submitted at: Click to apply . A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-Biomedical-Health-Sciences/44505-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor in  Biomedical Health Sciences",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor in  Biomedical Health Sciences Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44505 Job Title: Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor in  Biomedical Health Sciences City: Indianapolis Job Description: Job Summary The School of Health Sciences in the College of Health and Human Sciences at Purdue University – Indianapolis Campus invites applications for two 9-month, academic-year, non-tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Clinical Assistant or Associate professor commensurate with qualifications noted below. These positions primarily support teaching in the Biomedical Health Sciences (BMHS) program. The successful candidate will teach BMHS classes, contribute to the launch and growth of the new BMHS program at Purdue-Indy, and advance excellence in undergraduate education. Responsibilities Successful candidates will develop and teach undergraduate courses within the BMHS program, including courses such as introduction to health sciences professionals, medical terminology, immunology, healthcare leadership, applied anatomy, applied physiology, and occupational and environmental health (planned courses). They will also have the opportunity to develop courses aligned with their field of expertise, including disciplines such as microbiology and hematology. Faculty are expected to teach 6-8 classes per year, with courseload considered in the context of total effort. The BMHS program serves students preparing for medical, physician assistant, and other health professional pathways. Clinical faculty hold long-term renewable appointments and are expected to demonstrate excellence in teaching through innovative, evidence-based pedagogy, thoughtful curriculum development, and effective student education and mentoring on their path to promotion. They will contribute to the scholarship of teaching and learning within their disciplines and participate in School and College service, including faculty committees. Purdue University provides extensive opportunities and resources to support faculty development in both teaching and scholarly activities. Qualifications Applicants must hold a minimum of a Master’s degree in biomedical health sciences or a closely related field (e.g. medical laboratory science, physiology, neuroscience, occupational and environmental health) by the time of appointment. A doctoral degree is preferred. Prior teaching experience, familiarity with human health and medicine, and demonstrated excellence in teaching and student mentoring are highly desirable. Successful candidates must possess strong organizational, communication, and leadership skills and a commitment to student success and professional preparation. Candidates at the clinical associate professor level are expected to have >5 years of teaching experience in academia and a strong record of contributions to the scholarship of teaching, as evidenced by publications, book authorship, and other scholarly activities. Application Details Applications must include (1) cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) a teaching philosophy describing courses of interest to teach (listed in the Responsibilities section) and courses which will be developed, and (4) contact information for three references. Any interested candidate should apply here (internal candidates) or here (external candidates). About the Department These positions are part of a cluster hire expanding the School of Health Sciences programs from the West Lafayette campus to the Indianapolis campus. Founded in 1979, the School offers academic programs in BMHS, Medical Laboratory Sciences, Medical Physics, Health Physics, Toxicology, and Occupational and Environmental Health Sciences. BMHS is the largest program in the School. Review The positions will remain open until filled. Application review will begin on December 1, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027. A background check is required for employment in this position. Questions regarding these positions may be directed to Dr. Linda Nie, Chair of the Search Committee ( hnie@purdue.edu ). Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Clinical-Assistant-Professor/44525-en_US": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44525 Job Title: Clinical Assistant Professor City: West Lafayette Job Description: Position Summary The School of Health Sciences in the College of Health and Human Sciences at Purdue University – West Lafayette location invites applications for one 9-month, academic-year, non-tenure-track clinical assistant professor position. This position primarily supports teaching in our Biomedical Health Sciences (BMHS) and Medical Laboratory Sciences (MLS) programs. The successful candidate will teach BMHS and MLS classes, support continued program growth, and advance excellence in undergraduate education. Responsibilities The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses within the BMHS and MLS programs, including courses in the field of health sciences such as healthcare leadership, applied anatomy, applied physiology, and occupational and environmental health, consistent with their areas of expertise and the needs of the programs. They will also have the opportunity to develop new courses relevant to these programs. Clinical faculty are expected to teach 8 classes per year with potential administrative course releases. The BMHS and MLS programs serve students preparing for medical school, physician assistant programs, medical laboratory programs, and other health professional pathways.  Clinical faculty hold long-term renewable appointments and are expected to demonstrate excellence in teaching through innovative, evidence-based pedagogy, thoughtful curriculum development, and effective student education and mentoring on their path to promotion. They will contribute to the scholarship of teaching and learning within their disciplines and participate in School and College service, including faculty committees. Purdue University provides extensive opportunities and resources to support faculty development in both teaching and scholarly activities. Qualifications Applicants must hold a minimum of a Master’s degree in biomedical health sciences, medical laboratory sciences, public health, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. A doctoral degree is preferred. Prior teaching experience, familiarity with human health and medicine, and demonstrated excellence in teaching and student mentoring are highly desirable. Successful candidates must possess strong organizational, communication, and leadership skills and a commitment to student success and professional preparation. Application Details Applications must include (1) cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) a teaching philosophy describing courses of interest to teach and develop, and (4) contact information for three references. Any interested candidate should apply here (internal candidates) or here (external candidates). About the Department Founded in 1979, the School of Health Sciences offers academic programs in Biomedical Health Sciences, Medical Laboratory Sciences, Medical Physics, Health Physics, Toxicology, and Occupational and Environmental Health Sciences (OEHS). BMHS is the largest program in the School. About Purdue Purdue University is one of the nation’s leading land grant universities with a full range of academic majors, over 50,000 students, more than 10,000 employees, and ranked among the leading research institutions in the country. Purdue is located in West Lafayette, Indiana within easy driving distance of both Indianapolis and Chicago. The diverse greater Lafayette/West Lafayette community (http://www.homeofpurdue.com) has a population of approximately 200,000, and a low cost of living. Review The position will remain open until filled. Application review will begin on December 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027. A background check is required for employment in this position. Questions regarding the position may be directed to Dr. Linda Nie, Chair of the Search Committee ( hnie@purdue.edu ). Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/job/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Practice-in-Mathematics/44326-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice in Mathematics",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice in Mathematics Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Search Jobs Home Working at Purdue How to Apply Life in Lafayette-West Lafayette Life in Indianapolis Explore Careers Athletics, Recreation & Wellness Business and Finance Business Development/Sales Child Care Communication/Marketing/Public Relations Custodial and Skilled Trades Dining & Culinary Engineering Environment and Sustainability Executive Extension Facilities Management and Physical Plant Farming, Fishing and Forestry Grounds and Landscape Services Health and Medical Services Human Resources and Legal Information Technology Lecturer Library Office Administration Planning, Design, and Construction Postdoctoral Researcher Project Management Public Safety, Security and Emergency Services Research and Laboratory Secretarial/Clerical Student Affairs, Student Services, & Res Life Veterinary Medicine Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44326 Job Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice in Mathematics City: INDIANAPOLIS Job Description: Job Summary Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice in Mathematics The Department of Mathematics in the College of Science at Purdue University invites applications for multiple appointments as Professor of Practice in Mathematics at Purdue University Indianapolis to begin in August 2027.  These appointments will be at the level of Assistant or Associate Professor of Practice. Purdue University in Indianapolis is a new, fully integrated expansion of the West Lafayette campus, extending to central Indiana the academic rigor and accessible excellence for which Purdue is known. As the state’s only public top 10 university, most trusted university and most innovative university, Purdue is focused and committed to strengthening its presence in Indiana’s industrial and technological center. Purdue in Indianapolis is creating an innovative, STEM-based collegiate experience by connecting future-ready Purdue students and faculty in Indianapolis to local businesses to accelerate Indiana’s STEM pipeline and tech ecosystem, fueling impact for our region and the world. Learn more about Purdue’s latest giant leap at https://www.purdue.edu/campuses/indianapolis/ . For more information about our department, see https://www.math.purdue.edu/ . These positions are non-tenure track faculty positions with multi-year contracts, a promotion track, and a focus on undergraduate teaching and course administration.  Duties will typically consist of teaching 5-6 courses in Indianapolis each academic year, including large-lecture courses, course coordination, and/or other related scholarly and administrative activities. Successful applicants will have a documented record of effective teaching, the ability to teach a range of courses in the undergraduate curriculum, a commitment to teaching, mentoring, and interacting with undergraduate students, and a willingness to observe classes and provide teaching guidance to new instructors. Candidates should specifically note in their application any experience they have had with teaching large-lecture Calculus classes, teaching upper-division undergraduate courses, coordinating learning management or online homework systems, and any other unique teaching qualifications (such as experience with innovative instructional methods). Candidates must have a PhD (or its equivalent) in mathematics or a closely related field by the start of the appointment. Teaching experience after obtaining a PhD will be viewed favorably. Professors of Practice faculty will be involved in departmental activities and have professional development opportunities.  Salary and benefits are competitive. Application Process Applications should be submitted online through www.mathjobs.org and should include (1) the AMS cover sheet for academic employment, (2) a cover letter, (3) a curriculum vitae, (4) a teaching statement, and (5) at least three letters of recommendation focused on the candidate’s teaching qualifications. In addition, for purposes of equity, to be considered for the position, applicants will also need to create a profile including voluntary demographic data at SuccessFactors . Reference letter writers should be asked to submit their letters online through www.mathjobs.org. Direct all inquiries to mathexec@purdue.edu . Review of applications will begin on 1 November 2026 and continue until the positions are filled. A background check is required for employment in this position. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access university. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/5/26 Search Jobs Careers Home View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © Copyright 2024, Purdue University - An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    }
  },
